window.OPS = {"trooper":{"meta":{"word":"TROOPER","accent":"#d7dde6","body":"armor","budget":350,"btn":"⚔ EMPIRE","dur":"8 weeks","hrs":"60–120 hrs","parts":"Full armour","budgetRange":"€150–350+","lead":"One build, two troopers: Clone or Stormtrooper. The biggest armour build in the series — a full white shell head to toe.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"Print ONE forearm first as a test. If it fits and you can finish it, you can do the whole suit.","intro":"OPERATION TROOPER","introSub":"ARMOURY · BUILD MANUAL · FILE TK-421","footer":"OPERATION TROOPER · BUILD MANUAL · ONE BUILD, TWO TROOPERS · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"trooper_public.pdf","weekPdf":"trooper_byweek.pdf","quote":"These aren't the droids you're looking for."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The signature piece. Clone = curved T-visor; Stormtrooper = the classic angular dome. Print, seam-fill, sand, prime, gloss white.","tip":"Print the helmet first — it's the showpiece and your skills test.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Bells","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Two curved shoulder plates that strap over the arms.","tip":"Mirror one STL for the pair.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest + Back Plate","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":12,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The front chest and back plates — the core of the armour. Big prints; split for small printers.","tip":"The chest is the most-seen plate — take your time finishing it.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Ab / Kidney Plate","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The stomach and lower-back plates that link chest to belt.","tip":"Strap so it flexes when you sit.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Boxes","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":4,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The belt with side ammo boxes. Mounts on a real webbing belt.","tip":"Print the boxes, mount on a sports belt.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Codpiece + Thighs","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Front codpiece plate and the two thigh guards.","tip":"Elastic straps keep the thighs from sliding.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"No Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Troopers don't wear a cape. Skip this zone.","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the 501st Legion standards — they set the bar for both Stormtroopers (Imperial) and Clone Troopers (Republic).","tip":"The 501st has approved standards (CRLs) for both your trooper types.","files":[{"name":"501st Legion CRL","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin + Knee Plates","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Shin guards and knee diamonds for both legs.","tip":"Knees take knocks — finish them tough.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Plain white boots under the leg armour.","tip":"White trainers work to start.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Forearms + Biceps + Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":6,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Forearm plates AND upper-arm (bicep) plates for both arms — four pieces total — plus black (Clone) or white (Stormtrooper) gloves.","tip":"Test-print ONE forearm first as your fit test, then mirror the biceps for the pair.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blaster","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":30,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Troopers carry a blaster, not a saber. Clone = DC-15; Stormtrooper = E-11.","tip":"Print or buy a toy blaster; paint it.","files":[{"name":"E-11 blaster STL — search Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=e-11+blaster"}]},"blackundersuit":{"name":"Black Undersuit","type":"BASE · 13","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"A full black body glove worn under every plate — black for both Clone and Stormtrooper. Covers the neck, joints and all skin gaps so no skin shows through the white shell.","tip":"Get a snug black athletic base layer or zentai-style suit; it's the foundation the whole 'head to toe white shell' sits on.","files":[]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 8–7","task":"Plan + order filament & supplies"},{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Print + finish the helmet"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Print the torso (chest, back, ab)"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Arms, legs, belt + straps"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Weather, dress rehearsal, game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>This is the <span class='accent'>biggest build in the series</span> — a full-body white shell.</p><p>~3–5 kg of filament, dozens of plates, weeks of sanding and painting. Very doable, but it's a marathon. Print ONE forearm first as your test.</p><p>Before you spend a cent or a gram, know what you are signing up for. That is not a reason to skip it — it is a reason to plan it.</p><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Pieces</span><span class=\"col-val\">20+ separate armor parts (helmet, chest, back, ab, kidney, shoulder bells, biceps, forearms, hands, thighs, shins) plus a bodysuit</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Finishing</span><span class=\"col-val\">Every piece needs sanding, priming and painting</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Cost</span><span class=\"col-val\">Roughly €150–400 all-in, depending on free vs paid files and blaster props</span></div></div><p>Build a trooper if you have a reliable printer, time across several months, and you have finished at least one smaller armor piece before — the Anakin pauldron is a perfect warm-up. If this is your very first print ever, do a helmet or a single shoulder first, not the whole suit.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Clone or Stormtrooper?","body":"<p class='lead'>Same method, two troopers.</p><ul><li><b>Clone</b> — curved T-visor helmet, can be coloured by legion.</li><li><b>Stormtrooper</b> — the classic angular white armour.</li></ul><p>Pick before you print; the helmet differs most.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Quick Start</div><p>First trooper? Build a <strong>Stormtrooper</strong>. It is pure white — no unit markings to mask and paint — so it is a little less finishing work than a clone. Add coloured markings later and you basically have a clone.</p></div><h3>Quick Start</h3><p>Pick one before you start — it changes the colours, a few plate shapes, and the bodysuit underneath. First trooper? Build a Stormtrooper: it is pure white, no unit markings to mask and paint, so a little less finishing work. Later, add coloured unit markings, swap the helmet top to a fin, and tweak a couple of plates — and you've got a Clone Trooper from the same suit.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Fun Fact</div>Stormtroopers are the bad guys and Clones fight for the Republic, but BOTH are welcomed by the 501st Legion — the costuming club for Imperial and trooper armor. Jedi go in the Rebel Legion; troopers go in the 501st.</div>"},{"num":"03","title":"Anatomy of a Trooper","body":"<p class=\"lead\">A trooper is a lot of separate plates strapped over a bodysuit. Here is the full parts map so nothing surprises you.</p><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Head</span><span class=\"col-val\">Helmet (dome + face + back), visor</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Torso</span><span class=\"col-val\">Chest, back, ab and kidney plates</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Shoulders</span><span class=\"col-val\">Two shoulder bells</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Arms</span><span class=\"col-val\">Two biceps, two forearms, two hand guards</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Waist</span><span class=\"col-val\">Belt + drop boxes (the little buttoned boxes)</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Legs</span><span class=\"col-val\">Two thighs, two shins</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Under</span><span class=\"col-val\">Bodysuit, gloves, boots</span></div></div><h3>Print in Batches</h3><p>You do not print this all at once. Work zone by zone: helmet, then torso, then arms, then legs. Each finished zone feels like a win and keeps the project from feeling endless.</p><h3>How It All Holds On</h3><ul><li>Chest + back joined at the shoulders with elastic straps, so they hang like a sandwich.</li><li>Ab + kidney joined the same way around the waist.</li><li>Shoulder bells, biceps and forearms held with elastic loops around the arm.</li><li>Thighs and shins with elastic or velcro around the leg.</li><li>Everything sits over the bodysuit — that hides gaps and stops plastic rubbing your skin.</li></ul><p>Loose armor that flaps around ruins the look (and the photos).</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"Procurement Roster","body":"<p class=\"lead\">Three ways to gear up: (A) buy a finished armor kit, (B) 3D-print the armor yourself, (C) mix — print the hard stuff, buy the bodysuit and boots. Paste Chinese into Taobao or use English on AliExpress / eBay.</p><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Full armor kit</span><span class=\"col-val\">白兵 cosplay 全套 — or search \"stormtrooper armor kit\" on AliExpress / eBay</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Pre-made helmet</span><span class=\"col-val\">白兵 头盔 ABS — or \"stormtrooper helmet ABS\" on AliExpress</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Black bodysuit</span><span class=\"col-val\">连体紧身衣 黑色 — the under-layer base</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">White gloves</span><span class=\"col-val\">白色 手套</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Tall white boots</span><span class=\"col-val\">白色 高筒靴 — or paint black boots</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Filament</span><span class=\"col-val\">白色 PLA 耗材 — white PLA for the print path</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Blaster prop</span><span class=\"col-val\">E-11 (storm) / DC-15 (clone)</span></div></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Print vs Buy</div>A bought ABS armor kit is faster and already smooth, but costs more and may not fit a kid. Printing is cheaper and you can scale it to your size — but it is the big time investment this whole manual is about. Many people print the helmet (the showpiece) and buy a soft-armor kit for the body.</div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>Start here — it's the showpiece and your skills test.</p><p>Print in pieces, glue, seam-fill, sand smooth, prime, then gloss white. Tinted visor so you can see out.</p><h3>Free Helmet Files</h3><ul><li>Stormtrooper ANH helmet by KeepTheBOX · FREE · Printables model 3041 (full-scale, wearable) — printables.com/model/3041-stormtrooper-anh-helmet</li><li>Full-scale wearable Stormtrooper helmet · Thingiverse (community remix, free)</li><li>Clone helmet — search \"Phase 2 clone helmet\" on Cults3D / Printables (free + paid)</li></ul><p>It is one self-contained project that teaches every skill you need for the rest of the suit. The visor is usually dark mesh fabric or a strip of tinted plastic glued behind the slot — you need to be able to SEE out, so test it before the event. The little mic tips on the sides are called Hovi tips.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Printing the Armour","body":"<p class='lead'>Zone by zone: chest, back, shoulders, arms, legs, belt.</p><p>0.2mm layers, 3 walls, 10–15% infill. Split big plates for a small printer.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Size It to You</div><p>Most trooper files are modelled for a 6-foot adult. If you are smaller, scale the whole set down in your slicer (try 85–90%) and — importantly — scale every piece by the <strong>same</strong> amount so they still fit together. Test-print one small part at your chosen scale first.</p></div><h3>Free Full-Armor Files</h3><ul><li>Wearable Stormtrooper armor (full suit) · FREE · Thingiverse — community set, \"not screen-accurate\" but great to learn on</li><li>Stormtrooper armor (WIP, 501st-aimed) by KeepTheBOX · FREE · Printables model 56373</li><li>Screen-accurate / 501st sets · paid (e.g. Galactic Armory) — buy once you know you will finish; worth it for 501st approval</li></ul><p>Start on a free set to practise — you WILL re-print pieces as you learn.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Size It to You</div>Most files fit a 6-foot adult. Smaller? Scale the whole set down in your slicer (try 85–90%) and scale every piece by the SAME percent — or nothing lines up. Use a brim (the flat skirt the printer adds so a part grips the bed) on tall pieces.</div>"},{"num":"07","title":"Finishing","body":"<p class='lead'>Sand → fill → prime → gloss white → detail → clear coat.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ SPRAY SAFETY</div>Spray outside, wear a mask, and have an adult with you if you're under 18.</div><h3>Shopping List</h3><ul><li>Sandpaper — wet/dry, 180 / 320 / 600 (add 800–1000 for extra shine)</li><li>Grey filler primer + gloss white spray</li><li>Black acrylic — the detail lines (frown, vents, markings)</li><li>Respirator/dust mask, painter's tape, super glue, putty for seams</li><li>Clone only: coloured spray for unit markings + masking tape</li></ul><p>Troopers are GLOSS white, so the smoother you sand, the better the shine. Join multi-part pieces, putty the joins, cure, sand flat. Mask before painting the black frown and vents (and clone colour markings). Spray outside or in an open garage only — never indoors.</p>"},{"num":"08","title":"Strapping & Fit","body":"<p class='lead'>Elastic and webbing hold the plates on.</p><p>Do a 90-minute test wear — armour is hot and limits movement. Fix the pinch points at home.</p><p>Do a full test wear at home before the event: armor pinches, straps slip, and you find out fast if you can sit, walk, and see. Fix it in the workshop, not at the con.</p>"},{"num":"09","title":"Game Day","body":"<p class='lead'>Visor clear, plates secure, blaster ready.</p><ul><li>Repair kit: spare elastic, super glue, white touch-up paint.</li><li>Take helmet breaks; have a buddy guide you on stairs.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Look sir, droids!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; point at the floor, sudden and proud</i></li><li>&ldquo;Move along. Move along.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; flat and bored, one lazy hand wave</i></li><li>&ldquo;There's one. Set for stun.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; call it across the room, aim a finger</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I had a clear shot in dodgeball. I missed. It's tradition.</li><li>Move along, move along — the snack table isn't going anywhere.</li><li>Look sir, homework! ...I've decided not to hit that either.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"10","title":"Meeting Your Fans","body":"<p class=\"lead\">Half the magic of a costume is what you say when someone walks up. Here are in-character lines ready to go — gentle ones for little kids, and bigger ones for older fans and photos.</p><h3>For Little Kids · Kind and Playful</h3><ul><li>\"A clone trooper always looks out for little ones — reporting for duty!\"</li><li>\"Stand tall, recruit! You'd make a great trooper.\"</li><li>\"We stick together. That's how the good guys win.\"</li></ul><h3>Big and In-Character · For Older Fans and Photos</h3><ul><li>\"Rookies. They never listen.\"</li><li>\"Hold the line.\"</li><li>\"We're soldiers — we do our duty.\"</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Golden Rule · Read the Room</div>Kneel to their eye level, keep it warm, and never break character to correct them. Ask their name and make them the hero — and if a prop weapon is involved, keep it lowered and pointed away. The goal is simple: every kid walks away thinking they just met the real one.</div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Stormtrooper armour STL","designer":"search Thingiverse / Cults3D","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=stormtrooper+armor"},{"name":"Clone trooper armour STL","designer":"search Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=clone%20trooper"},{"name":"E-11 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=e-11+blaster"},{"name":"501st Legion standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Helmet","detail":"Clone T-visor or Stormtrooper dome. Print, seam-fill, gloss white."},{"name":"Chest + back plate","detail":"Core of the armour — split for small printers."},{"name":"Shoulder bells (×2)","detail":"Mirror one STL."},{"name":"Ab / kidney plate","detail":"Links chest to belt."},{"name":"Forearms + biceps (×4)","detail":"Test-print ONE forearm first."},{"name":"Shin + knee plates","detail":"Both legs."},{"name":"Belt boxes","detail":"Mount on a webbing belt."},{"name":"Codpiece + thighs","detail":"Elastic straps."}],"buy":[{"name":"White boots","detail":"Plain, under the leg armour."},{"name":"Black/white gloves","detail":"Clone black, Stormtrooper white."},{"name":"Filler primer + gloss white","detail":"2–3 cans."},{"name":"Sandpaper 120–400","detail":"For smoothing seams."},{"name":"Elastic + webbing belt","detail":"Straps everything on."},{"name":"Blaster","detail":"DC-15 (Clone) or E-11 (Stormtrooper)."}]}},"luke":{"meta":{"word":"LUKE","accent":"#3fae5a","body":"jedi","budget":110,"btn":"⚔ JEDI","dur":"4 weeks","hrs":"10–20 hrs","parts":"Cloth + saber","budgetRange":"€60–150","lead":"The black Jedi, two looks: Return of the Jedi & the Book of Boba Fett. The easiest build in the series — mostly cloth and a green blade.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The bib-front reads grey for most of the film — the pale white lining only flashes when the tunic falls open at the climax. Get that reveal and it reads as Luke instantly.","intro":"OPERATION LUKE","introSub":"JEDI ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE R2","footer":"OPERATION LUKE · JEDI BUILD MANUAL · THE BLACK JEDI · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"luke_public.pdf","weekPdf":"luke_byweek.pdf","quote":"I am a Jedi, like my father before me."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Hair","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Style","hours":1,"cost":10,"priority":"LOW","description":"Luke's neat, slightly tousled hair. A wig if yours isn't there.","tip":"ROTJ Luke is clean-shaven and tidy.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Outer Tunic","type":"TORSO · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The black ROTJ tunic that crosses over — opens to show a pale inner lining. Book of Boba Fett = looser robes.","tip":"Black outside, white/cream inside is the key tell.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"No plates — Luke is all cloth.","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Inner Tunic","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Pale cream/white layer under the black tunic — it shows at the opening.","tip":"Any plain cream top works to start.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark belt with a clip for the saber.","tip":"Match the boot colour.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Obi / Sash","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":10,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Cloth sash at the waist holding the tunic closed.","tip":"Snug = clean silhouette.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Robe (optional)","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":40,"priority":"LOW","description":"A dark hooded robe for the Book of Boba Fett look; ROTJ often goes without.","tip":"Hem ~5cm off the floor.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Luke is a hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion Luke CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Black trousers tucked into the boots.","tip":"Plain black.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tall black boots.","tip":"Riding-style boots work.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Black Glove","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":8,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"ROTJ Luke wears a black glove on the RIGHT hand (his mechanical hand).","tip":"One glove, right hand.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Green Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":60,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Luke's blade is GREEN. Buy a green LED/neopixel, or set any saber you own to green.","tip":"Green, not blue — that's ROTJ Luke.","files":[{"name":"Luke ROTJ saber STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=luke+rotj+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Plan + order tunic, robe, saber"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Fit & hem; black-outside/white-inside check"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Set saber to green; glove on right hand"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Luke Skywalker</span> two ways — ROTJ black Jedi and the Book of Boba Fett look. The easiest build in the series.</p><p>All cloth, a green blade, one glove. No printing needed.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>Return of the Jedi</b> — black tunic with a pale lining, green saber.</li><li><b>Book of Boba Fett</b> — looser dark Jedi robes.</li></ul><p>Same green blade for both.</p>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Tunic","body":"<p class='lead'>Black outside, white inside.</p><p>The ROTJ tunic crosses over and opens to show a cream layer — that's the detail fans look for.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Secret Detail</div><p>The film used the white lining on purpose — to make you wonder if Luke would turn to the dark side. For the reveal, wear a thin white shirt or collar under the black tunic, or line the robe's edge with white fabric. Cheap to do, and it's the detail that makes people say \"you really know Luke.\"</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Lightsaber","body":"<p class='lead'>Luke's blade is <span class='accent'>green</span>.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ EASY ANSWER</div>Buy a green saber, or set one you own to green and lock it.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Approval Note · Rebel Legion</div><p>Luke is a hero, so he belongs in the <strong>Rebel Legion</strong> (the good-guys' costuming club), not the 501st. For approval: green blade, mostly-black ridged hilt with silver ends. A hilt-only static prop is fine. Green = Jedi Knight Luke; don't use red — that's the dark side.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"Build Sequence","body":"<ul><li>Order tunic, robe, saber, boots.</li><li>Fit & hem; layer it.</li><li>Glove on the right hand; saber green.</li></ul>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Black-outside/white-inside is the key detail.</li><li>Green, not blue.</li><li>One glove, right hand.</li></ul><p class='accent'>May the Force be with you.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Two More Tips</div><ul><li><strong>Matte, not shiny.</strong> Shiny black reads as \"cheap costume\" — a light dusting of fabric-safe matte spray (or just washing it) knocks the shine down so it looks like real cloth.</li><li><strong>Why the glove?</strong> Like his father, Luke has a mechanical right hand — Vader cut his off. Going all-out? Paint a cheap glove silver underneath for the ROTJ torn-glove robot-fingers reveal.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Shien / Djem So</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ FORM V · SHIEN / DJEM SO — “The Way of the Krayt Dragon”</div><p>Power counters — take the strike on your blade, then send it back harder. Luke fights his father's form with a farm boy's patience: solid blocks, sudden strong answers, and the discipline to stop before the killing blow. He inherited Form V from the Skywalker line and proved in the Emperor's throne room that its power doesn't have to become anger.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#46d95e\">⬤</span> Green — self-built RotJ hilt — his first blue blade was lost at Bespin</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Block-and-answer: practise a two-count rhythm — catch an imaginary overhead cut on your blade, then step in with one strong diagonal counter; ten slow reps each side.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I'm Luke Skywalker. I'm here to rescue you.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; burst through a door for full effect</i></li><li>&ldquo;But I was going into Tosche Station to pick up some power converters!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; maximum whine — it's the law</i></li><li>&ldquo;That's not true! That's impossible!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; stagger back like the floor just dropped</i></li><li>&ldquo;The Force is strong in my family.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; quiet and serious, gaze into the distance</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>But I was going into Tosche Station to pick up some snacks!</li><li>I used to bullseye womp rats back home. Dodgeball doesn't scare me.</li><li>The Force is strong in my family. The Wi-Fi is not.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Luke ROTJ saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=luke+rotj+lightsaber"},{"name":"Full Luke ROTJ costume","designer":"AliExpress / eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Luke+Jedi+costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion standards","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Or buy a green neopixel saber."}],"buy":[{"name":"Black outer tunic","detail":"Crosses over, pale lining."},{"name":"Cream inner tunic","detail":"Shows at the opening."},{"name":"Obi / sash + belt","detail":"Holds it closed."},{"name":"Black trousers + tall boots","detail":"Plain black."},{"name":"Black glove (1)","detail":"Right hand only."},{"name":"Green lightsaber","detail":"Set to green."},{"name":"Dark robe (optional)","detail":"For the Book of Boba Fett look."}]}},"kylo":{"meta":{"word":"KYLO","accent":"#d42b2b","body":"jedi","budget":140,"btn":"⚔ SITH","dur":"6 weeks","hrs":"20–40 hrs","parts":"Cloth + helmet","budgetRange":"€80–200","lead":"Vader's grandson, three looks: masked, unmasked, and the cracked Rise of Skywalker mask. Layered black robes and a red crossguard blade.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"It's all about the layers — hood, cowl, tunic, ribbed sleeves. A single flat tunic looks bare.","intro":"OPERATION KYLO","introSub":"FIRST ORDER · BUILD MANUAL · FILE REN","footer":"OPERATION KYLO · BUILD MANUAL · THE MASKED HEIR · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"kylo_public.pdf","weekPdf":"kylo_byweek.pdf","quote":"Let the past die."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Helmet / Mask","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":8,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The masked look: black helmet with a silver mesh face strip. TROS adds glowing red cracks. Unmasked = just hair + a scar.","tip":"TROS cracks: glue red-painted glue lines into the seams.","files":[{"name":"Kylo helmet STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=kylo+ren+helmet"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Cowl / Hood","type":"TORSO · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":25,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The layered hood and cowl over the shoulders — a big part of his silhouette.","tip":"Layering is everything for Kylo.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Kylo is cloth, not armour.","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Tunic + Ribbed Sleeves","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Black layered tunic with the distinctive ribbed/pleated sleeves.","tip":"The ribbed sleeves are the signature — don't skip them.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide black belt over the tunic.","tip":"Black on black.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Sash / Skirt","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The hanging cloth panels below the belt.","tip":"Adds the layered look.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Outer Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":45,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The long black cloak/coat over everything.","tip":"Hem ~5cm off the floor.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check the build against the 501st Legion CRL — their approval standards for screen-accurate villain and Imperial costumes. Kylo Ren is an approved 501st costume.","tip":"501st Legion = the costuming club that sets the standard for villain builds.","files":[{"name":"501st Kylo CRL","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Black trousers tucked into the boots.","tip":"Plain black.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":45,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tall black boots.","tip":"Riding-style.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Black leather gloves — both hands.","tip":"Plain black leather.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Crossguard Saber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":80,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The red, unstable crossguard blade with two side vents. The signature weapon.","tip":"A crossguard neopixel saber sells the whole costume.","files":[{"name":"Kylo crossguard saber STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=kylo+ren+crossguard+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Plan + order robes, helmet, saber"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Helmet finish + layer the tunic"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Cowl, belt, sash, gloves"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"TROS cracks (optional) + saber to red"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Kylo Ren</span> three ways: masked, unmasked, and the cracked TROS mask.</p><p>Layered black robes and a red crossguard blade. Cloth build with one printed helmet.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Dark Side = 501st</div><p>Kylo is Vader's grandson — Ben Solo, fallen to the dark side. As a villain he belongs in the <strong>501st Legion</strong> (the bad-guys' costuming club), same as his grandfather Vader.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>Masked</b> — the full helmet.</li><li><b>Unmasked</b> — hair + scar, no helmet.</li><li><b>TROS cracked</b> — reassembled mask with glowing red cracks.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Scar</div><p>After his fight with Rey, Kylo has a long diagonal scar from his forehead, across the eye area, down to the neck. Draw it with cream scar makeup or thin scar wax — a clean line, not a gash. (In The Force Awakens, before the fight, there's no scar.)</p></div><p>Upgrade path: start unmasked for the fastest win — add a mask later for the masked look, or a cracked mask for the Rise of Skywalker version. Same robes the whole way.</p>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>Print, finish matte black, add the silver mesh face strip.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ TROS CRACKS</div>Run red-painted hot-glue lines into the seams for the repaired look.</div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Robes","body":"<p class='lead'>Layers, layers, layers.</p><p>Hood + cowl + ribbed-sleeve tunic + sash + outer cloak. The ribbed sleeves are the key detail.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Wire the Scarf</div><p>The hood and scarf give Kylo his hunched, looming silhouette — the screen costume hides wire inside the scarf so it holds its shape. A length of bendable craft wire sewn into the scarf and hood edge lets you shape that signature draped collar — the single biggest \"that's really Kylo\" upgrade to a cheap robe.</p></div><h3>Layer Order &amp; Texture</h3><p>Skin → out: under-tunic (high collar) → sleeved shirt → surcoat (the long ribbed outer layer) → belt with saber clip → hooded cowl + scarf → gloves and boots. Kylo's robes have a subtle ribbed / quilted texture, not plain flat black — textured fabric or pintucked panels read far more accurate than a smooth costume robe. Keep the surcoat matte black and floor-skimming: hem it about 5 cm (2 inches) off the floor, safe on stairs but still dramatic.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">WIRE THE SCARF</div>\"Let the past die — but wire your scarf so the hood doesn't flop.\" The screen costume hides wire inside the scarf so it holds its shape. Craft wire sewn into the scarf and hood edge shapes that hunched, looming draped collar — the single biggest \"that's really Kylo\" upgrade to a cheap robe.</div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>Red crossguard, two side vents, unstable look.</p><p>A crossguard neopixel saber is the showpiece.</p><h3>Ways to Get One</h3><p>The crossguard is the two small side blades venting out of the hilt, next to the main red blade. Own a saber from another build? You can set any saber to RED for the basic look — but the true crossguard needs the three-blade hilt: buy or print it.</p><ul><li><strong>A · Buy a crossguard saber</strong> — the easy route.</li><li><strong>B · Neopixel crossguard</strong> — bright red, sound, crackle effect. Best value.</li><li><strong>C · Print the hilt</strong> — search \"Kylo Ren crossguard saber\" on Thingiverse / Printables.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">501ST APPROVAL</div>Red main blade + two short crossguard vents, battered/sparking hilt. A hilt-only static prop is fine.</div><p>A crossguard is special, but you can set any saber to RED for the look while you save up or build the real thing — the robes and the attitude carry the costume.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"The Unmasked Look","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The easiest Kylo: same robes, no helmet. The whole costume rests on two details — the scar and the hair.</p><h3>The Scar</h3><p>After his fight with Rey, Kylo has a long diagonal scar from his forehead, across the eye area, down to the neck. Draw it with cream scar makeup or thin scar wax — a clean line, not a gash. (In The Force Awakens, before the fight, there's no scar.)</p><h3>The Hair</h3><p>Dark, wavy, shoulder-length hair, parted and swept. A wig nails it instantly if your hair is short. Clean-shaven to light stubble.</p><h3>Posture &amp; Photos</h3><p>Kylo is intense and a little unstable. For photos: red crossguard lit, an angry or brooding expression, blade held low and angled. The scar catches the eye — turn that side to the camera.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Finishing the Helmet","body":"<p class=\"lead\">(Unmasked builders skip this.) For the masked and cracked looks, the helmet is the showpiece: matte/satin black with silver/chrome ridges around the eye slot — the opposite of a glossy trooper. A fresh print is rough and striped; here's the routine that turns it into a screen-style mask.</p><h3>Print &amp; Shopping List</h3><p>Print in pieces (it's bigger than the bed), glue, fill the seams. You'll need:</p><ul><li>Sandpaper (180 / 320 / 600) · grey filler primer</li><li>Matte or satin black spray (not gloss) · chrome/silver spray or trim for the ridges</li><li>Black sheer mesh for the eye slot · painter's tape · super glue + putty</li><li>Cracked look: red LED strip + a diffuser (material that spreads the light into a smooth glow) + a battery pack</li></ul><h3>The Step-by-Step</h3><p>1 · SAND 180 → 320 → 600. 2 · GLUE &amp; FILL the seams, sand flat. 3 · PRIME grey, wet-sand, repeat until smooth. 4 · BASE matte/satin black, 2–3 thin coats. 5 · RIDGES — mask around the eye and spray chrome (or apply chrome trim). 6 · MESH — glue black sheer fabric behind the eye slot: hidden eyes, but you can still see. 7 · CRACKED? Cut thin crack lines and back them with red LEDs + a diffuser so they truly glow. Bonus detail: the screen helmet hides a vocoder — the voice-changer behind Kylo's modulated voice.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">SEE OUT, STAY SAFE</div>Test your visibility before the event — the eye slot is small. Use breathable sheer fabric, not solid plastic, behind the slot. Never drive in the mask.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">SPRAY SAFETY</div>Spray outside or in an open garage only — never indoors. If you're under 18, have an adult with you — especially for any wiring/soldering on the LED cracks.</div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Build Sequence","body":"<p class=\"lead\">Two tracks: cloth for every look, mask only if you're going masked or cracked.</p><h3>Cloth Track (All Looks)</h3><p>1 · Order robes, cowl, scarf, gloves, boots, belt, crossguard saber — order early. 2 · Fit &amp; hem: surcoat ~5 cm off the floor, sleeves to the wrist. 3 · Wire the scarf/hood so the collar drapes right. 4 · Layer drill: under-tunic → shirt → surcoat → belt → cowl. Gloves + boots on.</p><h3>Mask Track (Masked + Cracked Only)</h3><p>A · Print or buy the helmet early. B · Finish it: sand, prime, matte black, chrome ridges, mesh eyes. C · Cracked look? Cut cracks, wire red LEDs + diffuser, test the glow. D · Unmasked instead? Skip all this — just do the scar + hair.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE 90-MINUTE RULE</div>First full wear, do 90 minutes at home. Robes are hot, the scarf shifts, the mask limits your view. Find the problems before the event.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">GAME DAY KIT</div>Night-before check: saber charged and RED, scarf wired and draping, mesh eyes clear, cracks glowing — or scar drawn and wig ready. Pack safety pins, spare gloves, blade + LED batteries, and a touch-up of scar makeup.</div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Manufacturing Files","body":"<p class=\"lead\">Every file and link in this manual, gathered for quick reference. Three ways to source the costume: (A) buy a full Kylo set, (B) buy the pieces, (C) sew/print it — most builders do B.</p><h3>Helmet Files</h3><ul><li>Kylo Ren helmet (wearable) — cults3d.com / Thingiverse / Printables (search: Kylo Ren helmet) — free + paid versions exist</li><li>TROS cracked helmet — thingiverse.com (search: Kylo Ren broken helmet) — some are pre-grooved for LED strips</li></ul><h3>Lightsaber Files</h3><ul><li>Crossguard hilt — printables.com / Thingiverse (search: Kylo Ren crossguard lightsaber)</li><li>Neopixel-ready crossguard hilts — thingiverse.com (search: Kylo crossguard neopixel) — for the glow + crackle</li></ul><h3>Standards &amp; Shopping</h3><ul><li>Kylo TFA standards — crls.501st.com (search: Kylo Ren)</li><li>Full set — AliExpress / eBay (search: Kylo Ren costume)</li><li>Crossguard saber — AliExpress (search: Kylo Ren crossguard lightsaber)</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">FREE TO LEARN, PAID TO PERFECT</div>Same as every build in this series: start on a free file to practise, buy a screen-accurate set once you know you'll finish. The helmet is worth getting right — it's the whole look.</div>"},{"num":"10","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Layer everything; never a flat single tunic.</li><li>Both hands gloved.</li><li>Red blade, crossguard.</li></ul>"},{"num":"11","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Unorthodox</span>, wielded single (crossguard).</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · UNORTHODOX</div><p>All rage, no textbook — wide broadsword swings, brute-force blade locks, and forward pressure even while wounded. Reads closest to Form V Djem So pushed past its limits into raw, untamed fury. Trained by Luke, twisted by Snoke — the cracked, spitting crossguard blade is his conflicted fighting style made visible.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#e0312e\">⬤</span> Red (unstable) — crossguard hilt with two side-vent quillon blades — cracked kyber crystal</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single (crossguard)</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Heavy cuts: slow, exaggerated broadsword swings from the shoulder, freezing at the end of each one to check that the crossguard vents cleared your own arm and body.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"12","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;You need a teacher! I can show you the ways of the Force!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; shout it mid-duel, saber arm out</i></li><li>&ldquo;I will finish what you started.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; whisper it to a helmet if you've got one</i></li><li>&ldquo;I know what I have to do, but I don't know if I have the strength to do it.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; slow and quiet — no shouting</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>Let the past die. Especially the photo of my old haircut.</li><li>I will finish what you started... unless it's broccoli.</li><li>Nobody touches the helmet. The glue is still drying.</li></ul></div><h3>Meeting Your Fans</h3><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">GOLDEN RULE · READ THE ROOM</div>Villains are the best part of a photo — but a looming Sith can terrify a 4-year-old. If a little one looks unsure, drop the scary instantly and go kind: \"Even I started small — you're going to do big things.\" · \"Be brave. Even grumpy knights respect brave kids.\"</div><p>Universal tips for young fans: kneel to their eye level, never break character to correct them, ask their name and make them the hero, and keep the saber lowered and pointed away. Every kid walks away thinking they just met the real one.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">READ THE ROOM</div>Half the magic of a costume is what you say when someone walks up. Villains make the best photos — but if a little one looks unsure, drop the scary instantly and switch to the kind lines.</div>"},{"num":"13","title":"The Three Looks, Side by Side","body":"<p class=\"lead\">All three looks share the same black layered robes; what changes is the head — mask, no mask, or the cracked mask — and one scar.</p><h3>The Three Looks</h3><ul><li><strong>1 · Masked (The Force Awakens)</strong> — black robes + the silver-ridged helmet. The classic.</li><li><strong>2 · Unmasked</strong> — same robes, no helmet, plus the diagonal facial scar and Kylo's dark hair.</li><li><strong>3 · Cracked mask (Rise of Skywalker)</strong> — the helmet rebuilt with glowing red cracks, Kintsugi style (the Japanese art of repairing pottery with gold seams).</li></ul><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Head</span><span class=\"col-val\">Silver-ridged helmet · bare face + scar + dark hair · helmet with glowing cracks</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Robes</span><span class=\"col-val\">Black layered — identical in all three</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Blade</span><span class=\"col-val\">Red crossguard — identical in all three</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Difficulty</span><span class=\"col-val\">Masked: medium · Unmasked: easiest · Cracked: hardest (LEDs)</span></div></div><h3>Quick Start &amp; Upgrade Path</h3><p>Pick before you build — it decides whether you need a mask, and which mask. First Kylo? Build the unmasked look — it's just the black robes + saber + a drawn-on scar, no helmet to print or buy. Add a finished helmet → the masked look. Cut and backlight cracks in the helmet → the Rise of Skywalker look. Same robes and blade the whole way.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">ALL THREE SHARE THESE</div>Red crossguard saber · black layered robes · hooded cape/cowl · gloves · black boots. Only the head changes between looks.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">DARK SIDE = 501ST</div>Kylo is a villain, so he belongs in the 501st Legion (the bad-guys' costuming club), same as his grandfather Vader.</div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Kylo helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=kylo+ren+helmet"},{"name":"Kylo crossguard saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=kylo+ren+crossguard+lightsaber"},{"name":"Full Kylo costume","designer":"AliExpress / eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Kylo+Ren+costume"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Helmet","detail":"Matte black + silver mesh strip."},{"name":"Crossguard saber hilt","detail":"Or buy a crossguard neopixel."}],"buy":[{"name":"Layered black tunic","detail":"Ribbed sleeves — the signature."},{"name":"Hood + cowl","detail":"Big part of the silhouette."},{"name":"Outer cloak","detail":"Long, hemmed off the floor."},{"name":"Belt + sash","detail":"Over the tunic."},{"name":"Black trousers + tall boots","detail":"Plain black."},{"name":"Black gloves","detail":"Both hands."},{"name":"Red crossguard saber","detail":"The weapon."}]}},"mando":{"meta":{"word":"MANDO","accent":"#c8ccd2","body":"armor","budget":300,"btn":"⚔ GUILD","dur":"8 weeks","hrs":"50–100 hrs","parts":"Armour + helmet","budgetRange":"€150–350","lead":"Din Djarin, two looks: early mixed-metal armour & full shiny beskar. The T-visor helmet is the heart of the build.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The helmet is everything — nail the T-visor first and you're instantly the Mandalorian.","intro":"OPERATION MANDO","introSub":"GUILD · BUILD MANUAL · FILE DIN","footer":"OPERATION MANDO · BUILD MANUAL · THIS IS THE WAY · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"mando_public.pdf","weekPdf":"mando_byweek.pdf","quote":"This is the Way."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"T-Visor Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The iconic T-visor beskar helmet. Print, seam-fill, sand, then chrome/silver finish.","tip":"Start here — the helmet IS Mando.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Pauldrons","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Two shoulder pauldrons — one often has the mudhorn signet.","tip":"Paint the mudhorn signet on one.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Plates","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The central chest plates over the flak vest.","tip":"Early look = mismatched metals; beskar = all shiny silver.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Flak Vest","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The padded vest the plates mount onto, plus a cape/half-cape.","tip":"Brown/tan vest under the plates.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Pouches","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide belt with pouches and the side holster.","tip":"Leather belt + printed buckle.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Cod + Thigh Armour","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Cod plate and thigh guards.","tip":"Strap so you can sit.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Cape / Half-Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":25,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The worn half-cape over one shoulder.","tip":"Weather it to match the armour.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Mandalorian Mercs club standards.","tip":"Mando Mercs = the bounty-hunter club.","files":[{"name":"Mando Mercs","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin + Knee Armour","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Shin guards (the right shin shows the grip of a hidden knife/vibroblade) + knee plates.","tip":"Both legs — the flamethrower lives on the vambrace, not the shin.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":45,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Brown/tan tall boots.","tip":"Worn leather look.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gloves + Vambraces","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Forearm vambraces (the signature gadget pieces) + leather gloves.","tip":"Left vambrace = whistling-birds launcher; both vambraces carry the flamethrower/whipcord — add a flamethrower nozzle detail.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blaster / Rifle","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":35,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Mando carries an IB-94 blaster pistol and an Amban rifle, not a saber.","tip":"Print or buy; weather to match.","files":[{"name":"Amban rifle STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=mandalorian+amban+rifle"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 8–7","task":"Plan + order filament & flak vest"},{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Print + finish the helmet"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Chest, pauldrons, vambraces"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Legs, belt, cape"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Weather, dress rehearsal, game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>An armour build like the Trooper, but with a worn, mixed-metal look.</p><p>~1.5–3 kg of filament. The helmet is the heart of it.</p><h3>The Honest Numbers</h3><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Pieces</span><span class=\"col-val\">Helmet + ~14 armour plates + soft parts (flight suit, cape, belt, bandolier)</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Finishing</span><span class=\"col-val\">Every plate is sanded, primed, painted silver, then weathered</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Cost</span><span class=\"col-val\">Roughly €120–350 all-in, depending on free vs paid files and the flight suit</span></div></div><p><strong>The smart path:</strong> print the helmet first — it's the icon of the costume and your skills test. Then add the chest + pauldrons (the early look needs only a few beskar pieces), and grow into the full silver set.</p><p>Mandalorian costumes have their own famous club, the Mandalorian Mercs, plus the 501st/Rebel Legion depending on the character. Din fits the Mercs perfectly.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Early or Beskar?","body":"<ul><li><b>Early</b> — mismatched metals, scavenged feel.</li><li><b>Full beskar</b> — all shiny silver.</li></ul><p>Same parts; the difference is the finish.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Quick Start</div><p>First Mando? Build the <strong>early look</strong>. Grey, weathered armour hides print lines and paint mistakes, and you only need a couple of pieces to look shiny. Upgrade to full beskar later by painting the rest silver.</p></div><p>Din Djarin started in mixed, scuffed armour — mostly grey durasteel (ordinary metal) with only a few pieces of beskar, the shiny Mandalorian iron. Pick your look before you paint — it changes the colours and how many pieces shine.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">QUICK START</div>First Mando? Build the early look. Grey, weathered armour hides print lines and paint mistakes, and only the helmet, one pauldron and the chest need to shine. Later, paint the rest silver and lighten the weathering — full beskar, same armour map.</div><p><strong>The mudhorn signet:</strong> the right shoulder pauldron carries Din's clan symbol after the episode with the Child. It's a simple raised emblem you can print, sculpt, or paint on — a small detail fans always look for.</p>"},{"num":"03","title":"Procurement Roster","body":"<p class=\"lead\">Three ways to get the armour: (A) buy a finished kit, (B) 3D-print it, (C) mix — print the plates, buy the flight suit + cape. Paste Chinese search terms into Taobao, or use English on AliExpress / eBay.</p><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Full Mando set</span><span class=\"col-val\">Finished, pre-painted — AliExpress / eBay: \"Mandalorian Din Djarin costume\"</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Helmet</span><span class=\"col-val\">Pre-made silver — AliExpress: \"Mandalorian helmet beskar\"</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Flight suit</span><span class=\"col-val\">Grey under-layer, top + pants</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Cape / poncho</span><span class=\"col-val\">Worn cloth · plus grey gloves</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Filament</span><span class=\"col-val\">Grey or silver PLA (print path)</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Blaster / rifle prop</span><span class=\"col-val\">IB-94 pistol / Amban rifle</span></div></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">PRINT VS BUY</div>A bought kit is faster and pre-painted, but pricey and may not fit a kid. Printing is cheaper and you can scale it — it's the time investment this manual is about. Many builders print the helmet + a few plates and buy the soft flight suit.</div><p>Free to learn, paid to perfect: practise on a free file, buy a screen-accurate set once you know you'll finish. The Mando Mercs club has standards if you want to join — mandalorianmercs.org.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>The T-visor is the icon.</p><p>Print, seam-fill, sand glass-smooth, then a chrome/silver finish. Tinted visor so you can see out.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Helmet Never Comes Off</div><p>For a screen-accurate Mando the helmet never comes off in public — \"this is the Way\" — so visibility matters even more. Test that you can genuinely see out before the event, and never drive in the helmet.</p></div><h3>Helmet Files</h3><ul><li>Mandalorian / Din Djarin helmet — search Cults3D / Thingiverse / Printables for free + paid wearable versions</li><li>Print in pieces (dome, face, ears), glue, fill the seams, then finish</li></ul><p>Settings: 0.2 mm layers, 3 walls, 10–15% infill, brim on tall pieces. Keep the T-slot crisp and symmetrical when you sand.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE T-VISOR</div>The visor is usually tinted acrylic or dark mesh behind the T-slot. You must be able to see out — test it before the event. The helmet never comes off in public for a screen-accurate Mando (\"this is the Way\"), so visibility matters even more.</div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Armour","body":"<p class='lead'>Chest, pauldrons, vambraces, legs.</p><p>Mount the plates on a brown flak vest. One pauldron gets the mudhorn signet.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Mudhorn Signet</div><p>The right shoulder pauldron carries the mudhorn signet — Din's clan symbol after the episode with the Child. It's a simple raised emblem you can print, sculpt, or paint on. A small detail fans always look for.</p></div><p>Din's beskar is a set of separate plates worn over a grey flight suit. Once the helmet proves your settings, work zone by zone — the plates are mostly flat-ish curves, easier than a full trooper suit. Print them hollow: 8–12% infill.</p><h3>Armour Files</h3><ul><li>Full set — search \"Mandalorian Din Djarin armor STL\" on Cults3D / Printables (free + paid)</li><li>Pre-beskar (early) set — the season-1 mixed look, sold by some makers (e.g. 3D Planet Props, Great Ape Studio)</li><li>Mudhorn signet pauldron — in most Din sets, or print/sculpt separately</li><li>Jetpack &amp; blaster props — search \"Mandalorian jetpack STL\", \"IB-94 blaster STL\" on Thingiverse</li></ul><p><strong>Size it to you:</strong> most Din files fit a ~5'11\" adult (Pedro Pascal's height). Smaller? Scale the whole set down by the same percent (try 85–90%) so the plates still line up. Test-print one small plate first.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Finishing & Weathering","body":"<p class='lead'>Silver base, then grime and battle chips.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ SPRAY SAFETY</div>Outside, mask on, adult present if under 18.</div><h3>Shopping List</h3><ul><li>Sandpaper (180/320/600, +800 for shine) · grey filler primer</li><li>Silver / chrome spray, or a metallic like Alclad / Molotow for extra shine</li><li>Black + brown acrylic for the weathering wash · gloss or satin clear coat</li><li>Respirator/dust mask, painter's tape, super glue, putty</li></ul><h3>Step by Step</h3><p>1 · Sand 180 → 320 → 600 — the smoother you go, the shinier the silver. 2 · Fill seams, sand flat. 3 · Prime grey, wet-sand until glassy. 4 · Silver: 2–3 thin coats — thin = shiny. 5 · Weather a thin black/brown wash into the edges + a few silver scratches (early look = heavy; beskar = light). 6 · Add the mudhorn signet. 7 · Satin clear coat to seal. Spray outside or in an open garage only — never indoors.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Gear","body":"<p class='lead'>Belt, pouches, cape, blaster.</p><p>The half-cape and the gadget vambrace sell the character.</p>"},{"num":"08","title":"Strapping & Build Sequence","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The plates strap over a grey flight suit. The soft parts — flight suit, cape, bandolier — are half the look, so don't skip them. Armour alone isn't Mando.</p><h3>How It Goes Together</h3><ul><li>Flight suit first — the grey base everything attaches to.</li><li>Chest + back joined at the shoulders; pauldrons strap over them.</li><li>Vambraces velcro/elastic around the forearms; hand plates on the gloves.</li><li>Belt, cummerbund, bandolier around the waist + across the chest.</li><li>Thigh, knee and greaves with elastic around the legs. Cape over one shoulder; boots on.</li></ul><h3>The Order That Works</h3><p>1 · Buy the flight suit, cape, gloves, boots, filament — order early. 2 · Print &amp; finish the helmet first — your skills test. 3 · Torso (chest, ab, back) + pauldrons; add the mudhorn signet. 4 · Arms (vambraces, hand plates). 5 · Legs (thighs, knee, greaves) + belt bits. 6 · Strap it all to the flight suit, add cape + bandolier, do a full 90-minute test wear. 7 · Early look? Weather heavily. Beskar? Light weathering, more shine.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">BOUNTY HUNTER REPAIR KIT</div>Spare elastic, super glue, zip ties, a little silver paint for chips — plates pop loose on a long day, and every Merc carries a kit. On the hunt: take helmet breaks where it's allowed, drink water, and have a buddy guide you in crowds and on stairs.</div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Game Day","body":"<ul><li>Visor clear, plates secure.</li><li>Repair kit + silver touch-up paint.</li><li>This is the Way.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I can bring you in warm, or I can bring you in cold.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; low and even — never raise your voice</i></li><li>&ldquo;Wherever I go, he goes.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; deadpan, nod at a plush Grogu</i></li><li>&ldquo;I'm a Mandalorian. Weapons are part of my religion.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; matter-of-fact, like reading a rule</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I can bring your lunch in warm, or I can bring it in cold. Choose wisely.</li><li>Wherever I go, my snacks go. This is the Way.</li><li>I own a jetpack and I'm still not allowed on the trampoline.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"10","title":"Meeting Your Fans","body":"<p class=\"lead\">Half the magic of a costume is what you say when someone walks up. Here are in-character lines ready to go — gentle ones for little kids, and bigger ones for older fans and photos.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE GOLDEN RULE · READ THE ROOM</div>Heroes get mobbed by little fans — lean into it. Kneel to their height, keep it warm, and let them feel like part of the adventure.</div><h3>For Little Kids — Kind and Playful</h3><ul><li>\"I've got a little one too — want to wave to him? Hi!\"</li><li>\"A Mandalorian always protects the little ones. That's you!\"</li><li>\"This is the Way — and so is being kind.\"</li></ul><h3>Big and In-Character — for Older Fans and Photos</h3><ul><li>\"This is the Way.\"</li><li>\"I have spoken.\"</li></ul><p>A few universal tips for meeting young fans: kneel to their eye level, never break character to correct them, ask their name and make them the hero, and if a prop weapon is involved keep it lowered and pointed away. The goal is simple — every kid walks away thinking they just met the real one.</p>"}],"files":[{"name":"Mandalorian helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse / Cults3D","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=mandalorian+helmet"},{"name":"Mando armour set STL","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=mandalorian%20armor"},{"name":"Amban rifle STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=mandalorian+amban+rifle"},{"name":"Mando Mercs club","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"T-visor helmet","detail":"Chrome/silver finish."},{"name":"Chest plates","detail":"Mount on the vest."},{"name":"Pauldrons (×2)","detail":"One with the mudhorn signet."},{"name":"Vambraces (×2)","detail":"One with gadgets."},{"name":"Shin + knee plates","detail":"Both legs."},{"name":"Cod + thighs","detail":"Strapped to sit."}],"buy":[{"name":"Flak vest","detail":"Brown/tan, plates mount on it."},{"name":"Belt + pouches","detail":"Wide, with holster."},{"name":"Half-cape","detail":"Worn over one shoulder."},{"name":"Tall boots + gloves","detail":"Worn leather."},{"name":"Silver paint + clear coat","detail":"Plus weathering."},{"name":"Blaster","detail":"IB-94 or Amban rifle."}]}},"boba":{"meta":{"word":"BOBA","accent":"#6f9a45","body":"armor","budget":300,"btn":"⚔ GUILD","dur":"8 weeks","hrs":"50–100 hrs","parts":"Armour + jetpack","budgetRange":"€120–350","lead":"The original bounty hunter, two looks: Empire & Jedi. Weathered green armour, a jetpack, and the famous dented helmet.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"A clean Boba looks wrong — weather everything. Chips, scratches and grime are the whole point.","intro":"OPERATION BOBA","introSub":"GUILD · BUILD MANUAL · FILE FETT","footer":"OPERATION BOBA · BUILD MANUAL · NO DISINTEGRATIONS · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"boba_public.pdf","weekPdf":"boba_byweek.pdf","quote":"He's no good to me dead."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Dented Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The green dented helmet with the rangefinder stalk. The signature piece.","tip":"Sand a gentle dent in; mask the kill stripes (yellow→orange ESB / dark orange ROTJ).","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Bells","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Two shoulder bells — one with a Mythosaur-skull symbol (often mistaken for a bantha skull).","tip":"Paint the symbols on.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Display Plate","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The chest plate with the coloured display panels.","tip":"Mask + paint the red/yellow panels.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Flak Vest + Cape","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The vest under the plates plus the shoulder cape (brown ESB / green ROTJ) with Wookiee braids.","tip":"Cape colour tells the era.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Ammo Belt + Pouches","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The ammo belt, girth belt, hip pouches and holster.","tip":"Leather + printed pouches.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Cod + Knees","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Codpiece, kidney armour and the two knee plates (with darts).","tip":"Both knees.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Jetpack","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The iconic rocket jetpack — reads 'Boba' almost as much as the helmet.","tip":"Print it as its own zone; mount on a back harness.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Mando Mercs / 501st standards.","tip":"Boba fits the bounty-hunter club.","files":[{"name":"Mando Mercs","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin Tools","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Shin guards with tool details.","tip":"Both legs.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":45,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Grey/tan tall boots.","tip":"Worn look.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gloves + Gauntlets","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Gauntlets (green ESB / red ROTJ) with a mini flamethrower look + grey gloves.","tip":"Gauntlet colour tells the era.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"EE-3 Blaster","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":30,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Boba carries the EE-3 carbine, not a saber.","tip":"Print or buy; weather it.","files":[{"name":"EE-3 blaster STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ee-3+boba+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 8–7","task":"Plan + order filament, vest, cape"},{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Print + finish the helmet"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Chest, shoulders, gauntlets"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Jetpack + belt + legs"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Weather everything, dress rehearsal, game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>An armour build where the magic is the <span class='accent'>weathering</span>.</p><p>~1.5–3 kg of filament. A clean Boba looks fake — chips and grime are the point.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Which Club?</div><p>Boba is a bounty hunter — he fits the <strong>Mandalorian Mercs</strong> costuming club, and the 501st Legion accepts him too. Either way, weathering accuracy is what gets a Boba approved.</p></div><p>Boba is an armour build like Mando and the Trooper — plates over a flight suit, plus a famous helmet. Very doable, but it's not a weekend cloth build.</p><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Pieces</span><span class=\"col-val\">Helmet + chest/back/shoulder plates + gauntlets + knees + a jetpack</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Finishing</span><span class=\"col-val\">Every piece is painted green, THEN weathered heavily (chips, scratches, grime)</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Cost</span><span class=\"col-val\">Roughly €120–350 all-in, depending on free vs paid files and the flight suit</span></div></div><h3>The Smart Path</h3><p>Print the helmet first — the dented green helmet IS Boba Fett. It's your skills test and the showpiece. If you only finish the helmet, you've still got an instantly recognisable costume.</p><h3>Which Club?</h3><p>Boba is a bounty hunter — he fits the Mandalorian Mercs costuming club, and the 501st Legion accepts him too. Either way, weathering accuracy is what gets a Boba approved.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Empire or Jedi?","body":"<ul><li><b>ESB</b> — green gauntlets, brown cape, yellow kill stripes.</li><li><b>ROTJ</b> — red gauntlets, green cape, red stripes.</li></ul><p>Same armour; the colours differ.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">More Era Tells</div><p>The flight suit changes too — grey for Empire, light blue-grey for Return of the Jedi — and the jetpack colour scheme differs slightly between the films. The easiest switch later is the gauntlet colour (green → red) and the cape (brown → green).</p></div><p>Two versions, same armour — pick before you paint. The differences are mostly colour, and fans absolutely notice them. The flight suit changes too: grey for Empire, light blue-grey for Jedi — and ROTJ weathering runs dirtier.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Kill Stripes</div>The little painted stripes on the helmet are Boba's \"kill stripes.\" Yellow for Empire, red for Jedi. A tiny detail, but it's one of the first things a fan checks.</div><p>Upgrade path: build the armour once. The easiest switch later is the gauntlet colour (green → red) and the cape (brown → green) — same helmet, armour and jetpack the whole way.</p>"},{"num":"03","title":"Anatomy of Boba","body":"<p class=\"lead\">Boba is armour plates + a flight suit + a lot of gear. Here's the full parts map, zone by zone.</p><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Head</span><span class=\"col-val\">Dented helmet + rangefinder stalk, T-visor</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Torso</span><span class=\"col-val\">Chest plate (with the coloured display panels), back plate, collar</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Shoulders</span><span class=\"col-val\">Two shoulder bells (bantha-skull symbol on one)</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Arms</span><span class=\"col-val\">Two gauntlets (green ESB / red ROTJ) + gloves</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Waist</span><span class=\"col-val\">Ammo belt, girth belt, hip pouches, holster</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Lower</span><span class=\"col-val\">Codpiece, kidney armour, two knee plates (with darts)</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Soft</span><span class=\"col-val\">Flight suit, neck seal, flak vest, cape, boots</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Gear</span><span class=\"col-val\">Jetpack, EE-3 blaster rifle, sidearm</span></div></div><h3>The Key Gear</h3><ul><li>Cape over the left shoulder (brown ESB / green ROTJ), often torn and weathered.</li><li>Gauntlets with a mini flamethrower + dart look.</li><li>Braids (Wookiee scalps) hanging from the left shoulder — a famous odd detail.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Jetpack Is Iconic</div>Boba's jetpack is a signature piece — the tall rocket pack with the central booster. Print it as its own zone; it reads \"Boba\" almost as much as the helmet. The gear is half his character — it turns \"green armour guy\" into Boba Fett.</div>"},{"num":"04","title":"Procurement Roster","body":"<p class=\"lead\">Three ways to gear up: (A) buy a finished kit, (B) 3D-print the armour, (C) mix — print the plates, buy the flight suit + cape. Paste Chinese search terms into Taobao, or use English on AliExpress / eBay.</p><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Full Boba set</span><span class=\"col-val\">Finished, roughly ¥800–3000</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Helmet</span><span class=\"col-val\">Pre-made, ¥200–700</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Flight suit</span><span class=\"col-val\">Grey (ESB) / blue-grey (ROTJ) · neck seal · flak vest</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Cape</span><span class=\"col-val\">Brown (ESB) / green (ROTJ)</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">Filament</span><span class=\"col-val\">Green or grey PLA (or any colour, then paint)</span></div></div><h3>Print vs Buy</h3><p>A bought kit is faster but pricey and may not fit a kid. Printing is cheaper and scalable — the time investment this manual is about. Many builders print the helmet + jetpack and buy the soft flight suit + cape.</p><h3>Files & Sizing</h3><ul><li>Full armour set — cults3d.com (search: Boba Fett armor)</li><li>Jetpack — thingiverse.com (search: Boba Fett jetpack)</li><li>EE-3 blaster — thingiverse.com (search: Boba Fett EE-3 blaster)</li><li>Gauntlets — in most sets, or search \"Boba Fett gauntlet STL\"</li><li>Full bought set — AliExpress / eBay (search: Boba Fett costume armor)</li></ul><p>Most Boba files fit an adult. If you're smaller, scale the whole set by the same percent (try 85–90%) so the plates line up — and test-print one small plate first. Practise on a free file, then buy a screen-accurate set once you know you'll finish. The Mando Mercs and 501st have Boba standards if you want to join.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>Green, dented, with the rangefinder.</p><p>Sand a gentle dent, mask the kill stripes, weather around the damage.</p><p>Files: search \"Boba Fett helmet\" on Cults3D / Thingiverse / Printables — free + paid wearable versions. Print in pieces (dome, face, back), glue, fill the seams, then finish. Settings: 0.2 mm layers, 3 walls, 10–15% infill, brim on the dome.</p><ul><li>The rangefinder — the stalk on the right side that flips up and down — is the signature piece; many builders make it pivot.</li><li>Tinted acrylic or dark mesh goes behind the T-visor so you can see out.</li></ul><p>The famous dent: many files include it — if yours doesn’t, press it in gently after printing while the plastic is warm, or sculpt it with filler. Mask the kill stripes with tape for crisp lines.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"The Armour & Jetpack","body":"<p class='lead'>Chest, shoulders, gauntlets, knees, and the jetpack.</p><p>The jetpack is iconic — print it as its own zone.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Finishing — Green & Worn","body":"<p class='lead'>Green base, silver chips, grime wash.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ SPRAY SAFETY</div>Outside, mask on, adult present if under 18.</div><p>Shopping list: sandpaper (180/320/600) · grey filler primer · green spray (armour base) · silver acrylic (chips) · red / yellow acrylic (panels, stripes) · black + brown acrylic (grime wash) · satin clear coat · respirator mask, tape, super glue, putty.</p><p>The step-by-step: 1 · SAND 180 → 320 → 600. 2 · FILL seams, sand flat. 3 · PRIME grey, wet-sand. 4 · GREEN, 2–3 thin coats. 5 · PANELS &amp; STRIPES — mask + paint the chest displays and kill stripes (yellow/red). 6 · WEATHER — chip silver onto the edges, then a black/brown grime wash all over (heavier for ROTJ). 7 · CLEAR COAT satin to seal.</p><p>Spray outside or in an open garage only — never indoors, and mask up for sanding dust too.</p>"},{"num":"08","title":"Gear","body":"<p class='lead'>Cape, braids, belt, EE-3 blaster.</p><p>The cape colour and the gauntlets set the era.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Famous Odd Details</div><ul><li>Cape over the <strong>left</strong> shoulder, often torn and weathered.</li><li>Braids (Wookiee scalps) hanging from the left shoulder — a famous odd detail fans love to spot.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Build Sequence","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The order that works — one zone at a time, helmet first.</p><ul><li>1 · Buy the flight suit, cape, gloves, boots, filament. Order early.</li><li>2 · Print &amp; finish the helmet first (dent, stripes, rangefinder, visor). Skills test.</li><li>3 · Print the torso (chest, back, collar) + shoulder bells. Paint + panels.</li><li>4 · Print the gauntlets (green or red) + knees. Finish.</li><li>5 · Print the jetpack + belt bits. Finish.</li><li>6 · Weather EVERYTHING — chips + grime. Strap to the flight suit, add cape + braids.</li><li>7 · Set the look: ESB (green gauntlets, brown cape, yellow stripes) or ROTJ (red, green, red).</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Don't Burn Out</div>This is a marathon, like Mando. One zone a week is great — the jetpack or the helmet alone is a satisfying win if you need a break from the full suit.</div><h3>The 90-Minute Rule</h3><p>Full armour + jetpack + helmet is heavy and hot, and the visor limits your view. Do a 90-minute test wear at home — find the problems before the con. On the day: take helmet breaks, drink water, and have a buddy guide you in crowds and on stairs. Never drive in the helmet.</p>"},{"num":"10","title":"Game Day","body":"<ul><li>Visor clear, jetpack secure.</li><li>Repair kit + green/silver touch-up.</li><li>No disintegrations.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;As you wish.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; two words, zero emotion, slight nod</i></li><li>&ldquo;What if he doesn't survive? He's worth a lot to me.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; gravelly, arms crossed</i></li><li>&ldquo;I'm a simple man making his way through the galaxy. Like my father before me.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; slow — let the callback land</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>As you wish. But I'm not sharing my fries.</li><li>This armor survived a Sarlacc pit. It can survive recess.</li><li>Jabba ruled with fear. I rule the playground with juice boxes.</li></ul></div><p>Half the magic of a costume is what you say when someone walks up. Golden rule — read the room: villains are the best part of a photo, but a looming hunter can scare a 4-year-old. If a little one looks unsure, drop the scary instantly and go kind:</p><ul><li>\"A bounty hunter never misses — a high-five! Got it!\"</li><li>\"Want to see the jetpack? Whoosh — straight up!\"</li><li>\"Even Boba Fett says: you're a tough little hunter.\"</li></ul><p>Universal tips: kneel to their eye level, never break character to correct them, ask their name and make them the hero — and keep any prop weapon lowered and pointed away.</p>"}],"files":[{"name":"Boba Fett helmet STL","designer":"Cults3D / Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=boba+fett+helmet"},{"name":"Boba armour set STL","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=boba%20fett%20armor"},{"name":"Boba jetpack STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=boba+fett+jetpack"},{"name":"Mando Mercs club","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Dented helmet","detail":"+ rangefinder, kill stripes."},{"name":"Chest display plate","detail":"Coloured panels."},{"name":"Shoulder bells (×2)","detail":"Bantha-skull symbol."},{"name":"Gauntlets (×2)","detail":"Green ESB / red ROTJ."},{"name":"Jetpack","detail":"Its own build — iconic."},{"name":"Shins + knees","detail":"Both legs."}],"buy":[{"name":"Flak vest","detail":"Plates mount on it."},{"name":"Cape","detail":"Brown ESB / green ROTJ."},{"name":"Ammo belt + pouches","detail":"Leather + holster."},{"name":"Boots + gloves","detail":"Grey/tan."},{"name":"Green paint + silver + clear coat","detail":"Plus weathering."},{"name":"EE-3 blaster","detail":"Boba's carbine."}]}},"obiwan":{"meta":{"word":"OBI-WAN","accent":"#b8915a","body":"jedi","budget":110,"btn":"⚔ JEDI","dur":"4 weeks","hrs":"10–20 hrs","parts":"Cloth + saber","budgetRange":"€60–250+","lead":"The Negotiator, three looks: Attack of the Clones, Revenge of the Sith & Clone Wars (with armour). Classic Jedi robes and a blue blade.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The V-neck vest colour tells the era — white for AOTC, dark brown for ROTS. And the beard is mandatory.","intro":"OPERATION OBI-WAN","introSub":"JEDI ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE BEN","footer":"OPERATION OBI-WAN · JEDI BUILD MANUAL · HELLO THERE · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 9 TOTAL","pubPdf":"obiwan_public.pdf","weekPdf":"obiwan_byweek.pdf","quote":"Hello there."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Beard & Hair","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Style","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The neat full beard is THE Obi-Wan signature. Longer hair for AOTC, shorter for ROTS/CW. A costume beard if you can't grow one.","tip":"No beard, no Obi-Wan.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Outer Tunic","type":"TORSO · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Tan/brown Jedi tunic that crosses over in a V at the neck.","tip":"Linen-look fabric, not shiny.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Clone Armour (CW only)","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":25,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Clone Wars look only: a clone chest plate + the Jedi-symbol shoulder over the tunic. AOTC/ROTS skip this.","tip":"Switch to the Clone Wars look to use this.","files":[{"name":"Jedi Order symbol STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=jedi+order+symbol"}]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Vest + Tabards","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":25,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The vest under the tunic (WHITE for AOTC, DARK BROWN for ROTS) plus the long tabard panels.","tip":"The V-neck vest colour marks the era.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Leather Belt","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Brown leather belt with pouches.","tip":"Same colour family as the boots.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Obi / Sash","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide cloth sash holding the tunic closed.","tip":"Belt goes over it.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Jedi Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":45,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The big brown hooded cloak.","tip":"Hem ~5cm off the floor.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Obi-Wan is a hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion Obi-Wan CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"White (AOTC) or khaki (ROTS) trousers.","tip":"Tuck into the boots.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Brown tall boots.","tip":"Jedi boots.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Vambraces (CW only)","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print","hours":3,"cost":12,"priority":"LOW","description":"Clone Wars only: forearm vambraces the tunic sleeves tuck into.","tip":"The sleeve-tuck is the CW signature.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blue Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":60,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Obi-Wan's blade is BLUE, with a silver ridged hilt.","tip":"Blue, not red. Set any saber to blue.","files":[{"name":"Obi-Wan saber STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=obi-wan+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Plan + order robes, beard, saber"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"First fit + hem; get the V-neck vest colour right"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Saber to blue; (CW) paint clone armour + tuck sleeves"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Obi-Wan Kenobi</span> three ways: AOTC, ROTS, and Clone Wars (with armour).</p><p>All share the robe base, blue blade, and the beard.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>AOTC</b> — white vest, longer hair.</li><li><b>ROTS</b> — dark brown vest, shorter hair.</li><li><b>Clone Wars</b> — robes + clone armour.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">UPGRADE PATH</div><p>First Obi-Wan? Build the Revenge of the Sith look — the most iconic, all cloth, no printing. Swap the dark vest for white → Attack of the Clones. Add clone armor + the Jedi-symbol shoulder → Clone Wars. Same tunic, belt, boots, blade and beard the whole way.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"Robes & Tunic","body":"<p class='lead'>The classic Jedi silhouette.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ V-NECK = ERA</div>White vest = AOTC, dark brown = ROTS.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">LAYER ORDER (SKIN → OUT)</div><ul><li>Under-tunic + vest (white AOTC / dark brown ROTS)</li><li>Tan outer tunic — wraps in a V at the neck</li><li>Tabards front &amp; back, tucked under the obi and belt</li><li>Obi / sash, then the belt with pouches over it</li><li>Brown hooded robe on top — hem it ~5 cm off the floor</li></ul><p>Tan linen-look fabric reads \"Jedi\"; shiny costume satin reads \"cheap.\" Keep it matte.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"Clone Armour (CW)","body":"<p class='lead'>Clone Wars only.</p><p>A clone chest + shoulder plate + vambraces over the tunic, with the Jedi symbol on one shoulder. Tuck the sleeves into the vambraces.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Lightsaber","body":"<p class='lead'>Blue, silver ridged hilt.</p><p>Buy a blue saber or set one you own to blue.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"The Beard","body":"<p class='lead'>The single most important detail.</p><p>Grow it or buy a costume beard matched to your hair.</p><h3>The Hair &amp; the \"Hello There\" Energy</h3><p>AOTC: longer, swept back (the famous \"mullet\"). ROTS &amp; Clone Wars: shorter and neater — a wig nails any of them. And in photos, Obi-Wan is calm and witty, never angry like a Sith: blue blade lit, a relaxed but ready stance, maybe one eyebrow raised.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Beard is everything.</li><li>V-neck colour = era.</li><li>Blue, not red.</li></ul><p class='accent'>Hello there.</p>"},{"num":"08","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Soresu</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ FORM III · SORESU — “The Way of the Mynock”</div><p>Pure defense — tight guard, minimal movement, let the opponent tire themselves out. Soresu answers every strike with the shortest possible parry and offers no opening until the other side makes the first mistake. The Negotiator fights the way he talks — patient, economical, and perfectly happy to let you wear yourself out on his guard.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#3a86f0\">⬤</span> Blue — silver ridged hilt; blue in every era</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Circle drill: hold a tight centre guard and deflect an imaginary bolt to each quarter — high left, high right, low left, low right — moving the blade the shortest distance possible each time.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;It's over, Anakin! I have the high ground!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; shout it from anywhere slightly elevated — a stair will do</i></li><li>&ldquo;The Force will be with you, always.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; warm and calm — the goodbye line</i></li><li>&ldquo;If you strike me down, I shall become more powerful than you can possibly imagine.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; serene, no fear — then slowly lower your saber</i></li><li>&ldquo;So uncivilized.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; dry as Tatooine, said while holstering something</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>It's over, recess! I have the high ground — on top of the climbing frame.</li><li>You were the chosen one! You were supposed to SHARE the cookies, not eat them all!</li><li>A juice box? So uncivilized.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Obi-Wan saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=obi-wan+lightsaber"},{"name":"Jedi Order symbol STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=jedi+order+symbol"},{"name":"Full Obi-Wan costume","designer":"AliExpress / eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Obi-Wan+Kenobi+costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion standards","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Or buy a blue neopixel."},{"name":"Clone armour (CW only)","detail":"Chest + shoulder + vambraces."},{"name":"Jedi Order symbol","detail":"For the CW shoulder."}],"buy":[{"name":"Tan tunic + tabards","detail":"V-neck robe."},{"name":"Vest","detail":"White AOTC / brown ROTS."},{"name":"Obi + leather belt","detail":"Holds it closed."},{"name":"Trousers + brown boots","detail":"White/khaki trousers."},{"name":"Brown hooded robe","detail":"Hemmed off the floor."},{"name":"Beard","detail":"Grow or costume beard."},{"name":"Blue lightsaber","detail":"Set to blue."}]}},"ahsoka":{"meta":{"word":"AHSOKA","accent":"#e0833a","body":"jedi","budget":110,"btn":"⚔ JEDI","dur":"5 weeks","hrs":"20–40 hrs","parts":"Craft + paint","budgetRange":"€60–200","lead":"Snips, three looks: Clone Wars, Rebels & live-action. The montrals & lekku headpiece and dual sabers are the build.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"Build the montrals & lekku headpiece first — it IS Ahsoka, and it's the hardest part.","intro":"OPERATION AHSOKA","introSub":"JEDI ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE SNIPS","footer":"OPERATION AHSOKA · BUILD MANUAL · I AM NO JEDI · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"ahsoka_public.pdf","weekPdf":"ahsoka_byweek.pdf","quote":"I am no Jedi."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Montrals & Lekku","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Craft","hours":10,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The striped horns + three head-tails on a skullcap base — foam or fabric, painted blue & white. The key part of the whole build.","tip":"Keep it light foam, anchor it well, copy the stripe pattern.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Face Paint & Markings","type":"HEAD · 02","kind":"Makeup","hours":3,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Orange skin base + white facial markings (skin-safe paint).","tip":"Patch-test the paint a day before.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Plate (Rebels/LA)","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Rebels & live-action add a chest plate + leather pads. Clone Wars skips it.","tip":"Switch to a later look to use this.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Outfit","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Maroon top (Clone Wars) / grey + leather (Rebels) / grey robes (live-action).","tip":"Match the outfit to your chosen era.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Saber Hooks","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Belt with hooks for the two sabers.","tip":"Two hooks — she carries two blades.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Skirt / Pads","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The skirt panels / leg pads (more leather in Rebels).","tip":"Varies by era.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"No Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"No cape (a hood in live-action only).","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards.","tip":"Ahsoka is a hero.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion Ahsoka CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Leggings + Boots Tops","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":20,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Grey leggings; armoured boot tops in later looks.","tip":"Grey base.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tall boots.","tip":"Match the era.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Vambraces (Rebels/LA)","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print","hours":3,"cost":12,"priority":"LOW","description":"Forearm vambraces in the later looks.","tip":"Clone Wars uses light arm guards instead.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Dual Sabers","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":90,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Two curved hilts — one full, one shorter 'shoto'. Green (early Clone Wars) or blue (later Clone Wars); white (Rebels and live-action).","tip":"Don't forget the shorter shoto.","files":[{"name":"Ahsoka saber STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ahsoka+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 1","task":"Plan + order outfit, sabers, paint, headpiece materials"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Build the montrals & lekku headpiece"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Finish stripes + practice the face paint"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Outfit, vambraces, sabers"},{"label":"Week 5","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Ahsoka Tano</span> three ways: Clone Wars, Rebels, live-action.</p><p>Every Ahsoka shares the orange skin, the striped headpiece, and dual sabers.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>Clone Wars</b> — maroon, green/yellow-green sabers.</li><li><b>Rebels</b> — grey + leather, white sabers.</li><li><b>Live-action</b> — grey robes, white sabers.</li></ul><h3>The Outfits, Up Close</h3><ul><li><b>Clone Wars</b> — maroon tube-style top with a diamond pattern on the front, grey leggings, a belt with two saber hooks, light arm guards, tall boots.</li><li><b>Rebels</b> — grey and dark with more leather: chest plate, arm bracers, leather pads on the skirt, armored boots. The \"older, battle-hardened\" look.</li><li><b>Live-action</b> — grey hooded robes over a tunic, forearm vambraces, a head brace across the montrals. The most covered-up, practical look.</li></ul>"},{"num":"03","title":"Montrals & Lekku","body":"<p class='lead'>The key part.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ KEEP IT LIGHT</div>Foam, not solid. Anchor the headpiece well and copy the stripe pattern.</div><h3>How People Make Them</h3><p><b>Foam</b> — carved foam covered in fabric, painted stripes; light and comfy, the most popular. <b>Fabric + stuffing</b> — sewn tubes stuffed soft; easiest to sew. <b>3D-printed base</b> — a printed montral cap with soft fabric lekku; most accurate shape. Build it onto a skullcap or headband so it sits securely and comes off: the front lekku drape over your shoulders, the back one hangs down your back — longer for Rebels, shorter for live-action.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"Orange Skin & Markings","body":"<p class='lead'>Skin-safe orange base + white markings.</p><p>Patch-test a day before; never use craft paint on skin.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">COVERING THE REST</div><p>For hands and arms, either paint them orange or wear orange gloves/sleeves. Long sleeves + gloves are the easy way to avoid painting everything.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Dual Sabers","body":"<p class='lead'>Two curved hilts — one shorter shoto.</p><p>Green+yellow-green (CW), white (Rebels and live-action).</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Headpiece first, and light.</li><li>Skin-safe paint only.</li><li>Don't forget the shoto.</li></ul><p class='accent'>I am no Jedi.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Shien (reverse grip) + JarKai dual</span>, wielded dual JarKai.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ FORM V · SHIEN (REVERSE GRIP) + JARKAI DUAL — “The Way of the Krayt Dragon”</div><p>Two blades, reverse grip, always moving — she defends by attacking from angles nobody thinks to guard. The shoto covers whatever the main blade abandons, so the pair works like one weapon with two ends. The back-handed grip and the second blade are pure Ahsoka — unorthodox, improvised-looking, and impossible to pin down, just like her path out of the Order.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#f0f4f8\">⬤</span> White — full-length main blade, curved hilt</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#f0f4f8\">⬤</span> White — shoto short blade, curved hilt</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">dual JarKai</span></div></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ MORE THAN ONE BLADE — THE CRAFT</div><ul><li>Lead with the full-length blade; the shoto stays back as the guard hand — it blocks, it does not chase.</li><li>Reverse grip shortens your reach — step in closer than feels natural and cut outward, never across your own arm.</li><li>Two blades means double the arc: check a full arm-span on both sides before any swing, and never spin near people.</li><li>Train each hand solo until it is clean before you ever pair them.</li></ul></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Main blade in reverse grip, shoto held forward: walk a slow square, cutting outward at each corner turn so the blades never cross your own body. Speed is only allowed after ten clean laps.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I am Ahsoka Tano, Padawan learner to Anakin Skywalker.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; chin up, proud — the introduction</i></li><li>&ldquo;I'm sorry, Master, but I'm not coming back.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; quiet and steady — the walking-away line</i></li><li>&ldquo;I won't leave you. Not this time.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; soft but absolutely certain</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I carry two lightsabers because one hand is always holding snacks.</li><li>I am no Jedi. I'm the line leader.</li><li>My master crashed every ship he ever flew. I take the bus.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Ahsoka saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ahsoka+lightsaber"},{"name":"Montral / Togruta headpiece STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ahsoka+montral"},{"name":"Full Ahsoka costume","designer":"AliExpress / eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Ahsoka+Tano+costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion standards","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Montral base (optional)","detail":"Build foam/fabric onto it."},{"name":"Dual saber hilts","detail":"Main + shoto."},{"name":"Vambraces (Rebels/LA)","detail":"Forearm armour."},{"name":"Chest plate (Rebels/LA)","detail":"Later looks only."}],"buy":[{"name":"Outfit","detail":"Maroon CW / grey Rebels / robes LA."},{"name":"Headpiece materials","detail":"Foam, fabric, skullcap."},{"name":"Skin-safe orange + white paint","detail":"Patch-test first."},{"name":"Belt with two saber hooks","detail":"She carries two."},{"name":"Leggings + tall boots","detail":"Grey base."},{"name":"Two lightsabers","detail":"Right colour for the era."}]}},"maul":{"meta":{"word":"MAUL","accent":"#c0392b","body":"jedi","budget":120,"btn":"⚔ SITH","dur":"5 weeks","hrs":"20–40 hrs","parts":"Makeup + robes","budgetRange":"€60–200","lead":"The Sith apprentice, three looks: Phantom Menace, Clone Wars robot legs & grey old Rebels Maul. The red & black face and horn crown carry all three — the saber goes from full staff to broken half to rebuilt hilt.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"Maul IS his face — practice the red & black tattoo pattern until it's clean and symmetrical.","intro":"OPERATION MAUL","introSub":"SITH ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE MAUL","footer":"OPERATION MAUL · BUILD MANUAL · AT LAST WE WILL HAVE REVENGE · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"maul_public.pdf","weekPdf":"maul_byweek.pdf","quote":"At last we will have revenge."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Horn Crown","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Craft + Print","hours":6,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The ring of small horns on a bald cap. Foam, clay, or printed; blended in and painted.","tip":"Mark even spacing before gluing.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Face Paint","type":"HEAD · 02","kind":"Makeup","hours":4,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Red base + the black tattoo pattern (skin-safe paint). The showpiece.","tip":"Sketch lightly, then fill with a thin brush. Patch-test first.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Maul is robes, not armour.","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Layered Black Tunics","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Under-tunic + middle tunic + a shawl tabard — the dark mirror of a Jedi's robes.","tip":"Matte black, never shiny.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt / Sash","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Black belt/sash at the waist.","tip":"Black on black.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Lower Robes","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The hanging lower robe panels.","tip":"Adds the layered look.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Hooded Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":45,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The big black hooded cloak — hood up for the reveal.","tip":"Deep hood for the dramatic face reveal.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the 501st standards — Maul is a villain.","tip":"501st = bad guys.","files":[{"name":"501st Maul CRL","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Black trousers + boots (Phantom Menace).","tip":"Plain black.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Robot Legs (CW, expert)","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"3D Print","hours":12,"cost":40,"priority":"LOW","description":"Clone Wars only: mechanical legs. EXPERT and potentially dangerous — shells over your own legs are safest; never walk on stilts without training + an adult.","tip":"Phantom Menace skips this entirely.","files":[{"name":"Maul robot legs STL","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=darth%20maul%20legs"}]},"gloves":{"name":"Hands","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Makeup/Buy","hours":1,"cost":8,"priority":"LOW","description":"Red-painted or red-sleeved hands/arms to match the face.","tip":"Long sleeves are the easy option.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Double Saber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":80,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The saberstaff — a red blade from each end.","tip":"Mind its length in crowds.","files":[{"name":"Maul saber staff STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=darth+maul+lightsaber+staff"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 1","task":"Plan + order robes, double saber, bald cap, face paint"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Build the horn crown"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Practice the face pattern"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Robes + saber to red (both ends)"},{"label":"Week 5","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Darth Maul</span> two ways: Phantom Menace & Clone Wars robot legs.</p><p>The face, horns, and double saber are the real build.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<p class=\"lead\">One Sith, three eras — pick your Maul before you build. The horns and the red-black skin stay; the rest changes.</p><h3>The Phantom Menace — The Sith Apprentice</h3><p>Layered black Sith robes — a hooded outer robe over a tabard-and-sash tunic — with the full 10-horn crown and your own two legs. The wardrobe is forgiving black fabric; the hours go into the face and horns. <b>Saber:</b> The full double-bladed staff — one long hilt, a red blade from each end. <i>(Moderate — the makeup is the whole fight.)</i></p><h3>The Clone Wars — The Return</h3><p>Bare chest painted in the full red &amp; black pattern (or dark armoured robes if you'd rather not paint a torso), with mechanical legs below the waist. The show gives him spider legs first, then humanoid ones — build the humanoid pair from black trousers plus foam plates and silver piston detail, and leave the spider rig as a photo prop. <b>Saber:</b> The broken half of his old staff, wielded as a battered single blade. <i>(Expert — torso paint plus a leg rig.)</i></p><h3>Rebels — Old Master</h3><p>Aged Maul: the red skin dulled and streaked with grey, a shorter weathered horn crown with a few broken tips, and dark hooded robes over the mechanical legs. The hood hides most of the horns, and grey stipple over your red base does the ageing for you. <b>Saber:</b> Rebuilt from the wreckage into what looks like a plain single hilt — he hides it inside his walking stick, but it can still snap out a second blade. <i>(Moderate — easiest wardrobe, trickiest ageing.)</i></p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ PICK BEFORE YOU BUY</div><p>The three looks share the makeup and horn crown but almost nothing else — choose your era first so you only buy one wardrobe.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Face","body":"<p class='lead'>Red base + black tattoo pattern.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ SAFETY</div>Skin-safe paint only; patch-test a day before.</div><h3>Practice First</h3><p>The pattern is specific and symmetrical — do a full test run a week before, take photos, and adjust. Sketch the pattern lightly first, then fill it in with a thin brush for the black lines. A touch of black on the lips finishes the menacing grin.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Horns","body":"<p class='lead'>A crown of small horns on a bald cap.</p><p>Blend the bases so they look grown-in, then paint over them.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">COUNT &amp; SPACING</div><p>Check a reference photo and mark the horn positions on the bald cap before gluing, so the crown comes out even and symmetrical — then paint the whole thing as one surface so the tattoos flow over it.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"Double Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>Red blades from both ends.</p><p>A neopixel staff is the showpiece; mind its length in crowds.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Robot Legs (expert)","body":"<div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ IMPORTANT</div>Real stilts are dangerous. Shells over your own legs, or just do Phantom Menace. Adult help required.</div>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Juyo</span>, wielded double-bladed staff.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ FORM VII · JUYO — “The Way of the Vornskr”</div><p>Ferocity under total body control — Juyo channels rage into a relentless, acrobatic assault. The staff never stops moving; every spin is already setting up the next strike from an angle you didn't guard. The double-bladed staff exists to feed Juyo's appetite — twice the blades, zero pauses, pure predator.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#d42b2b\">⬤</span> Red — double-bladed staff — one red blade from each end of the saberstaff</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">double-bladed staff</span></div></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ MORE THAN ONE BLADE — THE CRAFT</div><ul><li>A staff needs full 360-degree clearance — check the whole circle around you before any spin, and never spin near people.</li><li>Treat one end as the lead blade and the other as the answer: strike with the front, guard with the back.</li><li>Keep the hilt at your centre — the staff moves around you, not you around the staff.</li><li>Build every move at half speed first; a saberstaff finds your own shins long before it looks cool.</li></ul></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Figure-eight flow: with full clearance, trace slow figure-eights alternating ends of the staff, both hands working and feet planted — only add footwork once the pattern is smooth.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;At last we will reveal ourselves to the Jedi.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; low whisper — long pause before 'Jedi'</i></li><li>&ldquo;He will avenge us.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; barely a breath — the very last line</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>At last... we will have recess.</li><li>My lightsaber has two ends because my homework is double-sided.</li><li>I have waited YEARS for my revenge... and for the bathroom pass.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Maul saber staff STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=darth+maul+lightsaber+staff"},{"name":"Maul horns STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=darth+maul+horns"},{"name":"Full Maul costume","designer":"AliExpress / eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Darth+Maul+costume"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Horn crown","detail":"On a bald cap, blended."},{"name":"Double saber hilt","detail":"Or buy a staff neopixel."},{"name":"Robot legs (CW, expert)","detail":"Shells over your own legs."}],"buy":[{"name":"Layered black tunics","detail":"Matte, never shiny."},{"name":"Bald cap","detail":"For the horns + tattoos."},{"name":"Skin-safe red + black paint","detail":"Patch-test first."},{"name":"Hooded black robe","detail":"Deep hood for the reveal."},{"name":"Black trousers + boots","detail":"Plain black."},{"name":"Red double saber","detail":"Both ends."}]}},"rey":{"meta":{"word":"REY","accent":"#c2a878","body":"jedi","budget":100,"btn":"⚔ JEDI","dur":"4 weeks","hrs":"8–18 hrs","parts":"Cloth + wraps","budgetRange":"€55–200","lead":"Scavenger to Jedi, three looks: Force Awakens, Last Jedi & the white Rise of Skywalker. Wraps, three buns, a staff or saber.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The three-bun hair is the one detail everyone knows — if you nail one thing, nail the hair.","intro":"OPERATION REY","introSub":"JEDI ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE BB-8","footer":"OPERATION REY · JEDI BUILD MANUAL · REY... JUST REY · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"rey_public.pdf","weekPdf":"rey_byweek.pdf","quote":"The garbage will do."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Three-Bun Hair","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Style","hours":2,"cost":20,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Rey's signature three stacked buns — your own hair or a wig.","tip":"If you nail one thing, nail the hair.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Wrap Top","type":"TORSO · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The crossed wrap top — taupe (TFA), darker (TLJ), or white (TROS).","tip":"Soft matte fabric, layered.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Rey is cloth + wraps.","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Base Layer","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"A fitted base layer under the wrap top.","tip":"Tank or long-sleeve.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Fabric Belt + Pouch","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide cloth belt with a pouch.","tip":"Scavenger style.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Arm & Hand Wraps","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Long cloth strips wound around the forearms, wrists and hands — one continuous wrap set. The signature.","tip":"Wind firmly, pin the ends. This single set covers arms and hands; leg wraps live with the trousers.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Hood / Cowl (TROS)","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":20,"priority":"LOW","description":"A hood for the white Rise of Skywalker look.","tip":"TROS only.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Rey is a hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion Rey CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers + Leg Wraps","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Baggy trousers with leg wraps near the boots.","tip":"Match the era's colour.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Brown lace-up boots.","tip":"Worn leather.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Hand Wraps","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":8,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Wrapped hands/wrists matching the arm wraps.","tip":"Part of the wrap set.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Staff / Saber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":55,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Quarterstaff (TFA), blue saber (TLJ), or her yellow saber (TROS, built from her staff).","tip":"Weapon tells the era; yellow is rare and striking.","files":[{"name":"Rey saber STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=rey+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Plan + order wrap top, wraps, weapon"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"First fit; practice winding the wraps"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Three-bun hair + weapon (staff or saber)"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Rey</span> three ways: Force Awakens scavenger, Last Jedi training, and the white Rise of Skywalker.</p><p>A cloth-and-wraps build with the three-bun hair.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>Scavenger (TFA)</b> — taupe + quarterstaff.</li><li><b>Training (TLJ)</b> — darker + blue saber.</li><li><b>White Jedi (TROS)</b> — all white + yellow saber.</li></ul>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Outfit & Wraps","body":"<p class='lead'>Layered, matte, lived-in.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ WIND FIRMLY</div>Pin the wrap ends so they don't unravel all day.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">LAYER ORDER (SKIN → OUT)</div><ul><li>Fitted base layer (tank / long-sleeve)</li><li>The wrap top — crosses over and ties (taupe / dark / white)</li><li>Arm wraps from wrist toward elbow; hand wraps</li><li>Fabric belt with a pouch at the waist</li><li>Baggy trousers, leg wraps near the boots</li><li>Hood / cowl on top (TROS)</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Three-Bun Hair","body":"<p class='lead'>The one detail everyone knows.</p><p>Three stacked buns down the back; a wig if your hair's short.</p><h3>How To Do It</h3><p>Part the hair into three sections down the back of the head, twist each into a small bun stacked top to bottom, and pin each with bobby pins — let a little hair fall loose for the lived-in look. In the story, she wore three buns so her long-lost parents could spot her.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"Staff & Sabers","body":"<p class='lead'>Weapon tells the era.</p><p>Quarterstaff (TFA), blue (TLJ), or the rare yellow saber (TROS).</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE STAFF FROM A DOWEL</div><p>Rey's quarterstaff is basically a long wooden pole (about your height) wrapped with leather/cloth strips and a few \"scavenged\" metal bits. A hardwood dowel + wraps + small bolted greebles makes a cheap, sturdy one. Mind its length in crowds.</p></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Nail the hair.</li><li>Wind the wraps firmly.</li><li>White (TROS) shows dirt — pack a stain pen.</li></ul><p class='accent'>Rey. Just Rey.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Self-taught</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · SELF-TAUGHT</div><p>Staff-fighter instincts with a saber in hand — she jabs, sweeps and spins like the quarterstaff never left her grip. Reads closest to Form V Djem So: hard counters and forward pressure, learned by surviving Jakku rather than studying in a temple. Years defending herself with a staff shaped every swing before she ever ignited a blade — her saber work is scavenger grit polished into Jedi discipline.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#3d85e0\">⬤</span> Blue — Anakin's blue lineage saber (TFA/TLJ) — carried, not built</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#e8c33a\">⬤</span> Yellow — her own blade (TROS) — hilt built from a section of her quarterstaff</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Staff-to-saber switch: run one slow quarterstaff sweep, then repeat the exact same motion one-handed with the saber — feel where the shorter weapon changes the arc, and keep 360-degree clearance for the staff half.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Rey. Rey Skywalker.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; the ending line — say it with a wink; half the fandom will cheer and the other half will gasp</i></li><li>&ldquo;You will remove these restraints and leave this cell with the door open.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; calm mind-trick voice — third try's the charm</i></li><li>&ldquo;I'm no one.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; small voice, big moment</i></li><li>&ldquo;I didn't know there was this much green in the whole galaxy.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; wide-eyed wonder, look around slowly</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>You will share those crayons. You WILL share those crayons.</li><li>I fixed the Millennium Falcon. Your jammed pencil sharpener doesn't scare me.</li><li>I lifted rocks with my mind. Your backpack is nothing.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Rey saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=rey+lightsaber"},{"name":"Rey staff parts STL","designer":"Printables","url":"https://www.printables.com/search/models?q=rey%20staff"},{"name":"Full Rey costume","designer":"AliExpress / eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Rey+Star+Wars+costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion standards","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Rey TROS staff-built hilt."},{"name":"Staff greebles (optional)","detail":"Scavenged metal bits."}],"buy":[{"name":"Wrap top","detail":"Taupe / dark / white."},{"name":"Arm + hand wraps","detail":"Wound firmly, pinned."},{"name":"Fabric belt + pouch","detail":"Scavenger style."},{"name":"Trousers + lace-up boots","detail":"Baggy, brown boots."},{"name":"Three-bun wig (optional)","detail":"If hair is short."},{"name":"Quarterstaff or saber","detail":"Tells the era."}]}},"han":{"meta":{"word":"HAN","accent":"#a08060","body":"han","budget":140,"btn":"⚔ SMUGGLER","dur":"3 weeks","hrs":"6–12 hrs","parts":"Cloth + blaster","budgetRange":"€50–180","lead":"The smuggler captain, three looks: A New Hope, Empire Strikes Back, and the Hoth winter parka. A fast, approachable cloth build with the iconic DL-44 blaster.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The pants-with-the-stripe + the vest + the holster = instantly Han. Get those three right.","intro":"OPERATION HAN","introSub":"FALCON ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE FALCON","footer":"OPERATION HAN · BUILD MANUAL · NEVER TELL ME THE ODDS · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"han_public.pdf","weekPdf":"han_byweek.pdf","quote":"Never tell me the odds."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Hair","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Style","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Han's tousled brown hair — a wig if yours isn't there.","tip":"Slightly messy reads as Han.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Vest","type":"TORSO · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Black vest (ANH/ESB) or the dark blue/brown Falcon jacket variant. The signature layer.","tip":"Black for ANH, similar cut for ESB.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Han is cloth, not armour.","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Shirt","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Cream / off-white long-sleeve shirt under the vest. V-neck, slightly open collar.","tip":"The shirt under the vest is the base.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Holster","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":28,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Brown leather belt with the DL-44 holster on the right hip. Real Han energy.","tip":"3-hole-belt with 2 prongs is the screen-accurate detail.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Belt Tools","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"LOW","description":"Tiny belt cylinders + droid caller — small details that sell it.","tip":"Print the droid caller; it's a fun greeble.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Hoth Parka","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":55,"priority":"LOW","description":"Hoth only: dark brown winter parka with fur trim.","tip":"Skip for ANH/ESB.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Han is a hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion Han CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Striped Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":28,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Navy blue with a red stripe (ANH) or brown with a yellow stripe (ESB). The stripe is what makes them Han trousers.","tip":"Run a sewn ribbon down the seam if you can't find them.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tall black knee-high boots (ANH) or worn mukluk-style for Hoth.","tip":"Riding/captain boots.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"No Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Han goes bare-handed (gloves for Hoth only).","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"DL-44 Blaster","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Han's heavy blaster pistol — the long-barrelled DL-44. Carry it in the right-hip holster.","tip":"A toy blaster + black paint + weathering looks great.","files":[{"name":"DL-44 blaster STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=dl-44+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 3","task":"Plan + order vest, shirt, striped trousers, boots, holster, blaster"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Fit & hem; sew the stripe on trousers if needed; build the holster rig"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Belt tools + droid caller; weather the blaster"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Han Solo</span> three ways — A New Hope, Empire Strikes Back, and the Hoth parka.</p><p>Fast cloth build with the famous DL-44 blaster.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">GREAT FOR A GROUP</div><p>Han pairs perfectly with a Leia, a Luke, a Chewbacca, or a Lando. Building with friends? This is a natural anchor for an original-trilogy crew.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>ANH</b> — black vest, navy trousers with a red stripe.</li><li><b>ESB</b> — dark Falcon jacket, brown trousers with a yellow stripe.</li><li><b>Hoth</b> — add the brown winter parka and mukluk boots.</li></ul>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Vest & Shirt","body":"<p class='lead'>Layered right, even cheap pieces read as Han.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ V-NECK SHIRT</div>Cream/off-white V-neck under a fitted vest — don't button it tight.</div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Striped Trousers","body":"<p class='lead'>The stripe is the signature.</p><p>ANH: navy + red. ESB: brown + yellow. Can't find them? Sew or fabric-tape a ribbon down the side seam.</p><h3>Why \"Bloodstripes\"?</h3><p>That single coloured stripe down the outside of each leg is Han's Corellian bloodstripe — an award for bravery. It's a tiny detail that screams \"Han Solo,\" and almost everyone forgets it.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The DL-44 & Holster","body":"<p class='lead'>The blaster lives on the right hip.</p><p>A weathered toy blaster looks great. The holster is a leather drop-rig.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Pants stripe + vest + holster = Han.</li><li>Never tell me the odds.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE SWAGGER — HOW TO STAND LIKE HAN</div><ul><li>Weight on one leg, hand resting near the blaster.</li><li>A slow, lopsided half-smile — like you know something funny nobody else does. Practise it in a mirror; it's half the costume.</li><li>Chin up, shoulders easy — Han is never impressed and never worried (even when he should be).</li><li>If someone quotes the odds at you, wave them off.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I know.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; cool as ice — the only correct answer to 'I love you'</i></li><li>&ldquo;Chewie, we're home.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; soft smile, look around slowly</i></li><li>&ldquo;Laugh it up, fuzzball.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; smirk at your nearest Wookiee</i></li><li>&ldquo;Great, kid! Don't get cocky.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; grinning, tossed over the shoulder</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>Never tell me the odds of my homework being done.</li><li>I made the Kessel Run in less than twelve parsecs. The school run? Ten minutes, easy.</li><li>Mom says she loves me. I say, 'I know.'</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"DL-44 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=dl-44+blaster"},{"name":"Falcon vest pattern","designer":"search Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=han+solo+vest+pattern"},{"name":"Full Han costume","designer":"AliExpress / eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Han+Solo+costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion standards","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"DL-44 blaster (optional)","detail":"Or buy + weather a toy blaster."},{"name":"Belt tools / droid caller","detail":"Small greebles for the belt."}],"buy":[{"name":"Cream/off-white V-neck shirt","detail":"Base layer."},{"name":"Black vest","detail":"ANH cut; dark jacket for ESB."},{"name":"Striped trousers","detail":"Navy+red (ANH) or brown+yellow (ESB)."},{"name":"Tall black boots","detail":"Knee-high captain boots."},{"name":"Brown leather belt + holster","detail":"Right hip."},{"name":"Hoth parka","detail":"Hoth look only."}]}},"leia":{"meta":{"word":"LEIA","accent":"#e8e3d5","body":"leia","budget":130,"btn":"⚔ REBEL","dur":"4 weeks","hrs":"10–20 hrs","parts":"Cloth + buns","budgetRange":"€55–200","lead":"The Princess, three looks: the classic A New Hope white gown, the Hoth snowsuit, and the Endor camo poncho. The two side buns are the icon.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The side buns ARE Princess Leia. If you nail one thing, nail the hair.","intro":"OPERATION LEIA","introSub":"REBEL ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE ORGANA","footer":"OPERATION LEIA · BUILD MANUAL · SOMEONE HAS TO SAVE OUR SKINS · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"leia_public.pdf","weekPdf":"leia_byweek.pdf","quote":"Help me, Obi-Wan Kenobi. You're my only hope."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Side Buns","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Style","hours":3,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The classic two side buns (ANH), a coiled braided crown (Hoth), or a single long braid (Endor). The icon.","tip":"If you nail one thing, nail the hair. A wig is fine.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"White Gown / Vest","type":"TORSO · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":55,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The flowing white ANH gown, the puffy-collared Hoth vest, or the Endor camo poncho.","tip":"Match the era. ANH white is the iconic one.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Leia is cloth, not armour.","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Base Layer","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"A simple white/cream base under the gown or vest.","tip":"Plain matte fabric.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Silver Disc Belt","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":1,"cost":25,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The ANH silver-disc belt over the gown.","tip":"A printable replica buckle is the screen-accurate detail.","files":[{"name":"Leia disc belt STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=princess+leia+belt"}]},"codpiece":{"name":"No Codpiece","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Not applicable.","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Hoth Vest / Endor Poncho","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":35,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Hoth: white puffy-collared vest over the jumpsuit. Endor: green camo poncho.","tip":"Swap by era.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Leia is a hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion Leia CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers / Skirt","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The gown reaches the floor (ANH). Hoth + Endor use white or khaki trousers.","tip":"ANH = no trousers showing.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"White slipper boots (ANH) or brown lace-up boots (Hoth/Endor).","tip":"ANH boots are barely visible under the gown.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"No Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Leia goes bare-handed.","tip":"Not used for this look.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blaster","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Leia carries the small Defender sporting blaster pistol, not a saber. She's a princess and a soldier.","tip":"A small holstered blaster sells the rebel look.","files":[{"name":"Leia blaster STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=leia+defender+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 4","task":"Plan + order gown/vest, belt, boots, wig (if needed)"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Fit + hem; sew the disc belt; practice the bun style"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Add the era extras (Hoth vest or Endor poncho)"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Princess Leia</span> three ways: ANH white gown, Hoth snowsuit, Endor camo.</p><p>All cloth. The hair is the showpiece.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">SHE'S A LEADER, NOT A PRIZE</div><p>Leia is a princess, a senator, a spy, a rebel leader, and later a general — iconic in every one of those roles. Build her as what she is: brave, sharp, in command. Play her with that confidence and the costume comes alive. Stand tall, chin level, shoulders back — Leia faced down Darth Vader without blinking.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>ANH</b> — white floor-length gown + the two side buns + silver disc belt.</li><li><b>Hoth</b> — white quilted jumpsuit + puffy-collared vest + braided crown.</li><li><b>Endor</b> — khaki + green poncho + single long braid.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">QUICK START</div><p>First Leia? The Senator look is the most iconic, but the side-bun hair takes practice. If you want easy-and-recognisable fast, the Endor look (poncho + single braid) is the simplest and still clearly Leia.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Buns","body":"<p class='lead'>The single most recognisable hairstyle in cinema.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ TWO BUNS</div>Two large buns over the ears for ANH. Roll, pin, and add a hairnet to hold them.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">SHORT HAIR? NO PROBLEM</div><p>Wigs are completely fair game and often look better in photos. A pre-styled Leia wig is one of the best small investments you can make for this build — it nails the buns instantly and saves an hour of pinning.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Gown","body":"<p class='lead'>Flowing white, floor-length, slightly hooded collar.</p><p>The silver disc belt sits on the hips. The white gown is matte — never shiny costume satin.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"Hoth & Endor","body":"<p class='lead'>Two era swaps from the same base.</p><p>Hoth = puffy-collared white vest + boots. Endor = green poncho over khakis.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Buns are everything.</li><li>Matte white fabric.</li><li>Carry a small blaster — she's a soldier.</li></ul><p class='accent'>Someone has to save our skins.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Aren't you a little short for a stormtrooper?&rdquo; <i>&mdash; deadpan — perfect whenever a trooper cosplayer walks by</i></li><li>&ldquo;Why, you stuck-up, half-witted, scruffy-looking nerf herder!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; rapid-fire, chin up, zero apology</i></li><li>&ldquo;Somebody has to save our skins. Into the garbage chute, flyboy!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; take charge — you're the one with the plan</i></li><li>&ldquo;The more you tighten your grip, Tarkin, the more star systems will slip through your fingers.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; cool and defiant, even when surrounded</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>Aren't you a little short for a fifth grader?</li><li>Help me, cafeteria crew. You're my only hope — I forgot my lunch.</li><li>I'm a princess AND a general. Yes, you have to call me both.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Leia disc belt STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=princess+leia+belt"},{"name":"Leia Defender blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=leia+defender+blaster"},{"name":"Full Leia costume","designer":"AliExpress / eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Princess+Leia+costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion standards","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Disc belt buckle (optional)","detail":"Or buy a replica."},{"name":"Defender blaster (optional)","detail":"Small holstered blaster."}],"buy":[{"name":"White floor-length gown","detail":"ANH matte white, slightly hooded collar."},{"name":"Hoth quilted jumpsuit + vest","detail":"For the Hoth look."},{"name":"Green poncho + khaki","detail":"For the Endor look."},{"name":"White slipper boots / brown lace-up","detail":"Match the era."},{"name":"Wig or hair clips for buns","detail":"Two side buns (ANH)."},{"name":"Silver disc belt","detail":"Sits on the hips."},{"name":"Hairnet + pins","detail":"Hold the buns."}]}},"grievous":{"meta":{"word":"GRIEVOUS","accent":"#9aa8a8","body":"grievous","budget":180,"btn":"⚔ SEPARATIST","dur":"6 weeks","hrs":"30–60 hrs","parts":"Print + robes + 2-4 sabers","budgetRange":"€100–300","lead":"The Separatist general, the lightsaber collector, the cyborg warrior. A challenging build with a printed head and a hint of extra arms.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"Don't try to walk on stilts. Suggest the height + extra arms with the costume, never with anything dangerous.","intro":"OPERATION GRIEVOUS","introSub":"SEPARATIST ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE GRIEV","footer":"OPERATION GRIEVOUS · BUILD MANUAL · GENERAL OF THE DROID ARMY · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 9 TOTAL","pubPdf":"grievous_public.pdf","weekPdf":"grievous_byweek.pdf","quote":"General Kenobi. You are a bold one."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Skull / Mask","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The bone-coloured cyborg head: long jaw, downturned mouth slits, yellow/green glowing eyes. Print, sand, prime, paint bone-grey, weather, then LED the eyes.","tip":"Eyes lit with tiny yellow LEDs read instantly as Grievous.","files":[{"name":"Grievous head STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=general+grievous+head"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Frame","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print + Foam","hours":4,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Skeletal shoulder plates over the cloak — sharp metallic spurs.","tip":"Foam-core + paint reads great in photos.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Ribcage Plate","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print + Foam","hours":8,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The exposed skeletal ribcage chest piece — the visual core.","tip":"Vacuum-formed plastic or layered foam, weathered dark grey + gold.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Heart Sac","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Craft","hours":2,"cost":10,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The bag/sac hanging in the centre of the ribcage. A pouch in dark grey.","tip":"Stuff a small pouch loosely — don't make it tight.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Saber Clips","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide dark belt with two saber clips. Two stolen sabers hanging is enough — don't try four.","tip":"Print clips that mount real-size hilts.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Hip Plates","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":4,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Bony hip flares either side of the belt.","tip":"Mirror one STL.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Tattered Cloak","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The dark hooded cloak. Cut and fray the hem; it hides the leg armour and adds menace.","tip":"Hood up for the entrance is iconic.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the 501st standards — Grievous is a villain.","tip":"501st = bad guys.","files":[{"name":"501st Grievous CRL","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Skeletal Shins","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print + Foam","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Thin armoured shin pieces in bone-grey. Hidden under the cloak in most photos.","tip":"Foam works if printing's too much.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Foot Talons","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":25,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Two-toed talon-style feet. Print toe caps over plain dark boots.","tip":"Toe caps over plain black boots is the kid-friendly trick.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Extra Arms","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Craft","hours":6,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The signature: two EXTRA prop arms hanging at your sides (built into the cloak), each holding a saber hilt.","tip":"Two extras is plenty. Four real moving arms is for adult experts only.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Stolen Sabers","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":4,"cost":90,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Two or four lightsabers — his collection from fallen Jedi. Different blade colours look great.","tip":"Two real sabers + two glued-in dummies on the extra arms is perfect.","files":[{"name":"Lightsaber hilt STLs","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=lightsaber+hilt"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Plan + order filament, cloak, two sabers, LED eyes"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Print head + ribcage + paint bone-grey"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Build the extra-arms rig + foam shoulders + hip plates"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Talon toe caps + LED eyes + weather everything"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>One of the <span class='accent'>hardest builds in the line</span> — a four-armed cyborg general.</p><p>The trick is to suggest his unusual shape with smart costume tricks rather than try to physically be 7 feet tall with four working arms.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE ONE RULE</div><p>The four arms and the hunched silhouette are Grievous. Even a simple version reads instantly if you get the two extra arms and the forward-hunched stance right — nail them and a rough build still stops the room. Nobody walks past a good Grievous.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Approach","body":"<ul><li><b>Static</b> — head + cloak + extra-arms rig (recommended).</li><li><b>Full skeletal</b> — add the ribcage and shin armour.</li><li><b>Puppet</b> — advanced builders use a shoulder harness with mechanical extras.</li></ul>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Head","body":"<p class='lead'>The bone-grey mask with yellow eyes is the showpiece.</p><p>Print, sand smooth, prime, paint bone-grey, weather with a brown wash, then add yellow LEDs behind the eye slits.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">YOU'LL SEE OUT THROUGH THE NECK / MOUTH</div><p>Plan your eye-line early. Most builders see out through a mesh panel at the mouth or neck. Test that you can walk safely before you finish painting.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Extra Arms","body":"<p class='lead'>Two hanging extra arms = instantly Grievous.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ HOW</div>PVC armatures in foam-padded sleeves with gloves at the ends holding dummy sabers. Mounted into the cloak shoulders.</div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Cloak","body":"<p class='lead'>Hides the legs and the rig joints.</p><p>Dark hooded cloak, frayed hem. Hood up for the entrance is the iconic image.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Sabers","body":"<p class='lead'>Two real + two dummy is plenty.</p><p>Mix blade colours — he stole them from Jedi.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Don't try to walk on stilts.</li><li>Hood up sells it.</li><li>Two hanging arms is enough.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE WALK &amp; THE COUGH</div><ul><li>Hunch forward — the signature silhouette. Elbows out, head low.</li><li>Move in sharp, mechanical bursts — he's a machine wearing a living heart.</li><li>The wheezing cough is weirdly iconic; a dry, rasping cough between lines is pure character.</li><li>Mind your width — four arms and a cape make you wider than usual. Watch doorways, crowds, and small kids.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Unorthodox (Dooku-trained)</span>, wielded quad.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · UNORTHODOX (DOOKU-TRAINED)</div><p>No Force, no single form — Count Dooku's personal drills executed at machine speed by arms that split from two into four. A whirling wall of stolen blades meant to overwhelm before the duel even starts; reads closest to Makashi precision multiplied past anything a human body could copy. Grievous fights like a collection — every move is a dead Jedi's technique replayed faster, without the Jedi.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#3d85dd\">⬤</span> Blue — stolen from a fallen Jedi</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#3d85dd\">⬤</span> Blue — stolen from a fallen Jedi</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#3fae5a\">⬤</span> Green — stolen from a fallen Jedi</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#3fae5a\">⬤</span> Green — stolen from a fallen Jedi</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">quad</span></div></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ MORE THAN ONE BLADE — THE CRAFT</div><ul><li>Carry two lit and two clipped — four live blades need arena-sized clearance no convention hall has.</li><li>Lead with the upper pair; the lower arms guard low and never chase.</li><li>Claim full 360-degree space (arm-span plus blade, all sides) before any windmill, and never spin near people.</li><li>Keep each blade on its own side of an imaginary center line — crossing your own arms is how the collection tangles.</li></ul></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Slow four-count windmill with ONE saber at a time, counting each position out loud; only add the second hand once each arm can run the pattern alone without drifting.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Your lightsabers will make a fine addition to my collection.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; hunched, raspy — add the trademark cough after</i></li><li>&ldquo;Army or not, you must realize you are doomed.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; slow menace, then a wheeze</i></li><li>&ldquo;I've been trained in your Jedi arts by Count Dooku.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; spread the arms wide — all four if your build has them</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>Your pencils will make a fine addition to my collection.</li><li>*cough cough* Homework or not, you must realize this worksheet is doomed.</li><li>Four arms means four lightsabers. Or four slices of pizza. Your choice, Kenobi.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Grievous head STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=general+grievous+head"},{"name":"Lightsaber hilt STLs","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=lightsaber+hilt"},{"name":"Instructables build","designer":"Instructables","url":"https://www.instructables.com/General-Grievous-Costume/"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Head/mask","detail":"Bone-grey paint, LED eyes."},{"name":"Ribcage plate","detail":"Or layered foam."},{"name":"Hip plates","detail":"Mirror one STL."},{"name":"Toe caps","detail":"Over plain dark boots."},{"name":"Saber hilts (×2-4)","detail":"Print or buy."}],"buy":[{"name":"Dark hooded cloak","detail":"Frayed hem."},{"name":"PVC + foam","detail":"Extra-arms rig."},{"name":"Black gloves (×2 spare)","detail":"Dummy hands."},{"name":"Yellow LEDs + CR2032","detail":"Behind the eyes."},{"name":"Bone-grey + brown paint","detail":"Plus clear coat."},{"name":"Two real sabers","detail":"Different blade colours."}]}},"bokatan":{"meta":{"word":"BO-KATAN","accent":"#3b6b9f","body":"bokatan","budget":300,"btn":"⚔ NITE OWL","dur":"8 weeks","hrs":"50–100 hrs","parts":"Blue Mandalorian armour","budgetRange":"€180–400","lead":"Bo-Katan Kryze — the Mandalorian warrior queen, two looks: classic Nite Owl and live-action. Blue-and-grey armour with the Nite Owl sigil.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The bird-eared helmet + the Nite Owl sigil + blue-and-grey paint = Bo-Katan. Don't skip the sigil.","intro":"OPERATION BO-KATAN","introSub":"NITE OWLS · BUILD MANUAL · FILE KRYZE","footer":"OPERATION BO-KATAN · BUILD MANUAL · THIS IS THE WAY · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"bokatan_public.pdf","weekPdf":"bokatan_byweek.pdf","quote":"Some of us serve a higher purpose."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Owl Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":12,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Bo-Katan's iconic helmet — T-visor with two angled bird-ear flares. Blue dome with grey accents and the Nite Owl sigil on the forehead.","tip":"The bird ears are the silhouette — don't shorten them.","files":[{"name":"Bo-Katan helmet STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=bo-katan+helmet"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Pauldrons","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Two angular pauldrons — both carry the Nite Owl sigil.","tip":"The sigil is a stylized angular V/dart with two grey eye dots — not a drawn owl.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Plates","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Layered chest and back plates over the flight suit. Live-action chest is mostly dark/light grey with blue trim; the animated Nite Owl version is bluer.","tip":"Light-grey chest, blue accents — weather it.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Flight Suit","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Dark jumpsuit base layer. Olive/dark blue.","tip":"Closer to dark navy than bright blue.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Pouches","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tactical belt with pouches and side holsters for two blasters.","tip":"Two holsters — she carries twin WESTAR-35s.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Cod + Thigh Plates","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Cod and thigh plates, matching blue.","tip":"Same colour family as the chest.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Half-Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Short cape over one shoulder (live-action). Skip for Clone Wars.","tip":"Live-action only.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Mandalorian Mercs club standards.","tip":"Mando Mercs = the Mandalorian club.","files":[{"name":"Mando Mercs","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin + Knee Armour","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Blue shin guards + knee diamonds, both legs.","tip":"Match helmet blue.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall dark tactical boots under the shin armour.","tip":"Plain dark boots.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gauntlets + Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":5,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Blue forearm vambraces + tactical gloves. Left vambrace gets the gadget cluster.","tip":"Left = gadgets.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Twin Blasters","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Twin WESTAR-35 blaster pistols, one on each hip.","tip":"Two blasters is the signature.","files":[{"name":"WESTAR blaster STL","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=westar+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 8–7","task":"Plan + order filament, flight suit, two blasters"},{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Print + finish the helmet — bird ears + owl insignia"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Chest, pauldrons, vambraces — all blue"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Belt + legs + twin holsters"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Weather + dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>An armour build like Mando, but in <span class='accent'>blue</span> with the iconic bird-eared helmet.</p><p>Two looks share the same kit — Clone Wars Nite Owl and live-action.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE ONE RULE</div><p>Bo-Katan Kryze is the Mandalorian warrior queen. The bird-eared helmet + the owl insignia + Mandalorian-blue paint = Bo-Katan. Don't skip the owl.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>Nite Owl (Clone Wars)</b> — brighter blue, owl insignia, no half-cape.</li><li><b>Live-action</b> — darker weathered blue, half-cape.</li></ul>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>The bird ears are the silhouette.</p><p>Paint Mandalorian blue with grey accents and the white owl insignia.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Armour","body":"<p class='lead'>Chest, pauldrons, vambraces, legs — all blue.</p><p>The Nite Owl insignia goes on both pauldrons.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"Finishing & Weathering","body":"<p class='lead'>Blue base, grey accents, light wear.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ SPRAY SAFETY</div>Outside, mask on, adult present if under 18.</div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Twin Blasters","body":"<p class='lead'>Twin WESTAR-35s, one per hip.</p><p>The double-holster rig is part of her signature stance.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day","body":"<ul><li>Visor clear, owl visible.</li><li>Repair kit + blue + grey touch-up.</li><li>This is the Way.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I am Bo-Katan of Clan Kryze. I was born on Mandalore and fought in the Purge. I am the last of my line.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; the full introduction — steady, no rush</i></li><li>&ldquo;Mandalorians are stronger together.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; the rallying speech — mean every word</i></li><li>&ldquo;For Mandalore!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; the battle cry — fist up, full volume</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I don't take my helmet off for picture day.</li><li>I am the last of my line. The lunch line.</li><li>Mandalorians are stronger together. Especially at tug-of-war.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Bo-Katan helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=bo-katan+helmet"},{"name":"Mandalorian armour set","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=mandalorian%20armor"},{"name":"WESTAR-35 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=westar+blaster"},{"name":"Mando Mercs club","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Bird-ear helmet","detail":"Blue + grey + owl."},{"name":"Chest plates","detail":"Blue."},{"name":"Pauldrons (×2)","detail":"Both with the owl."},{"name":"Vambraces (×2)","detail":"One with gadgets."},{"name":"Shin + knee plates","detail":"Both legs."},{"name":"Cod + thigh plates","detail":"Same blue."},{"name":"WESTAR blasters (×2)","detail":"Twin pistols."}],"buy":[{"name":"Dark flight suit","detail":"Base layer."},{"name":"Twin holster belt","detail":"Two blasters."},{"name":"Tall dark boots + gloves","detail":"Tactical."},{"name":"Mandalorian-blue + grey paint","detail":"Plus owl-white."},{"name":"Half-cape","detail":"Live-action look only."}]}},"vader":{"meta":{"word":"VADER","accent":"#c8102e","body":"vader","budget":250,"btn":"⚔ SITH","dur":"16 weeks","hrs":"80–150 hrs","parts":"12 components","budgetRange":"€80–1500+","lead":"From zero to Sith Lord in 16 weeks. A community-built guide to constructing a full Darth Vader cosplay — helmet, armor, saber, the works.","ruleLabel":"⚠ THE ONE RULE · NON-NEGOTIABLE","rule":"The helmet has no airflow — fit a small fan and take regular breaks, or you will overheat fast inside the mask.","intro":"OPERATION VADER","introSub":"CLASSIFIED · BUILD MANUAL · FILE 1138","footer":"OPERATION VADER · BUILD MANUAL · FROM ZERO TO SITH LORD · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 19 TOTAL","pubPdf":"manual_public.pdf","weekPdf":"manual_byweek.pdf","quote":"I am your father."},"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Helmet","detail":"Dome + faceplate. ¥75 Taobao base available — sand + paint."},{"name":"Chest plate","detail":"Roman Z Véšek (MakerWorld 189792) — primary. Free near-complete bundle: Jace1969 (Printables 22865). Paid: Galactic Armory €20."},{"name":"Chest control panel","detail":"TheMaker77 Thingiverse 3889513 (bundle) or BrettProjectGuy Printables 832807. NOTE: NOT in the Jace1969 bundle — must be sourced separately."},{"name":"Shoulder armor (×2)","detail":"Roman Z Véšek MakerWorld 189792 (bundled with chest) or Jace1969 Printables 22865 (free bundle). Mirror one STL for the pair."},{"name":"Belt panels / boxes (×2)","detail":"In TheMaker77 bundle. Print one, mirror for second."},{"name":"Belt buckle","detail":"In TheMaker77 bundle."},{"name":"Codpiece","detail":"MakerWorld 1834924 (free) or in Galactic Armory set."},{"name":"Shin guards (×2)","detail":"chadbaycroft Thingiverse 3244260 (life-size) OR Jace1969 bundle (Printables 22865 — includes shins). Avoid the OLD standalone shin file."},{"name":"Saber hilt","detail":"A neopixel saber (metal hilt, sound) from Taobao works — no print needed."}],"buy":[{"name":"Undersuit / robe / tunic","detail":"Black long-sleeve base layer."},{"name":"Cape","detail":"Long black flowing cape. Check thrift stores first."},{"name":"Wide leather belt","detail":"What the belt panels mount onto."},{"name":"Tall boots","detail":"Black, calf-height. Knee-high if possible."},{"name":"Leather gloves","detail":"Black, gauntlet-style."},{"name":"Steel chain (1m)","detail":"Hardware store €5–8/m, paint black, sew into cape hem. ALT: print Jace1969 bundle chain."},{"name":"LED kit","detail":"3mm LEDs · resistors · CR2032 or 9V battery · switch. Red + green + white."},{"name":"Spray paint","detail":"Black matte (Tamiya XF-69) · clear coat · small detail colors."}]},"note":"Full forge/weeks/chapters/files live in window.VADER_FORGE, window.VADER_WEEKS, window.VADER_FILES, window.VADER_CHAPTERS","forge":{}},"anakin":{"meta":{"word":"ANAKIN","accent":"#2b7fff","body":"jedi","budget":290,"btn":"⚔ JEDI","dur":"1–8 weeks","hrs":"10–120 hrs","parts":"Cloth + saber","budgetRange":"€42–400","lead":"Anakin Skywalker three ways: Episode III, Clone Wars (animated), and the Ahsoka flashback. Pick the look with the toggle above the Forge.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"One black glove on the RIGHT hand only — the mechno-hand. Left bare. Easiest accuracy win in the build.","intro":"OPERATION ANAKIN","introSub":"JEDI ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE 0001","footer":"OPERATION ANAKIN · JEDI BUILD MANUAL · BEFORE THE MASK · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 12 TOTAL","pubPdf":"anakin_public.pdf","weekPdf":"anakin_byweek.pdf","quote":"This is where the fun begins."},"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Or buy a blue neopixel saber."}],"buy":[{"name":"Brown outer tunic","detail":"Crosses over, ties under the obi."},{"name":"Cream under-tunic","detail":"Base layer."},{"name":"Tabards + obi + belt","detail":"Holds the tunic closed."},{"name":"Brown trousers + tall boots","detail":"Same colour family."},{"name":"Black glove (1)","detail":"Right hand only — the mechno-hand."},{"name":"Brown hooded robe","detail":"Hemmed ~5cm off the floor."},{"name":"Blue lightsaber","detail":"Set any saber to blue."}]},"note":"Full forge/weeks/chapters/files (incl. CW + Ahsoka look variants) live in window.ANAKIN_FORGE, window.ANAKIN_FORGE_CW, window.ANAKIN_FORGE_AHSOKA, etc.","forge":{}},"aayla":{"meta":{"word":"AAYLA","accent":"#6ba4d6","body":"aayla","budget":150,"btn":"⚔ JEDI","dur":"5 weeks","hrs":"15–30 hrs","parts":"Cloth + makeup + lekku","budgetRange":"€70–220","lead":"Aayla Secura — the Twi'lek Jedi Master, two looks: AOTC and Clone Wars. Muted medium-blue (teal-leaning) skin, leather halter outfit, and the two long head-tails (lekku). The Clone Wars look adds a single long sleeve and glove on the left arm.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The lekku and the blue skin ARE Aayla. Don't skip either — a Jedi tunic with no Twi'lek features just reads as a generic Jedi.","intro":"OPERATION AAYLA","introSub":"JEDI ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE SECURA","footer":"OPERATION AAYLA · BUILD MANUAL · THE TWI'LEK JEDI MASTER · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 9 TOTAL","pubPdf":"aayla_public.pdf","weekPdf":"aayla_byweek.pdf","quote":"Don't lose a thousand lives just to save one."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Head-Tails (Lekku)","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Craft","hours":8,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The two long head-tails draped over the shoulders, painted blue with brown leather wrap bands. Foam-stuffed fabric tubes on a skullcap.","tip":"Anchor to a snug skullcap; the lekku are heavy if oversized.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Blue Skin Paint","type":"HEAD · 02","kind":"Makeup","hours":3,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Skin-safe muted medium-blue (teal-leaning) paint on exposed skin: face, neck, midriff, and the right arm and hand. The left arm/hand are covered by the sleeve and glove in the Clone Wars look.","tip":"Use a muted teal-leaning blue, not bright sky-blue. Patch-test a day before. Skin-safe ONLY.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Aayla is cloth + makeup, not armour.","tip":"Not used for this build.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Leather Halter Top","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The brown leather halter top — short, leaves the midriff bare. Distinct from a typical Jedi tunic.","tip":"Brown leather-look. Crosses across the chest.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Wide Belt + Saber Clip","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide brown leather belt with a saber clip on the left hip.","tip":"Same brown family as the boots.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Hip Wraps","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The hanging cloth panels at the hips.","tip":"Adds the layered look below the bare midriff.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Robe (Clone Wars only)","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":40,"priority":"LOW","description":"Clone Wars look adds a brown Jedi cloak; AOTC goes without.","tip":"Hem ~5cm off the floor.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Aayla is a Jedi hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion Aayla CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Brown Leggings","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tight brown leather-look leggings tucked into the boots.","tip":"Match the leather of the top.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Tall Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tall brown leather boots up to the knee.","tip":"Riding-style or moto boots work.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Single Sleeve + Glove (left arm)","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Clone Wars look: one long tan/brown fitted sleeve plus a matching glove on the LEFT arm and hand. The right arm stays bare blue — that asymmetric single-sleeve is signature. The AOTC look leaves both arms largely bare.","tip":"Left arm only. Match the brown of the halter and belt; the right arm shows painted blue skin.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blue Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":60,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Aayla's blade is BLUE.","tip":"Set any saber to blue; the hilt is a clean cylindrical Jedi design.","files":[{"name":"Aayla saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=aayla+secura+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 1","task":"Plan + order skin paint, lekku materials, halter top, boots, saber"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Build the lekku headpiece (foam + fabric, painted blue)"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Practice the skin paint; refine the halter fit"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Assemble outfit + add the belt + saber clip"},{"label":"Week 5","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Aayla Secura</span> two ways — AOTC and Clone Wars.</p><p>Medium-blue skin, leather halter, two long head-tails. Mostly cloth + makeup + a crafted headpiece.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE TWO THINGS THAT MAKE HER</div><p>Blue skin and the wrapped head-tails. Get those right and even her fairly simple outfit reads instantly as Aayla — skip them and you're a Jedi with blue face paint. Most of your effort goes into the head-tails and the skin; the clothes are the easy part. Blue skin, two wrapped lekku, blue blade.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>AOTC</b> — brighter blue, no robe.</li><li><b>Clone Wars</b> — deeper blue + brown Jedi cloak.</li></ul>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Lekku (Head-Tails)","body":"<p class='lead'>The defining feature.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ KEEP IT LIGHT</div>Foam-stuffed fabric tubes on a snug skullcap. The leather wrap bands at the base hide where they attach.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE WRAP BANDS</div><p>The brown leather bands wrapped along the lekku at intervals are an Aayla signature — don't leave the tails bare. Strips of brown faux-leather or ribbon do the job. Match the lekku to your skin colour exactly, and anchor the skullcap firmly so they don't shift.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Blue Skin","body":"<p class='lead'>Skin-safe medium-blue paint only.</p><p>Face, neck, arms, hands, midriff. Patch-test a day before. Set with translucent powder so it doesn't rub off on the costume.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Outfit","body":"<p class='lead'>Brown leather halter + leggings + tall boots.</p><p>The bare midriff is part of the look — different from a typical Jedi tunic.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE PIECES</div><ul><li>Wide brown leather belt with a saber clip on the left hip.</li><li>Hip wraps — the hanging cloth panels at the waist.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"The Lightsaber","body":"<p class='lead'>Blue blade, clean cylindrical hilt.</p><p>Clipped on the left hip.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Lekku light + anchored well = the look holds all day.</li><li>Skin paint set with powder.</li><li>Blue blade.</li></ul>"},{"num":"08","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Ataru</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ FORM IV · ATARU — “The Way of the Hawk-Bat”</div><p>Acrobatic offense — flips, spins, and constant momentum, using the whole room as part of the weapon. A single blue blade covers everything because it never stops moving. Ataru suits a Twi'lek athlete who fights the way she moves — fluid, fast, and everywhere at once.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#2e7ff0\">⬤</span> Blue — single standard hilt, clipped left hip</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Set three soft targets (cushions) around the room and touch all three in one continuous run — pivot through each strike without stopping. Ataru scores on the move, so a pause is a miss.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;A great leap forward often requires first taking two steps back.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; calm teacher-voice, soft accent — from The Clone Wars, \"Jedi Crash\"</i></li><li>&ldquo;Sometimes it takes courage to stick to one's beliefs.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; gentle but firm — from The Clone Wars, \"Defenders of Peace\"</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>A great leap forward often begins with two steps back — especially in the lunch line.</li><li>A Jedi stays calm at all times. Even when the recess bell is late.</li><li>These headtails? Standard Jedi issue. Yours are still growing in.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Aayla saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=aayla+secura+lightsaber"},{"name":"Twi'lek lekku tutorial","designer":"search YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=twi%27lek+lekku+tutorial"},{"name":"Full Aayla costume","designer":"AliExpress / eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Aayla+Secura+costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion standards","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Or buy a blue neopixel saber."}],"buy":[{"name":"Lekku materials","detail":"Foam tubes + blue fabric + skullcap."},{"name":"Skin-safe medium-blue paint","detail":"Set with translucent powder."},{"name":"Brown leather halter top","detail":"Crosses across the chest."},{"name":"Brown leggings + tall boots","detail":"Match colour family."},{"name":"Wide leather belt + saber clip","detail":"Left hip."},{"name":"Hip wrap panels","detail":"Cloth, hanging."},{"name":"Brown Jedi robe","detail":"Clone Wars look only."},{"name":"Blue lightsaber","detail":"Set to blue."}]}},"phasma":{"meta":{"word":"PHASMA","accent":"#8a96a4","body":"phasma","budget":350,"btn":"⚔ FIRST ORDER","dur":"8 weeks","hrs":"60–120 hrs","parts":"Chrome armour + cape","budgetRange":"€180–400+","lead":"Captain Phasma — the First Order's chrome Stormtrooper commander. A full-body chrome armour build with a flowing black cape. Striking and difficult.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"It's chrome, not silver. The mirror finish is the whole point — a matte 'silver' Phasma reads as a regular trooper.","intro":"OPERATION PHASMA","introSub":"FIRST ORDER · BUILD MANUAL · FILE CHROME","footer":"OPERATION PHASMA · BUILD MANUAL · THE CHROME COMMANDER · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"phasma_public.pdf","weekPdf":"phasma_byweek.pdf","quote":"My troops will storm this block and kill you all."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Chrome Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":12,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Stormtrooper-shaped helmet with a sharper, more angular brow and a flared visor band. Mirror chrome finish.","tip":"Use mirror-finish spray or chrome vinyl wrap — painting chrome is the hardest part of the build.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Pauldrons","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Two chrome shoulder bells over the cape attachment.","tip":"Cape clips into the right pauldron.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest + Back Plate","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The chrome chest and back plates — same shape as a Stormtrooper but mirror-finished.","tip":"Practice mirror finish on a test piece first.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Ab Plate","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Chrome stomach plate linking chest to belt.","tip":"Strap so it flexes when you sit.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Boxes","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"3D Print","hours":4,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Chrome belt with the boxes — minimal compared to a Stormtrooper.","tip":"Cleaner profile than a Trooper.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Cod + Thighs","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Chrome codpiece + thigh plates.","tip":"Same lines as Trooper, all chrome.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Black Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The long flowing black cape with a dark red stripe along the front seam. It attaches at the right shoulder and falls diagonally across to the left side, hanging to near the floor. The signature.","tip":"Heavy fabric drapes best. The red is a narrow stripe along the front edge, not an interior lining.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the 501st standards — Phasma is First Order, villain.","tip":"501st = bad guys.","files":[{"name":"501st Phasma CRL","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin + Knee Plates","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Chrome shin guards + knee diamonds.","tip":"Both legs.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":45,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall black tactical boots under the leg armour.","tip":"Plain black, polished.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gloves + Forearms","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":6,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Chrome forearm plates + black gloves.","tip":"Black gloves under chrome — not white like Stormtrooper.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"F-11D Blaster","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":30,"priority":"HIGH","description":"First Order F-11D blaster rifle, weathered.","tip":"Same family as standard Trooper but First Order shape.","files":[{"name":"F-11D blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=f-11d+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 8–7","task":"Plan + order filament, chrome vinyl/paint, black cape fabric"},{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Print + finish the helmet — mirror chrome is the hardest"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Chest, pauldrons, ab plate"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Arms, legs, belt + the cape rig"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Polish everything, dress rehearsal, game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>The <span class='accent'>chrome finish</span> is the whole challenge.</p><p>A matte 'silver' Phasma reads as a generic trooper. Mirror chrome is hard — commit to it or pick a different build.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">IS THIS YOUR BUILD?</div><p>Phasma's mirror armour was salvaged, the story goes, from a Naboo yacht once owned by Palpatine himself. Choose her if you enjoy careful finishing work — sanding, priming, and getting a flawless surface. A great Phasma is a showstopper; a rushed one looks like a grey trooper. The difference is entirely in how much patience you put into the finish.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Chrome Method","body":"<ul><li><b>Mirror-finish spray</b> — specialty paint, careful application.</li><li><b>Chrome vinyl wrap</b> — easier, very flat surfaces only.</li><li><b>Chrome plating</b> — best result, expensive.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">SMOOTH FIRST, ALWAYS</div><p>Chrome magnifies flaws instead of hiding them. Whatever method you choose, the real work is the sanding underneath: 120 grit up to 800+, until the surface is like glass — get that right and even cheap chrome spray looks expensive. And always practise your chrome method on a scrap piece before you touch the real part.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>Sharper, more angular than Stormtrooper.</p><p>Print, seam-fill, sand glass-smooth (any bump shows in chrome), then chrome finish. Tinted visor band.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Armour","body":"<p class='lead'>Chest, pauldrons, ab plate, legs.</p><p>Smooth finish first — chrome reveals every imperfection. Strap with black webbing.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Cape","body":"<p class='lead'>The flowing red-lined black cape.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ HEAVY FABRIC</div>The cape needs weight to drape properly. Wool blend or heavy synthetic, red satin lining.</div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Gear","body":"<p class='lead'>F-11D blaster, black gloves.</p><p>First Order blaster, chromed to match the armour.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">FINISHING TOUCHES</div><p>Optionally add her collapsible quicksilver baton alongside the F-11D. The gloves are black, not white like a trooper's — a small detail people get wrong. And practise standing tall and commanding: Phasma does not slouch.</p></div>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day","body":"<ul><li>Polish the chrome — fingerprints show.</li><li>Repair kit + chrome touch-up.</li><li>Hux would not approve.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;FN-2187. Submit your blaster for inspection.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; cold and clipped, like the helmet is doing the talking</i></li><li>&ldquo;And who gave you permission to remove that helmet?&rdquo; <i>&mdash; slow, icy — let the silence after it do the work</i></li><li>&ldquo;You were always scum.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; her last words to Finn in The Last Jedi — flat, zero emotion</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>Your armor is out of regulation. And by armor, I mean your backpack.</li><li>Submit your homework for inspection. ...As I suspected. Incomplete.</li><li>This cafeteria is now under First Order control. The chocolate milk belongs to me.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Phasma helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse / Cults3D","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=captain+phasma+helmet"},{"name":"Phasma armour set","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=captain%20phasma"},{"name":"F-11D blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=f-11d+blaster"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Chrome helmet","detail":"Mirror finish."},{"name":"Chest + back plate","detail":"Sand glass-smooth before chrome."},{"name":"Pauldrons + ab plate","detail":"One pauldron holds the cape."},{"name":"Forearms + biceps","detail":"Black gloves underneath."},{"name":"Shin + knee plates","detail":"Both legs."},{"name":"Belt + boxes","detail":"Cleaner than Trooper."}],"buy":[{"name":"Tall black boots","detail":"Plain black."},{"name":"Black gloves","detail":"Not white."},{"name":"Heavy black cape fabric + red lining","detail":"Drape is everything."},{"name":"Mirror-chrome spray OR chrome vinyl","detail":"Hardest finish in the line."},{"name":"Sandpaper 120–800","detail":"Smooth before chrome."},{"name":"F-11D blaster","detail":"First Order rifle."}]}},"dooku":{"meta":{"word":"DOOKU","accent":"#5e3a3a","body":"dooku","budget":120,"btn":"⚔ SITH","dur":"4 weeks","hrs":"10–20 hrs","parts":"Cloth + curved saber","budgetRange":"€70–250","lead":"Count Dooku — the Sith Lord, the Separatist leader, the fallen Jedi. A regal, aristocratic build: long dark-brown robes, white hair and beard, and the iconic curved-hilt red lightsaber.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The curved-hilt saber and the white hair + beard are the signature. Without both, he's just a black-robed villain.","intro":"OPERATION DOOKU","introSub":"SITH ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE TYRANUS","footer":"OPERATION DOOKU · BUILD MANUAL · THE COUNT OF SERENNO · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"dooku_public.pdf","weekPdf":"dooku_byweek.pdf","quote":"I have become more powerful than any Jedi."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"White Hair & Beard","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Style","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Silver-grey swept-back hair + a long, sharp-pointed beard. A wig + costume beard if yours isn't there.","tip":"The beard is mandatory — it's half of Dooku.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Outer Robe (High Collar)","type":"TORSO · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":45,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Long dark-brown robe (lighter-brown lining) with the iconic high stiff collar.","tip":"The high collar is unique — not a hood. Brown wool, not grey/black.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Dooku is robes, not armour.","tip":"Not used for this build.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Inner Tunic","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark inner tunic under the robe.","tip":"Black or very dark grey.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Curved Clip","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Black belt with a clip for the curved saber hilt.","tip":"Curved hilts need a different clip than straight sabers.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Sash","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Wide dark sash at the waist.","tip":"Tied at the side.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Long Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Floor-length dark-brown cape with a clean cut — no hood. Aristocratic, not Jedi.","tip":"Hem ~5cm off the floor. Brown, not black.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the 501st standards — Dooku is a Sith villain.","tip":"501st = bad guys.","files":[{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Black Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Black (or very dark brown) trousers tucked into the boots.","tip":"Black reads best on screen; very dark brown also works.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tall black equestrian-style boots, medium gloss, no buckles.","tip":"Black lace-less riding boots — not brown.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Black Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Plain black leather gloves — both hands.","tip":"Tighter than gauntlet-style.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Curved-Hilt Red Saber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":80,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Dooku's iconic CURVED-HILT lightsaber, red blade. The curve fits his fencer's grip.","tip":"Most printable curved hilts are based on his.","files":[{"name":"Dooku curved saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=count+dooku+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Plan + order robe, cape, curved saber, wig/beard"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"First fit + hem; practice the swept-back hair"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Set saber to red; fit the curved-hilt belt clip"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Count Dooku</span> — the Sith Lord, the Count of Serenno, the elegant villain.</p><p>Almost entirely cloth + a curved saber + the white hair and beard.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Elegant-Villain Build</div><p>Where Vader is brute menace, Dooku is cold elegance. Play him with a straight back, slow precise movements, and quiet contempt — Dooku looks down on everyone, politely. The fencer's saber salute is a perfect photo pose. The performance is half the costume.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Robes","body":"<p class='lead'>Aristocratic, not Jedi.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ HIGH COLLAR, NO HOOD</div>Dooku's defining silhouette: the stiff high collar instead of a hood. Don't substitute a Jedi robe.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Layers</div><ul><li>Inner tunic — dark, simple.</li><li>Outer robe — long, dark grey/black, with the high collar; stiffen it with interfacing or wire so it stands up properly.</li><li>Cape — floor-length, clean cut, no hood, pinned at the shoulders — aristocratic, like an old-world duellist.</li><li>Sash + belt — dark, at the waist, with a clip for the curved saber.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"Hair & Beard","body":"<p class='lead'>The single most important detail.</p><p>Silver-grey, swept back, with the long sharp-pointed beard. Grow it or use a costume beard matched to your wig.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Curved Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>Red blade, the curved hilt is the icon.</p><p>The curve fits the fencer's grip he uses in duels. A curved neopixel hilt is the showpiece.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Plan the Clip</div><p>Because the hilt curves, it needs a slightly different belt clip than a straight saber — plan for that so it hangs correctly on the hip.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"Build Sequence","body":"<ul><li>Order robe, cape, boots, saber, wig + beard.</li><li>Fit & hem.</li><li>Hair + beard + red saber. Done.</li></ul>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>High collar, NOT a hood.</li><li>Beard is mandatory.</li><li>Curved hilt, red blade.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Makashi</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ FORM II · MAKASHI — “The Way of the Ysalamiri”</div><p>Duelist's precision — one hand behind the back, all economy and point control, built purely for blade-to-blade combat. He wins with the smallest movement in the room and never wastes an inch of it. Makashi is Dooku distilled — an aristocrat's form for an aristocrat, right down to the curved hilt made for a fencer's angle of attack.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#d9302b\">⬤</span> Red — curved fencing hilt, one-handed grip</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Tape a straight line on the floor and stay on it: advance and retreat in small fencing steps, off hand behind your back, throwing single thrusts and tight wrist-circle parries. If your feet leave the line, start over.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Twice the pride, double the fall.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; silky and slow — savor every word like Christopher Lee</i></li><li>&ldquo;What if I told you that the Republic was now under the control of a Dark Lord of the Sith?&rdquo; <i>&mdash; lean in, conspiratorial — you know something they don't</i></li><li>&ldquo;I sense great fear in you, Skywalker. You have hate. You have anger. But you don't use them.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; circling, taunting — one beat between each sentence</i></li><li>&ldquo;It is obvious that this contest cannot be decided by our knowledge of the Force... but by our skills with a lightsaber.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; aristocratic shrug, then ignite</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I have become more powerful than any hall monitor.</li><li>Twice the homework, double the fall.</li><li>It is obvious this contest cannot be decided by our knowledge of the Force... but by rock, paper, scissors.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Dooku curved saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=count+dooku+lightsaber"},{"name":"Curved hilt designs","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=curved%20lightsaber"},{"name":"Full Dooku costume","designer":"eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Count+Dooku+costume"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Curved saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Or buy a curved neopixel."}],"buy":[{"name":"Dark robe with high collar","detail":"NOT a hooded Jedi robe."},{"name":"Inner tunic + sash","detail":"Dark layers."},{"name":"Floor-length cape","detail":"Clean cut, no hood."},{"name":"Brown trousers + tall boots","detail":"Aristocratic."},{"name":"Black gloves","detail":"Both hands."},{"name":"Silver-grey wig + costume beard","detail":"The signature."},{"name":"Curved-hilt red saber","detail":"The icon."}]}},"royalguard":{"meta":{"word":"ROYAL GUARD","accent":"#d9352e","body":"royalguard","budget":200,"btn":"⚔ EMPIRE","dur":"6 weeks","hrs":"25–50 hrs","parts":"Red robes + helmet + force pike","budgetRange":"€100–300","lead":"The Emperor's Royal Guards — the silent crimson sentinels. A striking head-to-toe red build: long robes, the tinted-visor helmet, and the force pike.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"Keep everything in the red family — crimson outer robe, boots and helmet, with deeper burgundy/wine inner robe and gloves. Avoid an off-tone red that clashes and breaks the silhouette.","intro":"OPERATION ROYAL GUARD","introSub":"IMPERIAL ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE CRIMSON","footer":"OPERATION ROYAL GUARD · BUILD MANUAL · THE EMPEROR'S SENTINELS · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 6 TOTAL","pubPdf":"royalguard_public.pdf","weekPdf":"royalguard_byweek.pdf","quote":"(silent — duty above all)"},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Tinted-Visor Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The tall, sleek crimson helmet with a slender red/smoke-tinted visor down the center front. The most identifiable piece — the tint hides the eyes while you can still see out.","tip":"Use transparent red or smoke acrylic for the visor so the face reads as hidden but stays see-through — never a mirrored or opaque visor.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Folds","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Sew","hours":2,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The robe's shoulder folds drape down into the cape — not separate pauldrons.","tip":"Part of the robe construction; fall naturally from the collar.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Robe","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Sew","hours":4,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The robe's chest section. Heavy red fabric, structured.","tip":"Heavy fabric drapes correctly; thin fabric looks like a sheet.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"No Panel","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"No control panel — the robe is one piece.","tip":"Not used for this build.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Hidden Belt","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"LOW","description":"A simple belt under the robe to hold it shape. Not visible.","tip":"Inside the robe — nothing shows.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"No Codpiece","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Hidden under the floor-length robe.","tip":"Not used for this build.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Long Cape Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Sew","hours":6,"cost":55,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The floor-length, sweeping red cape-robe that forms most of the silhouette.","tip":"Hem ~2cm off the floor — they walked very slowly so it grazed.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the 501st standards — Royal Guard is Imperial.","tip":"501st = bad guys.","files":[{"name":"501st Royal Guard CRL","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Red Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":20,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Red trousers under the floor-length robe — barely visible but there.","tip":"Match the robe red.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Red Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Red boots or red-painted black boots, mostly hidden by the robe.","tip":"Hidden, but show when walking.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Burgundy Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Burgundy/wine cloth or suede gloves — both hands. Darker than the crimson outer robe, matched to the inner robe lining.","tip":"Aim for a burgundy/wine tone rather than crimson robe-red; avoid shiny/satin/leather — spray-paint plain cloth gloves if needed.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Force Pike","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":5,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"A tall single-ended polearm (min ~122cm) — a long pole with a black pommel and grips at the base and one metallic emitter/power tip at the top. Not a double-bladed staff.","tip":"Lightweight pole + one foam or 3D-printed emitter tip; mind its length in crowds.","files":[{"name":"Force pike STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=imperial+royal+guard+force+pike"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Plan + order red fabric, helmet filament, pole for the pike"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Print + finish the helmet — match the fabric red"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Sew the long cape robe + shoulder folds"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Build the force pike + match all reds"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>The Emperor's silent sentinels — head-to-toe crimson.</p><p>Long robe, slit-visored helmet, force pike. A striking silhouette built almost entirely from heavy red fabric.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Match Your Reds","body":"<div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ ONE RED, EVERYWHERE</div>Robe, helmet, gloves, boots — ALL the same red. Bring a fabric swatch when shopping for anything. Mismatched reds are the single most common mistake.</div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>Tall, narrow vertical visor slit.</p><p>Print, prime, then paint to MATCH the robe fabric exactly. Take the fabric to the paint store.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Seeing Out</div><p>The narrow visor slit is your view-port — back it with dark mesh so you can see out while your face stays hidden. Confirm vision and airflow before you finish. The hood sits over the helmet, so leave room for both.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Robe","body":"<p class='lead'>Heavy fabric, floor-length, structured shoulders.</p><p>Thin fabric falls flat — you need weight. Wool blend or heavy synthetic.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Fabric &amp; Coverage</div><p>Heavy, matte fabric drapes best — avoid shiny costume satin. Add red gloves and soft red boots so no skin shows anywhere.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Force Pike","body":"<p class='lead'>Tall staff with bladed ends.</p><p>Lightweight pole + foam caps painted to match. Mind its length around small kids and ceilings.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Game Day","body":"<ul><li>Silent, slow movement is part of the character.</li><li>Mind the pike around crowds and ceilings.</li><li>Stand at parade rest by the throne.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;(Return of the Jedi — the throne room) The Emperor says \"Leave us.\" The Guards turn in perfect sync and glide out without one word. That IS the line.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; your whole performance is the silent pivot-and-exit</i></li><li>&ldquo;(Return of the Jedi — the shuttle landing) Rows of crimson Guards flank the Emperor's arrival, motionless as statues. Not a sound, not a twitch.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; practice standing perfectly still for 30 seconds — it's harder than it looks</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>(says nothing — but points at the snack table with tremendous authority)</li><li>(turns head very slowly toward whoever took the last cookie. Says nothing. It works.)</li><li>(silence. But it is an extremely loud silence.)</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Royal Guard helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=imperial+royal+guard+helmet"},{"name":"Force pike STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=imperial+royal+guard+force+pike"},{"name":"Full Royal Guard costume","designer":"eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Imperial+Royal+Guard+costume"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Slit helmet","detail":"Match the robe red exactly."},{"name":"Force pike STL parts","detail":"Pole + bladed ends."}],"buy":[{"name":"Heavy red fabric (long robe)","detail":"Wool blend or heavy synthetic."},{"name":"Red trousers + boots","detail":"Match the robe."},{"name":"Red gloves","detail":"Both hands, matching."},{"name":"Hidden belt","detail":"Under the robe."},{"name":"Lightweight pole","detail":"For the force pike."},{"name":"Red spray paint","detail":"To match all components."}]}},"jango":{"meta":{"word":"JANGO","accent":"#2c4b6e","body":"jango","budget":320,"btn":"⚔ GUILD","dur":"8 weeks","hrs":"50–100 hrs","parts":"Navy Mando armour","budgetRange":"€180–400","lead":"Jango Fett — the original Mandalorian, Boba's father, the bounty hunter the clone army was modeled on. Two looks: Geonosis (with cape) and Kamino (without).","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"Jango is NAVY, not Boba's green. The blue is darker and more saturated than Bo-Katan's — it's its own colour.","intro":"OPERATION JANGO","introSub":"GUILD · BUILD MANUAL · FILE PRIME","footer":"OPERATION JANGO · BUILD MANUAL · THE ORIGINAL MANDALORIAN · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"jango_public.pdf","weekPdf":"jango_byweek.pdf","quote":"I'm just a simple man trying to make my way in the universe."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Silver T-Visor Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Mandalorian T-visor helmet, similar to Boba's shape but unweathered, silver/grey with navy detail.","tip":"Cleaner finish than Boba; less battle damage.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Pauldrons","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Two navy shoulder pauldrons over the flight suit.","tip":"Navy with silver detail.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Plate","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The central navy chest plate with the curved silver chest panel.","tip":"Navy base, silver/grey middle band.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Flight Suit","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Grey/blue flight suit base under the armour.","tip":"Closer to grey than blue under the plates.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Holsters","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tactical belt with two side holsters for the twin blasters.","tip":"Twin hip holsters — Jango's own signature, later copied by Boba.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Cod + Thigh Plates","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Navy codpiece + thigh guards.","tip":"Match the chest navy.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Poncho (Geonosis only)","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"A heathered charcoal/grey wool western-style poncho (head-through neck slit) draped over the shoulders for the Geonosis arena look; Kamino skips it.","tip":"Geonosis only — grey wool poncho, not a brown cape.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Mando Mercs standards.","tip":"Mando Mercs = the Mandalorian club.","files":[{"name":"Mando Mercs","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin + Knee Armour","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Navy shin guards + knees, both legs.","tip":"Navy + silver.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall grey/dark boots under the shins.","tip":"Grey under the navy.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gauntlets","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Navy vambraces — left one with the wrist gadgets (flamethrower, dart) — plus grey gloves.","tip":"Left = gadgets, same as Mando family.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Twin Westar-34 Blasters","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Twin Westar-34 blaster pistols, one on each hip. The twin-blaster move is Jango's signature.","tip":"Twin Westar-34s — Jango's signature dual-wield draw.","files":[{"name":"Westar-34 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=westar-34+blaster"}]},"jetpack":{"name":"Jetpack","type":"BACK · 13","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":35,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Jango's jetpack — the Geonosis arena pack or the JT-12-style Kamino pack he flies with against Obi-Wan. Silver with dark/light blue detail; mounts on a back harness.","tip":"Print as its own zone; silver + blue, mount on a back harness.","files":[]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 8–7","task":"Plan + order filament, flight suit, two Westar blasters"},{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Print + finish the helmet — navy + silver"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Chest, pauldrons, gauntlets — keep clean (unweathered)"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Belt + legs + twin holsters"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"(Geonosis: add the cape) + dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>An armour build like Boba but in <span class='accent'>navy</span> — and clean, not weathered.</p><p>Jango's armour is unbattered — the look is sharp and new, the opposite of Boba's worn ROTJ kit.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Family Resemblance</div><p>Jango was so good the Republic cloned an entire army from him. He and Boba share the same helmet shape and gear layout — if you already understand a Boba build, you're 80% of the way to Jango. Building both, father and son, is a fantastic pair project, and the Mando Mercs costuming community takes this kit seriously.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Jango vs Boba","body":"<ul><li><b>Jango (Geonosis/Kamino)</b> — navy, clean, twin Westar-34s.</li><li><b>Boba (ESB/ROTJ)</b> — green, weathered, EE-3 carbine + cape.</li></ul><p>Father and son. Same helmet shape, different paint and condition.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Pick Your Look</div><p>Kamino (the rainy cloning world) is the clean look with no cape — simplest. Geonosis (the arena battle) adds a short cape over one shoulder. Start with Kamino.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>T-visor, navy + silver.</p><p>Cleaner finish than Boba — don't weather it.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Armour","body":"<p class='lead'>Chest, pauldrons, gauntlets, legs — all navy.</p><p>The chest centre band is silver/grey — that's distinct from Boba.</p><h3>The Jetpack</h3><p>Jango wears the silver-and-navy jetpack with the central fin and rocket — the piece that says 'Mandalorian' from across a room. Light is right: build it from foam or a hollow print, not solid plastic — a heavy jetpack ruins your back and your day. It hangs on a harness under the chest plate. Even a simplified jetpack reads perfectly.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"Finishing — CLEAN","body":"<p class='lead'>Navy base, silver accents, NO weathering.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ SPRAY SAFETY</div>Outside, mask on, adult present if under 18.</div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Twin Blasters","body":"<p class='lead'>Twin Westar-34s, one per hip.</p><p>The dual-wield draw is the Jango move.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day","body":"<ul><li>Polish the chrome accents.</li><li>Repair kit + navy + silver touch-up.</li><li>I'm just a simple man trying to make my way in the universe.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Always a pleasure to meet a Jedi.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; dry, unhurried — a handshake that's also a warning</i></li><li>&ldquo;They'll do their job well. I'll guarantee that.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; quiet pride, no bragging — you built that army</i></li><li>&ldquo;Seismic charges... stand by.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; pause, then make the BWAAAH sound yourself — everyone will get it</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I'm just a simple kid, trying to make my way to the cafeteria.</li><li>Always a pleasure to meet a substitute teacher.</li><li>My jetpack's in the shop. I take the bus like everyone else.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Mandalorian helmet STL (Jango shape)","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=jango+fett+helmet"},{"name":"Jango armour set","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=jango%20fett"},{"name":"Westar-34 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=westar-34+blaster"},{"name":"Mando Mercs club","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"T-visor helmet","detail":"Navy + silver, clean."},{"name":"Chest plate","detail":"Navy + silver centre band."},{"name":"Pauldrons (×2)","detail":"Navy."},{"name":"Vambraces (×2)","detail":"Left has the gadget cluster."},{"name":"Shin + knee plates","detail":"Both legs."},{"name":"Cod + thigh plates","detail":"Navy."},{"name":"Westar-34 blasters (×2)","detail":"Twin pistols."}],"buy":[{"name":"Grey/blue flight suit","detail":"Base layer."},{"name":"Twin holster belt","detail":"Two blasters."},{"name":"Grey boots + gloves","detail":"Under the navy."},{"name":"Navy + silver paint","detail":"Plus clear coat."},{"name":"Brown cape","detail":"Geonosis only."}]}},"padme":{"meta":{"word":"PADMÉ","accent":"#c9a85e","body":"padme","budget":250,"btn":"⚔ NABOO","dur":"6 weeks","hrs":"30–60 hrs","parts":"Cloth + headdress + makeup","budgetRange":"€120–400","lead":"Padmé Amidala — Queen of Naboo, Senator, the woman behind the masks. Three looks: the red Queen throne gown, the white Geonosis battle outfit, and the senate robes.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The Queen look is high-effort: red throne gown + white face paint + ornate headdress. Don't half-do any of the three — pick the simpler senator/battle look if budget or time is tight.","intro":"OPERATION PADMÉ","introSub":"NABOO ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE AMIDALA","footer":"OPERATION PADMÉ · BUILD MANUAL · QUEEN, SENATOR, MOTHER · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"padme_public.pdf","weekPdf":"padme_byweek.pdf","quote":"So this is how liberty dies... with thunderous applause."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Headdress / Hair","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Craft","hours":10,"cost":60,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Queen: the ornate gold + red headdress with the floating gold pendant. Senator/Geonosis: braided hair.","tip":"The Queen headdress is the most distinctive prequel costume detail. Worth the effort.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Outer Gown / Top","type":"TORSO · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":4,"cost":70,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Queen: red velvet floor-length throne gown. Geonosis: white halter-top (the torn-midriff battle look). Senator: layered cream/gold robes.","tip":"Match the era — these are very different garments.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Padmé is cloth, not armour.","tip":"Not used for this build.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Inner Layer","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Base layer under the gown or halter.","tip":"White or matching the era.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt / Sash","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":20,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Cinched belt on the Geonosis look; sash on the senator look; hidden under the gown for the Queen.","tip":"Matches the era.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"No Codpiece","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Not applicable.","tip":"Not used for this build.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Sleeves / Sash","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":25,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The flowing senator over-sleeves OR the trailing Queen sleeves — the gown's drama lives here.","tip":"Heavier fabric drapes better.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Padmé is a hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion Padme CRL","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers / Skirt","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Geonosis: white trousers. Queen + Senator: floor-length — no trousers visible.","tip":"Era-dependent.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Geonosis: tall white/cream boots. Queen + Senator: hidden under the gown.","tip":"Geonosis only really shows.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"No Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Padmé goes bare-handed in most looks.","tip":"Not used for this build.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"ELG-3A Blaster Pistol","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Padmé's silver Naboo sporting pistol (the ELG-3A 'Diplomat's Blaster') for the Geonosis arena battle.","tip":"She's a senator AND a soldier — carry it for the Geonosis look. Silver with a wood-look grip.","files":[{"name":"Defender blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=defender+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Pick a look + order fabric / pre-made base; gather makeup if Queen"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Sew or fit the gown / battle outfit"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Build the headdress (Queen) or do the braided hair (Senator/Geonosis)"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Practice the Queen white face paint + red lip + cheek dots"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Padmé Amidala</span> three ways — Queen of Naboo, Geonosis arena, Senate.</p><p>Three very different looks; pick one to start.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">A Leader and a Fighter</div><p>Padmé is a queen who rules, a senator who argues, and a fighter who grabs a blaster in the Geonosis arena. Build her with that backbone — she's never just standing there looking pretty. Whatever the era, stand tall and composed: Padmé commands a room by stillness and presence, not fuss. And commit fully — a fully-realised Senator beats a half-finished Queen every time.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>Queen (Episode I)</b> — red throne gown + white face paint + ornate headdress. HARD.</li><li><b>Geonosis (Episode II)</b> — white halter top + trousers + the torn-midriff battle look. MEDIUM.</li><li><b>Senator</b> — layered cream/gold robes + braided hair. EASIEST.</li></ul>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Queen Headdress","body":"<p class='lead'>The most distinctive prequel costume detail.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ CRAFT IT</div>Wire frame + papier-mâché or foam + gold paint + faux gems. Tutorials exist on YouTube.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">What You're Building</div><p>The wide black hairpiece with the gold side medallions and the hanging centre pendant — the most distinctive single piece in the entire prequel wardrobe. Shape the frame wide on both sides and cover it in black fabric or a styled wig. It's fiddly but hugely rewarding.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Queen Makeup","body":"<p class='lead'>White base + red lower lip stripe + red cheek dots (the royal beauty marks).</p><p>Skin-safe theatrical white. Set with powder. Take your time — sharp lines matter.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Geonosis Battle Outfit","body":"<p class='lead'>White halter top + cream trousers + tall boots + ELG-3A blaster.</p><p>The torn-midriff is intentional — cut it after wearing and moving in it.<div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Carry the Blaster</div><p>Padmé carries her small silver blaster into the arena — she's a fighter, not a damsel, and the prop completes the look. Check your event's prop rules before carrying any blaster.</p></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"The Senator Robes","body":"<p class='lead'>Layered cream/gold with braided hair.</p><p>The easiest of the three. Beautiful but less effort than the Queen.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Pick ONE look and commit — don't mix.</li><li>Queen needs MOST effort; Senator needs LEAST.</li><li>Queen face paint patch-tested.</li></ul>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Anakin, you're breaking my heart! You're going down a path I can't follow.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; big and tearful — hand over heart</i></li><li>&ldquo;I was not elected to watch my people suffer and die while you discuss this invasion in a committee!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; queen voice — stand tall, no pauses, let it build</i></li><li>&ldquo;I will not condone a course of action that will lead us to war.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; calm and regal — chin up, every word even</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>So this is how recess dies... with thunderous applause.</li><li>I was not elected to watch soggy fries be discussed in a committee.</li><li>Relax — that's not me, that's my decoy. I'm already in line for snacks.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Queen Amidala headdress tutorial","designer":"YouTube search","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=queen+amidala+headdress+tutorial"},{"name":"Padmé ELG-3A blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=padme+defender+blaster"},{"name":"Full Padmé costume (any look)","designer":"Etsy / eBay","url":"https://www.etsy.com/market/padme_amidala_costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion standards","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"ELG-3A blaster (Geonosis only)","detail":"Silver Naboo pistol."}],"buy":[{"name":"Red velvet (Queen) OR white halter (Geo) OR cream robes (Senate)","detail":"Pick one era."},{"name":"Headdress materials (Queen)","detail":"Wire + foam + gold paint + gems."},{"name":"White theatrical face paint + red","detail":"Queen only."},{"name":"Tall white/cream boots (Geo)","detail":"Or hidden under gown."},{"name":"Layered base + sash","detail":"Era-dependent."},{"name":"Braided wig OR hair clips","detail":"Senator/Geo."},{"name":"Gold accent fabric","detail":"For the senate robes."}]}},"nihilus":{"meta":{"word":"NIHILUS","accent":"#b8a890","body":"nihilus","budget":150,"btn":"⚔ SITH","dur":"5 weeks","hrs":"20–40 hrs","parts":"Death mask + tattered robes","budgetRange":"€80–250","lead":"Darth Nihilus — the Lord of Hunger from Knights of the Old Republic II. The white death mask, the tattered black robes, the red lightsaber. One of the most distinctive Sith looks in any era.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The mask IS Nihilus. A floor-to-floor terror in black robes is just generic Sith without that bone-white face.","intro":"OPERATION NIHILUS","introSub":"SITH ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE HUNGER","footer":"OPERATION NIHILUS · BUILD MANUAL · LORD OF HUNGER · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"nihilus_public.pdf","weekPdf":"nihilus_byweek.pdf","quote":"(speaks no words — only hunger)"},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Death Mask","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The bone-white death mask: smooth oval, no skull features, black void eye-slits. Two red vertical stripes rise over the eye holes and taper upward, with a two-layered metallic silver bar running from the nose up the forehead.","tip":"Print, sand glass-smooth, prime, paint bone-white, then a light brown wash to age it. Mask the silver forehead bar, then add the two red eye-stripes last in thin red, tapering upward.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Wraps","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Sew","hours":2,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tattered dark fabric strips draping from the shoulders into the cape.","tip":"Cut raw edges, don't hem.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Nihilus is robes, not armour.","tip":"Not used for this build.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Inner Layered Tunic","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Multiple layered dark robes — a base black robe, then a tattered grey-black over-layer.","tip":"Tatter the over-layer with scissors after wearing it; uneven cuts read as 'ancient'.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt / Sash","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Dark sash at the waist — simple, hidden.","tip":"Same dark as the inner robe.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Lower Robes","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The hanging lower robe panels, also tattered.","tip":"Tatter the hem.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Tattered Hooded Cloak","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":45,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The big floor-length tattered hooded cloak. Hood up reveals only the mask — the entrance shot.","tip":"Hood up is the iconic image; eyes hidden, only the mask shows.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Nihilus is from the KOTOR II game, so 501st has him as a game-era Sith.","tip":"Niche but the 501st knows him.","files":[{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Black trousers — totally hidden by the robe.","tip":"Plain black.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Black boots, hidden by the floor-length robe.","tip":"Mostly invisible.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Black Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Black leather gloves, both hands.","tip":"The only skin showing is none — mask + gloves only.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Red Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":70,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Red blade, plain dark hilt.","tip":"Nothing fancy about the hilt — the mask carries the look.","files":[{"name":"Sith saber hilt STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=sith+lightsaber+hilt"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 1","task":"Plan + order fabric (tatter quality), mask filament, red saber"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Print + finish the mask — bone-white, runes, brown wash"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Sew the tattered cloak + layered tunic"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Test wear; tatter where it falls; refine hood placement"},{"label":"Week 5","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Darth Nihilus</span> — the Lord of Hunger from KOTOR II.</p><p>Bone-white death mask, tattered black robes, red blade. One of the most distinctive Sith looks in any era.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Mask","body":"<p class='lead'>THE signature.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ BONE WHITE + AGED</div>Smooth print, sand glass-smooth, prime, paint bone-white, brown wash for age, then thin red runes across the brow and cheeks.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Seeing &amp; Breathing</div><p>The eye hollows are deep shadow and your view-port — back them with dark mesh that hides your real eyes while letting you see out. Make sure you can breathe and see clearly before you finish painting. Comfort first.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Tattered Robes","body":"<p class='lead'>Layered, raw-cut, ancient.</p><p>Base robe + over-tunic + cloak — all dark. Cut the edges raw after wearing them so the cuts fall naturally.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Fray It on Purpose</div><p>Lightweight, flowing fabric drifts as you move — which makes the empty figure feel alive and wrong in the best way. Gently fray the ragged hems so the figure looks like it's dissolving at the edges.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Silhouette","body":"<p class='lead'>Hood up, mask out, only black gloves visible.</p><p>The entrance shot: only the mask and the hands show. The Force-aura is implied by the way you stand still.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Move Like the Hunger</div><p>Slow, gliding movement — he should seem to float in those robes. Total silence; let the blank mask do the talking. Tilt the head slowly, as if studying you with eyes that aren't there. Pairs beautifully with a Revan — the two Old Republic Sith make a stunning duo.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>Red blade, plain hilt.</p><p>The mask carries the costume — don't overcomplicate the saber.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Mask + tatter + hood. Three things.</li><li>Stand still. Nihilus is silent.</li><li>The Lord of Hunger does not speak.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Old Republic style</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · OLD REPUBLIC STYLE</div><p>No numbered form on record — the Force does the fighting and the blade merely finishes what the hunger started. What swordwork he shows reads closest to Form VI Niman: a plain, balanced frame wrapped around overwhelming dark-side power. A wound in the Force does not need technique — the mask, the silence, and the drain do the duelling for him.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#d02828\">⬤</span> Red — plain dark Old Republic hilt</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Practice stillness: hold one low guard for a slow count of ten, deliver a single heavy diagonal cut, then freeze again. For Nihilus, the pause IS the technique — move like the room owes you its life.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;(He never speaks a single translatable word in KOTOR II — only a deep, warped drone from behind the mask. That IS the line.)&rdquo; <i>&mdash; hum low in your throat, stand perfectly still — silence does the work</i></li><li>&ldquo;(The slow head-turn and hollow groan aboard the Ravager when Visas kneels and pledges 'My life for yours' — he answers with sound, not speech.)&rdquo; <i>&mdash; tilt the mask very slowly toward whoever spoke, then hold</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>Mrrhhhnnnn. (Translation: someone ate my lunch. It was me. I am the hunger.)</li><li>I don't talk. I snack — on planets. Your granola bar is safe. Probably.</li><li>Teacher: 'Any questions?' Me: one long, spooky drone.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Nihilus mask STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=darth+nihilus+mask"},{"name":"Sith hilt STL (any plain)","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=sith+lightsaber+hilt"},{"name":"Full Nihilus cosplay reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=darth+nihilus"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Death mask","detail":"Bone-white, brown wash, red runes."},{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Plain dark."}],"buy":[{"name":"Dark robes (base + over-layer)","detail":"Tatter the over-layer."},{"name":"Tattered hooded cloak","detail":"Hood up for the entrance."},{"name":"Black trousers + boots","detail":"Hidden under the robe."},{"name":"Black gloves","detail":"Both hands."},{"name":"Bone-white + brown wash paint","detail":"For the mask."},{"name":"Red lightsaber","detail":"Plain hilt."}]}},"palpatine":{"meta":{"word":"PALPATINE","accent":"#d4b834","body":"palpatine","budget":80,"btn":"⚔ EMPEROR","dur":"3 weeks","hrs":"6–12 hrs","parts":"Cloth (the easiest build)","budgetRange":"€40–150","lead":"The Emperor himself — the Sith Master pulling every string. The easiest build in the line: a deep black hooded robe + makeup + Sith lightning hands.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"Hood UP, face IN SHADOW. The hidden face is the menace. A visible face under good light kills it.","intro":"OPERATION PALPATINE","introSub":"SITH MASTER · BUILD MANUAL · FILE SIDIOUS","footer":"OPERATION PALPATINE · BUILD MANUAL · THE EMPEROR · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"palpatine_public.pdf","weekPdf":"palpatine_byweek.pdf","quote":"Unlimited POWER!"},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Aged Face / Hood","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Makeup","hours":2,"cost":15,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Pale grey-yellow skin, deep wrinkles, golden Sith eyes. Or just keep the hood deep enough that nothing shows.","tip":"Hood deep + face in shadow is the easiest path.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"No Shoulders","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Hidden by the robe.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Pure cloth.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"No Panel","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Hidden by the robe.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Saber Clip","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"LOW","description":"Hidden inside the robe; just for the saber clip.","tip":"Invisible from outside.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"No Codpiece","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Hidden under robe.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Deep Hooded Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":4,"cost":45,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The signature: floor-length, very deep hood, deep black. Wide bell sleeves.","tip":"DEEP hood that hides the face is the whole costume.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against 501st standards — Emperor is the villain-in-chief.","tip":"501st = bad guys.","files":[{"name":"501st CRL","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"No Trousers Visible","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Hidden by the floor-length robe.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":30,"priority":"LOW","description":"Black, hidden under the robe.","tip":"Plain black.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Bare Hands","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Bare gnarled hands are the menacing detail — white/pale makeup on hands.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Red Saber (hidden)","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":60,"priority":"LOW","description":"Red saber kept hidden up the sleeve until needed. Hands are the real weapon — use Sith lightning prop wire FX for photos.","tip":"Force lightning effect FX is achievable with bare-wire LEDs in the sleeves.","files":[{"name":"Force lightning FX tutorial","designer":"YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=force+lightning+cosplay"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 3","task":"Plan + order robe, makeup, optional saber"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Fit + hem; practice the hood depth in a mirror"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Practice the makeup (pale + golden Sith eyes if desired)"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>The <span class='accent'>easiest build in the line</span>.</p><p>A black hooded robe + makeup + the hidden face = instantly Palpatine. No printing, no armour.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">WHY THIS IS THE SMART FIRST BUILD</div><p>You'll learn the three skills every costume needs — fit, fabric, and presence — without spending a single hour at a 3D printer. Master the Emperor and every cloth-based build after this (Dooku, Nihilus, Revan, the Inquisitors) gets easier. Done right, a good Emperor can stand perfectly still in a doorway and make a whole room go quiet.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Robe","body":"<p class='lead'>Deep hood matters more than fabric.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ HOOD DEPTH</div>Test your robe in front of a mirror with overhead light. If your face shows, the hood isn't deep enough. Add lining or reshape.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">MATTE, NEVER SHINY — AND THE SLEEVES MATTER</div><p>Look for heavy, matte fabric — wool-blend or a thick synthetic. Cheap costume-shop shine reads as 'wizard,' not 'Sith Lord.' The hem should just kiss the floor so you glide rather than walk. Palpatine's sleeves are wide and long — they hide the hands until he wants them seen, and give you somewhere to conceal a saber or your lightning props for a dramatic reveal.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Face","body":"<p class='lead'>Or, the no-face.</p><p>Easiest: keep hood deep, face in shadow. Harder: pale yellow makeup with deep wrinkles + golden Sith eye contacts.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Hands","body":"<p class='lead'>Bare, gnarled, pale.</p><p>Pale makeup on hands sells the age. For photos, the Force-lightning FX in post or with prop wires steals every shot.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Hood up, face dark.</li><li>Hands pale.</li><li>Cackle on command.</li><li>Power. Unlimited POWER!</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">HOW TO MOVE LIKE SIDIOUS</div><ul><li>Slow down. The Emperor is never in a hurry — the galaxy waits for him.</li><li>Hunch slightly, as if hiding great age and greater power.</li><li>Speak low and quiet, so people lean in.</li><li>Save the big moment — the hood-back reveal, the lightning pose — for cameras. Stillness is power: the scariest Emperor barely moves.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Unorthodox — no single form</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · UNORTHODOX — NO SINGLE FORM</div><p>Canon never pins him to one number — Legends calls him a master of every form, and on screen he simply erupts. His frenzy against Windu and Yoda reads closest to Form VII Juyo: raw dark-side speed, and even then the saber is only the warm-up act for the lightning. The saber is a stage prop for a man whose real weapons are lightning and patience — he only draws once the audience is already doomed.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#c9242c\">⬤</span> Red — slim gilded hilt, kept hidden up the sleeve</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Rehearse the sleeve draw: saber flat along the forearm, then one motion — snap to ignition height, single strike, and return to perfect stillness. Ten slow repetitions before you are ever allowed to do it fast.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Execute Order 66.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; quiet and calm — the stillness is what makes it chilling</i></li><li>&ldquo;I am the Senate.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; slow and offended, eyebrows up</i></li><li>&ldquo;Do it.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; almost a whisper — lean in</i></li><li>&ldquo;So be it... Jedi.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; spit the last word</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I am the Senate. Also the line leader. Also the snack committee.</li><li>Somehow, my homework returned.</li><li>Execute Order 66: everyone gets dessert first.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Force lightning FX","designer":"YouTube tutorials","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=force+lightning+cosplay"},{"name":"Sith robe pattern","designer":"Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=sith+robe+pattern"},{"name":"Full Palpatine costume","designer":"eBay","url":"https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=Emperor+Palpatine+costume"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Red saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Concealed up the sleeve."}],"buy":[{"name":"Deep-hooded black robe","detail":"Floor-length, wide sleeves."},{"name":"Pale theatrical makeup","detail":"Yellow-grey skin tone."},{"name":"Golden Sith eye contacts (optional)","detail":"Costume contacts only."},{"name":"Plain black boots","detail":"Hidden under robe."},{"name":"Optional red saber","detail":"Concealed."}]}},"rex":{"meta":{"word":"REX","accent":"#1e4d80","body":"rex","budget":300,"btn":"⚔ 501ST","dur":"8 weeks","hrs":"50–100 hrs","parts":"Clone armour with 501st blue markings","budgetRange":"€150–350","lead":"Captain Rex — the 501st clone captain, Anakin's right hand, the soldier who survived the Empire. White Clone Trooper armour with the iconic blue 501st markings.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"It's a Clone Trooper base + 501st BLUE markings. Get the blue stripes right — they're the signature.","intro":"OPERATION REX","introSub":"501ST · BUILD MANUAL · FILE CT-7567","footer":"OPERATION REX · BUILD MANUAL · EXPERIENCE OUTRANKS EVERYTHING · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"rex_public.pdf","weekPdf":"rex_byweek.pdf","quote":"In my book, experience outranks everything."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Phase II Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Phase II Clone helmet with Rex's two blue jaig eyes on the forehead (his signature marking), the blue visor band and cheek stripes, plus the kill/tally marks.","tip":"The jaig eyes are THE detail — get those right first. Phase II is rounder than the Phase I that Trooper uses; don't paint a Stormtrooper helmet.","files":[{"name":"Phase II clone helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=phase+ii+clone+helmet"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Pauldrons","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"White pauldrons with blue accent stripes.","tip":"501st blue trim.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest + Back Plate","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Phase II chest + back plates with blue accents on the edges and the centre.","tip":"Slightly rounded Phase II shape.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Kama (Skirt Plate)","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The blue-trimmed Kama — the cloth skirt over the legs, signature commander piece.","tip":"Officers wear the Kama; regular clones don't.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Holsters","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tactical belt with TWO side holsters — Rex carries TWIN DC-17 blaster pistols.","tip":"Twin holsters — the dual-wield is his signature.","files":[{"name":"DC-17 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=dc-17+blaster"}]},"codpiece":{"name":"Cod + Thigh Plates","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"White cod + thighs with blue trim.","tip":"Match the chest blue.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"No Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Rex doesn't wear a cape.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against 501st standards — yes, Rex is in the 501st (different costume club, same name).","tip":"Confusing: 501st Legion the costume club has Rex of the 501st Legion the in-universe unit.","files":[{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin + Knee Plates","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"White shins + knees with blue stripes, both legs.","tip":"501st blue stripes down the front.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"White or dark boots under the leg armour.","tip":"Mostly hidden.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gauntlets + Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"White vambraces + tan/black tactical gloves.","tip":"Standard Clone vambraces.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Twin DC-17 Blasters","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"TWIN DC-17 hand blaster pistols — one each hip. The dual-wield is Rex.","tip":"Rex's signature is the twin draw.","files":[{"name":"DC-17 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=dc-17+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 8–7","task":"Plan + order filament, undersuit, twin blasters"},{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Print + finish the Phase II helmet — blue stripes are key"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Chest, pauldrons, vambraces — all white + blue trim"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Belt, Kama, twin holsters, legs"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Weather lightly + dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>An armour build like Trooper, but in the <span class='accent'>Phase II Clone</span> shape and with 501st BLUE markings.</p><p>Same family as Stormtrooper but the helmet and details are clearly Clone-era.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Phase II vs Stormtrooper","body":"<ul><li><b>Phase II Clone</b> — rounder helmet, blue 501st stripes, twin DC-17s, Kama skirt.</li><li><b>Stormtrooper</b> — simpler angular helmet, all-white, E-11 rifle.</li></ul><p>They share DNA but Rex's helmet is distinctly Clone.</p>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>Phase II shape + 501st blue stripes + visor tally marks.</p><p>Print Phase II (not Stormtrooper), then paint white, then mask + paint the blue forehead band and cheek stripes.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">JAIG EYES — OPTIONAL HONOUR</div><p>Rex's helmet sometimes carries 'jaig eyes' — a Mandalorian mark of valour. A nice detail to add once the basics are done. And take your time on the masking — crisp blue lines are what make people say 'that's Rex,' not just 'a clone.'</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Armour","body":"<p class='lead'>White base, 501st blue accents everywhere.</p><p>Chest centre stripe, pauldron edges, shin stripes, knee diamonds.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">UNDERSUIT + LIGHT WEATHERING</div><p>Strap everything over a black undersuit so the white plates seem to float on black. Rex is a front-line soldier — a little grime and a few scuffs (a thin black/brown wash, dry-brushed edges) makes him look battle-tested rather than brand-new. Keep it subtle: a little grime says veteran, too much says you fell in mud.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Kama (Skirt)","body":"<p class='lead'>Officer signature.</p><p>Heavy fabric, blue trim, sits over the belt.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Twin Blasters","body":"<p class='lead'>TWIN DC-17 hand blaster pistols.</p><p>The dual-wield draw is Rex.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day","body":"<ul><li>Helmet polished, blue stripes clean.</li><li>Twin holsters secure.</li><li>Experience outranks everything.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;We're not droids. We're not programmed. You have to learn to make your own decisions.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; steady soldier voice — this is Rex's whole heart</i></li><li>&ldquo;Congratulations. You're not shinies anymore.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; proud grin, helmet under the arm</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>In my book, experience outranks everything — except pizza day.</li><li>Congratulations, shiny. You survived picture day.</li><li>This is Rex. The playground is secure. Repeat: the swings are ours.</li></ul></div><h3>The Soldier</h3><p>Rex isn't a faceless trooper — he's a leader who thinks for himself. Carry him that way: squared shoulders, steady stance — disciplined, not stiff — and the twin-blaster ready pose for photos. Rex respects experience over rank; play him as the calm, capable one who's seen it all and still shows up.</p>"}],"files":[{"name":"Phase II Clone helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=phase+ii+clone+helmet"},{"name":"Clone armour set (full)","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=phase%20ii%20clone%20armor"},{"name":"DC-17 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=dc-17+blaster"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Phase II helmet","detail":"Round, NOT Stormtrooper-shaped."},{"name":"Chest + back plate","detail":"Blue trim."},{"name":"Pauldrons (×2)","detail":"Blue accents."},{"name":"Vambraces (×2)","detail":"Plain white."},{"name":"Shin + knee plates","detail":"Blue stripes."},{"name":"Cod + thigh plates","detail":"White + blue."},{"name":"DC-17 blasters (×2)","detail":"Twin pistols."}],"buy":[{"name":"Black undersuit","detail":"Base layer."},{"name":"Twin holster belt","detail":"Two pistols."},{"name":"Tan/black gloves","detail":"Tactical."},{"name":"Tactical Kama","detail":"Officer skirt, blue trim."},{"name":"Boots","detail":"Hidden under shins."},{"name":"501st blue + white paint","detail":"Plus matte clear coat."}]}},"ventress":{"meta":{"word":"VENTRESS","accent":"#ddd0c0","body":"ventress","budget":160,"btn":"⚔ NIGHTSISTER","dur":"5 weeks","hrs":"15–30 hrs","parts":"Cloth + makeup + twin curved sabers","budgetRange":"€90–280","lead":"Asajj Ventress — Nightsister, Dooku's apprentice, the bald assassin with twin curved red sabers. A makeup-heavy build: pale grey-white skin and dark face markings.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"Bald head + pale skin + twin CURVED red sabers. The shaved head is non-negotiable to the look — use a bald cap.","intro":"OPERATION VENTRESS","introSub":"NIGHTSISTER · BUILD MANUAL · FILE ASAJJ","footer":"OPERATION VENTRESS · BUILD MANUAL · NIGHTSISTER OF DATHOMIR · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"ventress_public.pdf","weekPdf":"ventress_byweek.pdf","quote":"The Jedi shall fall."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Bald Cap + Markings","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Makeup","hours":4,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Bald cap + pale grey-white skin paint + thin dark tattoo lines down the head and brow.","tip":"Quality bald cap (latex/silicone) matters — cheap ones look fake.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Leather Halter Top","type":"TORSO · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Dark leather/pleather halter with strap detail. Edgy Sith-assassin look.","tip":"Black leather/pleather; armoured-style straps.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Ventress is leather + cloth.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Skin Paint Continuation","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Makeup","hours":2,"cost":10,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Pale skin paint continues to neck + arms + any showing midriff.","tip":"Set with translucent powder.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Twin Clips","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Belt with TWO clips for the curved sabers.","tip":"Twin clips — one each hip.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Lower Skirt","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Long dark hanging skirt panels.","tip":"Side-slit so legs show.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Long Cape (Clone Wars)","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Dark hooded cape (Clone Wars look).","tip":"Hood up for the entrance.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the 501st standards — Ventress is a Sith villain.","tip":"501st = bad guys.","files":[{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Dark Leggings","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tight black leggings or trousers.","tip":"Tight, dark, simple.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Tall Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tall black knee-high boots, riding-style.","tip":"Knee-high, dark.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Optional Gauntlets","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"LOW","description":"Optional dark fingerless gauntlets.","tip":"Skip for clean assassin look.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Twin Curved Red Sabers","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":4,"cost":120,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"TWO curved-hilt red lightsabers, one each hip. Often linked into the saber-staff.","tip":"Twin curved hilts — her signature.","files":[{"name":"Ventress curved saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ventress+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 1","task":"Plan + order bald cap, makeup, twin curved sabers, halter top"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Practice the bald cap application + skin paint"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Practice the dark tattoo markings"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Fit the halter + cape + belt + twin clips"},{"label":"Week 5","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Asajj Ventress</span> — Nightsister, ex-Sith, dark mercenary.</p><p>Heavy on makeup (bald cap + pale skin + tattoos) + leather + twin red sabers.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE TWO THINGS THAT MAKE HER</div><p>The bald pale head and the two curved sabers. Nail both and even a simple dark outfit underneath reads instantly as Ventress — skip either and the costume loses her. She starts as Count Dooku's deadly apprentice and, across her story, becomes something more complicated and her own person: proud and unbowed, answering to no one by the end.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Bald Cap","body":"<p class='lead'>Mandatory.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ QUALITY MATTERS</div>Get a silicone or latex bald cap from a costume supplier, not a cheap toy version. Glue carefully, blend with skin paint.</div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Skin & Markings","body":"<p class='lead'>Pale grey-white + dark line tattoos.</p><p>Practice the tattoo lines before the day — they curve down the head, around the eyes, and onto the cheeks.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">PATCH-TEST THE PAINT</div><p>Use skin-safe pale grey-white on the face, neck, and scalp, and set it with translucent powder so it doesn't smear through the day. Patch-test the face paint 24 hours early on a small area to be sure your skin is happy with it.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Outfit","body":"<p class='lead'>Black leather halter + leggings + tall boots.</p><p>Sith-assassin edge, not Jedi modesty.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">KEEP IT LEAN</div><p>Ventress is wiry and fast — don't bulk the silhouette. Fitted, layered, dark, and built for movement: layered wraps rather than bulky robes. The drama comes from the head and the blades, not from volume.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"Twin Curved Sabers","body":"<p class='lead'>Two curved red hilts.</p><p>Sometimes linked into a saber-staff. Twin clips on the belt.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Bald cap blend is everything.</li><li>Pale skin + dark tattoos.</li><li>Twin curved red.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Makashi (JarKai dual-blade)</span>, wielded dual JarKai.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ FORM II · MAKASHI (JARKAI DUAL-BLADE) — “The Way of the Ysalamiri”</div><p>Dooku's fencing form split across two blades — elegant thrusts and cutting ripostes arriving from angles a single saber can't cover. She duels like a dancer with a grudge: precise, mocking, always probing for the one opening she needs. Trained personally by Dooku, she took his aristocratic Makashi and doubled it — twin curved hilts, JarKai style, that link into a saberstaff when a duel turns serious.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#d42b2b\">⬤</span> Red — curved hilt — lead blade, right hip</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#d42b2b\">⬤</span> Red — curved hilt — off blade; the pair links end-to-end into a saberstaff</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">dual JarKai</span></div></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ MORE THAN ONE BLADE — THE CRAFT</div><ul><li>Lead blade attacks, off blade guards — never commit both at once.</li><li>Keep the blades out of each other's arc: figure-eights on opposite sides of the body, never crossing in front of your face.</li><li>Linked staff mode needs full 360-degree clearance — check your circle first, and never spin near people.</li></ul></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Slow fencing lunges with the lead blade while the off blade holds a high guard — ten each side, then swap lead hands. Ventress is ambidextrous, and JarKai only works if both hands are.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;The pleasure's all mine, my dear Obi-Wan. I've missed you.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; silky and mocking — enjoy every single word</i></li><li>&ldquo;Kenobi, don't tell me someone's finally knocked the fight out of you. Wake up.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; bored drawl with an eye-roll</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>The Jedi shall fall... right into my glitter trap.</li><li>Two lightsabers. Zero patience for broccoli.</li><li>Kenobi couldn't catch me. Good luck at tag.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Ventress curved saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ventress+lightsaber"},{"name":"Bald cap supplies","designer":"Pro makeup suppliers","url":"https://www.bensimage.com/category/bald-caps"},{"name":"Full Ventress costume","designer":"Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=ventress+cosplay"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Curved saber hilts (×2)","detail":"Or buy twin neopixel."}],"buy":[{"name":"Silicone/latex bald cap","detail":"Quality matters."},{"name":"Pale grey skin paint","detail":"Set with powder."},{"name":"Black tattoo liner","detail":"Practice the marking pattern."},{"name":"Leather halter top","detail":"Strap detail."},{"name":"Black leggings + tall boots","detail":"Tight, dark."},{"name":"Long dark skirt panels","detail":"Side-slit."},{"name":"Dark hooded cape","detail":"Clone Wars look."},{"name":"Belt with twin clips","detail":"Two sabers."}]}},"k2so":{"meta":{"word":"K-2SO","accent":"#4a5358","body":"k2so","budget":250,"btn":"⚔ RECRUIT","dur":"6 weeks","hrs":"30–60 hrs","parts":"Tall droid suit + head","budgetRange":"€120–300","lead":"K-2SO — the reprogrammed Imperial security droid from Rogue One and Andor. Tall, skeletal, dryly hilarious. A black/charcoal full-body droid suit with a printed head and glowing white eyes.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"K-2 is TALL. Add height with platform boots + posture; don't try stilts — dangerous.","intro":"OPERATION K-2SO","introSub":"REBEL ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE KX","footer":"OPERATION K-2SO · BUILD MANUAL · REPROGRAMMED · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"k2so_public.pdf","weekPdf":"k2so_byweek.pdf","quote":"Congratulations. You are being rescued."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Droid Head","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":12,"cost":45,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The angular charcoal head with the long jaw and the small inset eyes glowing cool white.","tip":"Print, sand, prime, paint charcoal with metallic weathering. Light the eyes with cool blue / blue-white LEDs.","files":[{"name":"K-2SO head STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=k-2so+head"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Plates","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":4,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Square angular shoulder armour, dark with mechanical details.","tip":"Foam-core if printing's too much.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Plate","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print + Foam","hours":8,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The flat angular chest with the central control panel and visible mechanical details.","tip":"Imperial-droid grey-black, weathered.","files":[{"name":"K-2SO chest STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=k-2so+armor"}]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Control Panel","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Print + LEDs","hours":3,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The lit control panel in the chest centre.","tip":"Small LEDs + black-painted housing.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Holster","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Simple dark belt with optional blaster holster.","tip":"K-2 is unarmed in most scenes; holster optional.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Hip Plates","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":3,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Angular dark hip plates.","tip":"Match the chest grey.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"No Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"K-2 has no cape — he's a droid.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — reprogrammed K-2 fights for the rebels.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Long Shin Plates","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print + Foam","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Long angular shin plates emphasising the height.","tip":"Tall and thin reads as droid.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Platform Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy/Mod","hours":3,"cost":60,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Platform boots to add the height. Plain black or modded.","tip":"Don't try stilts — dangerous.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Mechanical Hands","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Print + Buy","hours":4,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark gloves with printed knuckle armour suggesting mechanical fingers.","tip":"Articulated finger plates over plain gloves.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blaster (optional)","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"LOW","description":"Optional Imperial blaster.","tip":"K-2 is mostly unarmed; carry only for rescue scenes.","files":[{"name":"E-11 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=e-11+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Plan + order filament, charcoal paint, platform boots"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Print + finish the head — white eyes + weathering"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Chest, shoulders, hip plates"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Long shins + platform boots integration"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>K-2 is <span class='accent'>seven feet tall</span> in canon.</p><p>You're not. Use platform boots + good posture to suggest the height. Don't try stilts.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Head","body":"<p class='lead'>Angular, jaw-prominent, white-eyed.</p><p>Print, prime, paint charcoal, weather with light scratches and silver highlights, then white LEDs in the eyes.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">SEE AND BREATHE</div><p>You'll see out through the mouth grille or a hidden mesh panel — plan your eye-line and confirm you can see and breathe before finishing the head.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Body","body":"<p class='lead'>Skeletal, angular, dark.</p><p>The body is leaner than most Star Wars armour builds — use minimal padding.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"Height & Posture","body":"<p class='lead'>Hunch forward slightly with elbows out — K-2's posture is part of the silhouette.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ SAFETY</div>Platform boots OK with practice. Stilts are not safe — ever.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">A RAISED HEAD ADDS INCHES</div><p>An extended neck/head piece that sits above your own head adds safe inches and reads as droid proportions. Slim shapes help too — K-2 is gangly, not chunky, and slim, dark shapes make you look taller than bulk does. Build forearm or shin extensions light, and make sure you can still move and sit.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"Voice & Manner","body":"<p class='lead'>Optional but it sells it.</p><p>K-2 talks in a flat, dry deadpan. Practice the delivery.</p><h3>Move Like K-2</h3><p>Slightly stiff, mechanical movements — but loose-limbed and a bit awkward. Tilt the head when 'considering' something. He's a comedy character in a menacing frame: loom helpfully over shorter people and announce, deadpan, that they're being rescued.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Tall is the silhouette.</li><li>Charcoal, not black.</li><li>Eyes lit, head down.</li><li>Congratulations. You are being rescued.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I'll be there for you. Cassian said I had to.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; flat robot deadpan — the pause before 'Cassian said I had to' is the whole joke</i></li><li>&ldquo;I find that answer vague and unconvincing.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; arms crossed if you can, head tilted</i></li><li>&ldquo;The captain says you are a friend. I will not kill you.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; say it like it's the nicest compliment ever</i></li><li>&ldquo;Did you know that wasn't me?&rdquo; <i>&mdash; genuinely curious, slightly offended</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>There is a 97.6% chance you forgot your homework. I did the math.</li><li>Congratulations. You are being tidied. Your room, I mean.</li><li>I calculated the odds that this costume is awesome. They are excellent. You're welcome.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"K-2SO head STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=k-2so+head"},{"name":"K-2SO armour set","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=k-2so"},{"name":"Full K-2 costume","designer":"Etsy / eBay","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=k-2so+cosplay"},{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Droid head","detail":"Charcoal + white-LED eyes."},{"name":"Chest plate","detail":"Angular, central panel."},{"name":"Shoulder plates","detail":"Square."},{"name":"Long shins","detail":"Emphasise height."},{"name":"Hip plates","detail":"Match chest."},{"name":"Mechanical knuckle armour","detail":"Over plain gloves."}],"buy":[{"name":"Tight black undersuit","detail":"Base layer."},{"name":"Platform boots","detail":"Plain black."},{"name":"Charcoal grey paint","detail":"Plus silver weathering."},{"name":"White LEDs + battery","detail":"For the eyes."},{"name":"Dark gloves","detail":"Under knuckle armour."}]}},"ig11":{"meta":{"word":"IG-11","accent":"#a5acb3","body":"ig11","budget":280,"btn":"⚔ NURSE-DROID","dur":"6 weeks","hrs":"30–60 hrs","parts":"Tall droid suit + bare metal head","budgetRange":"€140–320","lead":"IG-11 — the reprogrammed bounty-hunter droid from The Mandalorian. Tall, cylindrical, with twin rifles and a distinctive narrow domed head. The good droid.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"IG-11's silhouette is THIN — narrow body, narrow head. Don't bulk up; he should look mechanical and spindly.","intro":"OPERATION IG-11","introSub":"GUILD ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE NURSE","footer":"OPERATION IG-11 · BUILD MANUAL · PROGRAMMED TO PROTECT · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"ig11_public.pdf","weekPdf":"ig11_byweek.pdf","quote":"I am no longer a hunter. I am a nurse droid."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Dome Head","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The narrow tall metal dome with the red-LED eye band around it. Sits HIGH above the shoulders.","tip":"The head sits on a long stalk — height matters.","files":[{"name":"IG-11 head STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ig-11+head"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Joints","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":4,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Cylindrical pivots at the shoulders, visible mechanical details.","tip":"Make them look like real joints, not pads.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Cylinder Body","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print + PVC","hours":10,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The tall metal cylindrical body — IG-11 is essentially a tall thin pillar.","tip":"PVC tube wrapped in printed plates is faster than full print.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Centre Detail","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Print + LEDs","hours":2,"cost":10,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Small lit panel on the centre of the cylinder.","tip":"Tiny detail; don't oversize.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Bandolier","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Crossing bandolier with ammunition + grenades.","tip":"Bounty-hunter detail — visible across the chest.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Waist Joint","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":3,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Visible mechanical waist pivot.","tip":"Joint detail, not armour.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"No Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"IG-11 is unclothed — he's a droid.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Mando Mercs standards (post-reprogramming, IG-11 is one of the good guys).","tip":"Mando Mercs has him as a Guild-era then ally character.","files":[{"name":"Mando Mercs","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Mechanical Legs","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print + PVC","hours":6,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Two thin cylindrical legs with visible joints at knee and ankle.","tip":"Thin, not bulky.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Platform Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy/Mod","hours":3,"cost":55,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Platform boots disguised as mechanical feet.","tip":"Don't try stilts.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Claw Hands","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":20,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Three-fingered mechanical claw hands — distinctive IG-series detail.","tip":"Print over gloves; the three-finger design is iconic.","files":[{"name":"IG-series claw STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ig+claw+hand"}]},"saber":{"name":"Twin Rifles (DLT-20A + E-11)","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":45,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Two DIFFERENT long rifles, dual-wielded: a DLT-20A blaster rifle and an E-11 medium blaster rifle. The dual-wield is essential to IG-11.","tip":"Two mismatched rifles — a DLT-20A in one claw, an E-11 in the other.","files":[{"name":"DLT-20A blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=dlt-20a+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Plan + order filament, PVC tube for body, platform boots, twin rifles"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Print + finish the dome head — red LED ring is the signature"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Cylindrical body + joints"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Thin legs + platform boot integration + bandolier"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>IG-11 is THIN and TALL.</p><p>Bulky armour ruins the silhouette. Use a PVC body tube with printed details — lighter and skinnier.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">SAFE HEIGHT, NOT STILTS</div><p>IG-11 towers over people — add that height the safe way: platform boots or built-up soles, a raised head piece above your own head, and slim vertical shapes, which read taller than bulk. Never use stilts — they're genuinely dangerous in a crowd. Boots plus posture give you plenty of height, safely.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Head","body":"<p class='lead'>Tall narrow dome + red LED ring around it.</p><p>The head sits on a stalk above the shoulders — don't shorten it.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">PLAN YOUR EYE-LINE</div><p>You'll see out through the receptor band or a hidden mesh strip — plan your eye-line and confirm vision and breathing before finishing the head.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Body","body":"<p class='lead'>Cylindrical, metal, joints visible.</p><p>PVC tube wrap with printed plates over it.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Claws","body":"<p class='lead'>Three-fingered claw hands.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ THE DETAIL</div>The three-finger claw is distinctive to IG-series droids. Don't substitute regular gloves.</div>"},{"num":"05","title":"Twin Rifles","body":"<p class='lead'>TWIN long DLT-20A rifles, one each hand.</p><p>The reverse-grip dual-wield is the iconic IG-11 pose.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Thin silhouette.</li><li>Red LED ring on the head.</li><li>Three-finger claws.</li><li>Programmed to nurse and protect.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I am not a living thing.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; calm and matter-of-fact — no drama at all</i></li><li>&ldquo;I must self-destruct.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; cheerfully unbothered, like announcing lunch</i></li><li>&ldquo;There is nothing to be sad about. I have never been alive.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; gentle, slow, the tearjerker — deliver it kindly</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I am no longer a bounty hunter. I am a snack-fetching droid.</li><li>Please do not be alarmed. I am programmed to protect this lunchbox.</li><li>Bedtime protocol initiated. Resistance is inefficient.</li></ul></div><h3>The Nurse, Not the Hunter</h3><p>IG-11 moves precisely and speaks in a calm, polite, matter-of-fact way. Keep movements smooth, deliberate, and mechanical; the head swivels independently, so a small head-turn 'scan' is pure IG-11. Lean into the gentle-protector arc — a towering droid offering politely to help is wonderfully on-character.</p>"}],"files":[{"name":"IG-11 head STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ig-11+head"},{"name":"IG-11 armour parts","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=ig-11"},{"name":"DLT-20A blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=dlt-20a+blaster"},{"name":"Mando Mercs","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Dome head","detail":"Red LED ring."},{"name":"Cylindrical body plates","detail":"Over a PVC tube."},{"name":"Three-finger claws","detail":"IG-series signature."},{"name":"Joint cylinders","detail":"Shoulders, waist, knees."},{"name":"DLT-20A rifles (×2)","detail":"Twin long rifles."}],"buy":[{"name":"PVC tube (body)","detail":"Light, thin."},{"name":"Platform boots","detail":"For height."},{"name":"Bare metal silver paint","detail":"Plus bronze weathering."},{"name":"Red LED ring + battery","detail":"Head signature."},{"name":"Bandolier","detail":"Visible across the chest."}]}},"cadbane":{"meta":{"word":"CAD BANE","accent":"#4a9eab","body":"cadbane","budget":150,"btn":"⚔ BOUNTY","dur":"5 weeks","hrs":"15–30 hrs","parts":"Cloth + makeup + hat + breathing tubes","budgetRange":"€80–250","lead":"Cad Bane — the Duros bounty hunter, the cool one in the wide-brimmed hat. Blue skin, long brown coat, twin LL-30 blasters, and the breathing tubes from chin to coat collar.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The hat + the breathing tubes + the blue skin = Cad Bane. Skipping the tubes makes him look like a generic cowboy with face paint.","intro":"OPERATION CAD BANE","introSub":"GUILD ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE BANE","footer":"OPERATION CAD BANE · BUILD MANUAL · ALWAYS GETS HIS MAN · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"cadbane_public.pdf","weekPdf":"cadbane_byweek.pdf","quote":"I'm your worst nightmare, pal."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Wide-Brim Hat","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Buy/Mod","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The signature flat wide-brim Duros hat. Dark, slightly battered.","tip":"Western-style hat works as a base; flatten the crown.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Blue Skin Paint","type":"HEAD · 02","kind":"Makeup","hours":3,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Skin-safe Duros-teal blue on face + neck + hands. Red Duros eyes (contacts).","tip":"Patch-test 24h before. Skin-safe only.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Cad is cloth + gear.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Vest + Shirt","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Dark vest over a dark shirt; western/spacer cut.","tip":"Black or dark grey.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Twin Holsters","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":28,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Wide bounty-hunter belt with TWO side holsters for the twin LL-30s.","tip":"Twin holsters, gun-slinger draw.","files":[{"name":"LL-30 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ll-30+blaster"}]},"codpiece":{"name":"Pouches","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Belt pouches for bounty kit.","tip":"Western-bounty feel.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Long Coat","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":55,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Long brown leather/canvas coat. The Cad Bane silhouette.","tip":"Hem mid-calf, brown.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Breathing Tubes","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Craft","hours":3,"cost":15,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"TWO breathing tubes from under the chin down to the coat collar / chest. Iconic detail.","tip":"Aquarium tubing painted dark + glued to the chin and coat.","files":[{"name":"Cad Bane breathing tube tutorial","designer":"cosplay tutorials","url":"https://www.google.com/search?q=cad+bane+breathing+tubes+tutorial"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Dark trousers tucked into the boots.","tip":"Plain.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tall brown leather western/spacer boots.","tip":"Brown to match the coat.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gauntlets + Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Print + Buy","hours":3,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wrist gauntlets (dart launcher, grappling line) + dark gloves.","tip":"Left gauntlet has the gadgets.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Twin LL-30 Blasters","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"TWIN LL-30 hand blasters — his signature western-style draw.","tip":"Twin holsters, gun-slinger draw.","files":[{"name":"LL-30 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ll-30+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 1","task":"Plan + order coat, hat, twin blasters, blue paint, tubing"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Practice the blue skin + red Duros eyes"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Build the breathing tubes from the chin down to the coat collar"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Holster rig + gauntlets"},{"label":"Week 5","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Cad Bane</span> — the cool bounty hunter, the Duros with the hat.</p><p>Cloth + makeup + the iconic breathing tubes.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The One Rule</div><p>The hat, the breathing tubes, and the blue skin together make Cad Bane. Skip the tubes and you're a cowboy with face paint; skip the hat and you're a blue alien. All three, and you're unmistakably the coolest bounty hunter in the galaxy.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Hat","body":"<p class='lead'>The silhouette starts here.</p><p>Wide flat brim. A western hat with the crown flattened works as a base.</p>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Blue Skin","body":"<p class='lead'>Duros teal-blue.</p><p>Skin-safe paint, face + neck + hands. Red contacts for eyes (costume contacts only, not on minors without an adult eye-care check).</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Breathing Tubes","body":"<p class='lead'>The forgotten detail that sells the costume.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ TWO TUBES</div>From just under the chin / cheek down to the inside of the coat collar. Aquarium tubing painted dark works perfectly.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Anchoring &amp; Comfort</div><p>Anchor the top ends near the jaw (spirit gum for skin, or attach to the hat band) and run them down into the coat collar. Make sure they don't pull on your skin or get in your mouth — comfort and safety first. A small, cheap detail with an enormous payoff.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"Twin Blasters","body":"<p class='lead'>TWIN LL-30s, western draw.</p><p>The gun-slinger pose is Cad.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Outfit Underneath</div><ul><li><strong>Long coat</strong> — a brown leather/canvas duster, mid-calf. The gunslinger silhouette.</li><li><strong>Vest + dark shirt</strong> — underneath, western-cut.</li><li><strong>Wide belt with twin holsters</strong> — for the two blasters.</li><li><strong>Tall boots + gloves</strong> — brown, scuffed.</li><li><strong>Wrist gauntlets</strong> — he carries gadgets (a dart launcher, a grappling line).</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Hat + tubes + blue.</li><li>Walk slow, talk slower.</li><li>Always get your man.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I'm in control. I make the rules now.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; slow gunslinger drawl, thumbs in belt</i></li><li>&ldquo;You've gone soft in your old age.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; taunting, half-smile under the hat brim</i></li><li>&ldquo;Consider this my final lesson. Look out for yourself. Anything else is weakness.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; quiet and cold — his duel speech from the Boba Fett finale</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I'm the fastest draw in this galaxy... at recess.</li><li>Name's Bane. I take on any job — even homework, for the right price.</li><li>I'd tip my hat to you, pal, but I never take off my hat.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"LL-30 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=ll-30+blaster"},{"name":"Cad Bane breathing tube tutorial","designer":"Cosplay forums","url":"https://www.google.com/search?q=cad+bane+breathing+tubes+tutorial"},{"name":"Full Cad costume","designer":"Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=cad+bane+cosplay"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"LL-30 blasters (×2)","detail":"Or buy a twin set."},{"name":"Wrist gauntlet gadgets","detail":"Optional."}],"buy":[{"name":"Wide-brim flat hat","detail":"Western base, modded."},{"name":"Duros-blue skin paint","detail":"Set with powder."},{"name":"Red costume contacts","detail":"Adult eye-care check first."},{"name":"Long brown coat","detail":"Mid-calf hem."},{"name":"Dark vest + shirt + trousers","detail":"Western/spacer feel."},{"name":"Twin holster belt","detail":"Two pistols."},{"name":"Brown boots + gloves","detail":"Match coat."},{"name":"Aquarium tubing","detail":"For breathing tubes."}]}},"armorer":{"meta":{"word":"ARMORER","accent":"#c4753a","body":"armorer","budget":350,"btn":"⚔ TRIBE","dur":"8 weeks","hrs":"50–100 hrs","parts":"Bronze Mandalorian armour + apron + tools","budgetRange":"€200–450","lead":"The Armorer — the leader of the Mandalorian covert, the smith of Beskar. Distinctive horned bronze helmet, heavy leather apron over Mando armour, hammer and tongs.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"BRONZE, not gold. The Armorer's signature colour is rich aged bronze — not shiny yellow gold.","intro":"OPERATION ARMORER","introSub":"TRIBE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE COVERT","footer":"OPERATION ARMORER · BUILD MANUAL · KEEPER OF THE FORGE · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"armorer_public.pdf","weekPdf":"armorer_byweek.pdf","quote":"A foundling is in your care."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Horned Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":14,"cost":45,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Mandalorian helmet with a cluster of FIVE horns on the dome (two larger front horns, two smaller mid horns, one small center horn), bronze finish, T-visor.","tip":"Five horns are the signature — get the count and placement right (see Mando Mercs CRL).","files":[{"name":"Armorer helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=armorer+helmet"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Pauldrons","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Bronze shoulder pauldrons.","tip":"Match the helmet bronze.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Bronze Chest","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The bronze chest plate, slightly different shape from Mando's.","tip":"Distinctive feminine cut compared to Mando.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Leather Apron","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":4,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"HEAVY brown leather smith's apron over the armour — the signature.","tip":"Real leather drapes best; pleather works for budget.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Tool Loops","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Belt over the apron with loops for the hammer and tongs.","tip":"Tool storage = forge worker.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Cod + Thigh Plates","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Bronze cod + thighs.","tip":"Match the chest..","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"No Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Armorer doesn't wear a cape.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Mando Mercs standards.","tip":"Mando Mercs = the Mandalorian club.","files":[{"name":"Mando Mercs","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin + Knee Plates","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Bronze shins + knees.","tip":"Both legs.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall dark boots.","tip":"Plain dark.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gauntlets + Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":5,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Bronze vambraces + heavy work gloves.","tip":"Smith gloves — thicker than Mando's.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Hammer + Tongs","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":4,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Smith's HAMMER + TONGS (not a blaster). The Armorer's identity is the forge.","tip":"Hammer + tongs = forge keeper.","files":[{"name":"Smith's hammer STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=blacksmith+hammer"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 8–7","task":"Plan + order filament, leather for apron, bronze paint"},{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Print + finish helmet — horns + bronze patina"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Chest, pauldrons, vambraces — all bronze"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Heavy leather apron + tool belt + smith tools"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Bronze patina + dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>The Armorer is a <span class='accent'>Mando build + a smith</span>.</p><p>Same armour family as Mando, in BRONZE, with the heavy leather apron over the top.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Bronze","body":"<p class='lead'>Aged bronze, not gold.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ PATINA</div>Start with bronze paint, then add a wash of dark green or black to settle into the recesses. That's what makes it look like a real ancient metal, not a yellow toy.</div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>Horns are the silhouette.</p><p>Two short horns rising from the top — don't omit them.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Horns Must Be Secure</div><p>Anchor the horns solidly — they're the silhouette, and you don't want one drooping mid-event. Build them light so they don't unbalance the helmet, and confirm you can see well through the T-visor before finishing.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Apron","body":"<p class='lead'>Heavy leather smith's apron over the chest plate.</p><p>Real leather drapes best. Heavy weight, brown, stained.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Fur Mantle</div><p>The shaggy fur cape across her shoulders is a signature — it reads 'smith and elder,' not 'soldier.' Use a faux-fur piece that drapes over the shoulders and upper back. It also helpfully covers the tops of the pauldrons and any strap-work.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Tools","body":"<p class='lead'>Hammer + tongs.</p><p>The Armorer's identity. Carry them visibly — they're the costume's purpose.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Bronze Patina Method","body":"<p class='lead'>Bronze base → black/green wash → dry-brush metallic high spots → sealer.</p><p>The result reads as ancient ceremonial bronze, not a costume colour.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Bronze, not gold.</li><li>Horns up.</li><li>Apron heavy.</li><li>Hammer and tongs always visible.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Play Her Grave</div><p>The Armorer is grave, ceremonial, and wise. Move slow and deliberate — she speaks the Creed. Hold the tongs or hammer as if you've used them ten thousand times. She pairs beautifully with a Mando (Din Djarin) — smith and foundling — and belongs with the Mando Mercs, the Mandalorian costuming club.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;This is the Way.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; solemn, slow nod — everyone nearby must repeat it back</i></li><li>&ldquo;You are a clan of two.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; quiet and formal, like handing over something precious</i></li><li>&ldquo;When one chooses to walk the Way of the Mandalore, you are both hunter and prey.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; measured forge-speech rhythm, never hurried</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>You have eaten your vegetables. This is the Way.</li><li>A backpack is in your care. Guard it well.</li><li>I have forged this armor from cardboard. It is still the Way.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Armorer helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=armorer+helmet"},{"name":"Mandalorian armour set","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=mandalorian%20armor"},{"name":"Smith's tools STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=blacksmith+hammer"},{"name":"Mando Mercs","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Horned helmet","detail":"Bronze + green patina."},{"name":"Chest plate","detail":"Match the bronze."},{"name":"Pauldrons (×2)","detail":"Same bronze."},{"name":"Vambraces (×2)","detail":"Bronze."},{"name":"Shin + knee plates","detail":"Both legs."},{"name":"Cod + thigh plates","detail":"Same bronze."},{"name":"Hammer + tongs","detail":"Forge tools."}],"buy":[{"name":"Heavy brown leather apron","detail":"Real leather drapes best."},{"name":"Tall dark boots","detail":"Plain."},{"name":"Heavy work gloves","detail":"Thicker than Mando."},{"name":"Bronze paint + green wash","detail":"For patina effect."},{"name":"Tool belt + loops","detail":"To carry hammer + tongs."}]}},"sabine":{"meta":{"word":"SABINE","accent":"#7a5dbc","body":"sabine","budget":280,"btn":"⚔ REBEL","dur":"7 weeks","hrs":"30–60 hrs","parts":"Painted Mandalorian armour + twin pistols","budgetRange":"€160–350","lead":"Sabine Wren — the Mandalorian artist, painter, demolitionist. Colourful graffiti-painted armour, twin blaster pistols. The most personal armour in the line: YOU paint it.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The armour is YOUR canvas. Paint it however YOU want — that's the whole point of Sabine.","intro":"OPERATION SABINE","introSub":"REBEL ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE WREN","footer":"OPERATION SABINE · BUILD MANUAL · PAINT IT YOUR WAY · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"sabine_public.pdf","weekPdf":"sabine_byweek.pdf","quote":"Forget the explosion. Look at the color."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Painted Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print + Paint","hours":14,"cost":45,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Mandalorian T-visor helmet, painted with whatever design YOU want — violet/orange/teal stripes are Rebels-era; magenta/orange is later.","tip":"Helmet design is YOUR signature. Plan + sketch first.","files":[{"name":"Mando helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=mandalorian+helmet+sabine"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Pauldrons","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Two pauldrons — painted to match YOUR helmet design.","tip":"One pauldron usually has a graffiti tag or symbol.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Plate","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print","hours":8,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Chest + back plates, painted in YOUR colour scheme.","tip":"Bold colour blocks read best from a distance.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Flight Suit","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark grey/black flight suit base under the armour.","tip":"Plain so the painted armour pops.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Holsters","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tactical belt with TWO side holsters for the twin WESTAR-35s.","tip":"Twin blasters like Bo-Katan.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Cod + Thigh Plates","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Painted to match.","tip":"More canvas for art.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"No Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Sabine doesn't wear a cape.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Mando Mercs standards (Sabine is recognised; bring photos of YOUR design).","tip":"Mando Mercs has flexible standards for Sabine because of the paint variation.","files":[{"name":"Mando Mercs","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin + Knee Plates","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Painted shins + knees, both legs.","tip":"More canvas.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall dark boots.","tip":"Plain so the legs pop.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gauntlets + Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":5,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Painted vambraces (left with gadgets) + tactical gloves.","tip":"More canvas.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Twin WESTAR-35 Blasters","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Twin WESTAR-35 pistols, one each hip.","tip":"Twin blasters are Sabine.","files":[{"name":"WESTAR-35 STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=westar-35+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 7–6","task":"Plan + SKETCH the paint scheme + order filament, flight suit, twin blasters"},{"label":"Weeks 5–4","task":"Print all armour parts (paint LAST)"},{"label":"Weeks 3–2","task":"Sand glass-smooth + prime EVERYTHING"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"PAINT — mask + paint in colour blocks; add graffiti tags last"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Clear coat + dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>The most <span class='accent'>personal</span> build in the line.</p><p>Mandalorian armour base, then YOU paint it. The paint is the costume.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Era","body":"<ul><li><b>Rebels-era</b> — violet helmet + orange pauldron + Rebels graffiti.</li><li><b>Ahsoka-era</b> — magenta/orange, more graffiti symbols.</li><li><b>Your own</b> — yes, that's authentic Sabine. Paint it YOUR way.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Match the Hair</div><p>Sabine's hair changes as often as her armour — purple, orange, blue, and more, in various short styles. A coloured wig is the easy route and lets you match your paint scheme. She often wears the helmet pushed up or carried, so the hair shows — pick a colour that ties the whole look together.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"Sketch First","body":"<p class='lead'>Before you paint, SKETCH.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ PLAN ON PAPER</div>Print blank helmet/armour outlines, sketch the design with markers. Test it before committing paint.</div>"},{"num":"04","title":"Paint Method","body":"<p class='lead'>Smooth → prime → base → mask → colour blocks → graffiti → clear coat.</p><p>Patience pays here. Take your time on every step.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"Twin Blasters","body":"<p class='lead'>WESTAR-35s, one each hip.</p><p>Same family as Bo-Katan's twins.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Optional: Darksaber &amp; Jetpack</div><p>In later stories Sabine wields the black-bladed Darksaber — a striking optional prop (search 'Darksaber STL'); set the blade black/white. A light foam jetpack, like the other Mandos, is another optional add. Check your event's prop rules for any blasters or sabers.</p></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"The Graffiti","body":"<p class='lead'>Tags + symbols on top of the colour blocks.</p><p>Use white paint markers; add a Mandalorian crest or your own personal sigil.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Starbird</div><p>The starbird — the rebel phoenix — is a signature Sabine motif worth including. And give the helmet the boldest design of all: it's the centrepiece of the art.</p></div>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Sketch first.</li><li>Bold colour blocks.</li><li>Graffiti symbols last.</li><li>Going down swinging.</li></ul>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Pretty gutsy move, kid. If the big guy catches you, he'll end you.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; her very first line to Ezra — smirk, totally unimpressed</i></li><li>&ldquo;What does it look like? Art.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; shrug, spray-can flourish</i></li><li>&ldquo;The Empire wanted to destroy worlds. And they did. They destroyed mine.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; the serious one — drop the smirk, let it land</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I don't make messes. I make masterpieces.</li><li>Sure, I could use just one color. But why would I ever do that?</li><li>My homework isn't late — it's a limited-edition art drop.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Mando helmet STL (Sabine)","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=mandalorian+helmet+sabine"},{"name":"Sabine armour set","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=sabine%20wren"},{"name":"WESTAR-35 blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=westar-35+blaster"},{"name":"Mando Mercs","designer":"mandalorianmercs.org","url":"https://www.mandalorianmercs.org/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Helmet","detail":"Painted YOUR way."},{"name":"Chest + back plate","detail":"Bold colour blocks."},{"name":"Pauldrons (×2)","detail":"One with a tag."},{"name":"Vambraces (×2)","detail":"Left has gadgets."},{"name":"Shin + knee plates","detail":"Both legs."},{"name":"Cod + thigh plates","detail":"Match."},{"name":"WESTAR-35 blasters (×2)","detail":"Twin pistols."}],"buy":[{"name":"Dark flight suit","detail":"Plain base."},{"name":"Twin holster belt","detail":"Two blasters."},{"name":"Tall dark boots + gloves","detail":"Tactical."},{"name":"Acrylic paints in YOUR colours","detail":"Plus white paint marker for graffiti."},{"name":"Masking tape + sandpaper","detail":"For clean colour blocks."}]}},"hera":{"meta":{"word":"HERA","accent":"#5a8a55","body":"hera","budget":140,"btn":"⚔ GHOST","dur":"4 weeks","hrs":"10–20 hrs","parts":"Cloth + makeup + lekku","budgetRange":"€70–220","lead":"Hera Syndulla — the Twi'lek rebel pilot, Captain of the Ghost. Light green skin, gold/tan flight suit, twin head-tails (lekku) with the iconic off-white pilot cap and goggles.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The off-white flight cap + goggles are what make her read as Hera, not a generic Twi'lek. Her lekku drape back over the shoulders; the cap simply sits over them.","intro":"OPERATION HERA","introSub":"GHOST ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE SYNDULLA","footer":"OPERATION HERA · BUILD MANUAL · CAPTAIN OF THE GHOST · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"hera_public.pdf","weekPdf":"hera_byweek.pdf","quote":"We have hope; hope that things can get better. And they will."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Flight Cap + Lekku","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Craft","hours":8,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The off-white/cream pilot cap/headpiece on top + two head-tails (lekku) coming out the back and draping over the shoulders.","tip":"Cap fits like a beanie and sits over the lekku — it doesn't restrain them. Add the aviator goggles up on the cap.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Green Skin Paint","type":"HEAD · 02","kind":"Makeup","hours":3,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Skin-safe light green paint on face + neck + hands, matching the lekku.","tip":"Patch-test. Set with powder. Match the lekku to the same light green.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Hera is cloth + makeup.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Gold/Tan Flight Suit","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":55,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"One-piece gold/tan/mustard-orange jumpsuit cut for Hera. Loosely pilot-inspired (her pants use X-wing flight-suit material) but NOT bright safety-orange.","tip":"Gold/tan ochre, jumpsuit cut — not bright orange.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Holster","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Belt plus a low holster for the holdout blaster, worn on the lower right leg/boot (cross-draw).","tip":"Holster sits low on the right leg/boot, not the hip.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Pouches","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":10,"priority":"LOW","description":"Pilot belt pouches.","tip":"Practical, not decorative.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"No Cape","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Hera flies; no cape.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Hera is a Rebel pilot.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Flight Suit Legs","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Part of the one-piece flight suit — doesn't need separate trousers.","tip":"Tucks into boots.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Pilot Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":45,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Tall brown leather pilot boots over the flight suit cuffs.","tip":"Brown, knee-high.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Pilot Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Brown leather pilot gloves — fingerless or full.","tip":"Both hands.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blaster","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Hera carries a small Blurrg-1120 holdout blaster — a compact concealable sidearm, not a heavy pistol.","tip":"Small holdout pistol, holstered low on the right leg/boot.","files":[{"name":"Rebel pilot blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=rebel+pilot+blaster"}]},"flightvestshoulder":{"name":"Flight Vest + Shoulder Pads","type":"BODY · 13","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":4,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Fitted brown leather flight vest / chest harness with detail lines, plus matching brown leather shoulder pads. This is one of her most identifying pieces.","tip":"Brown leather, fitted over the flight suit. Reference the Rebel Legion CRL for the detail lines.","files":[]},"aviatorgoggles":{"name":"Aviator Goggles","type":"HEAD · 14","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":15,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Brown-base aviator goggles with tinted lenses, worn up on the off-white cap. Reads instantly as Hera together with the headpiece.","tip":"Brown straps, tinted lenses — sit them on the cap, not over the eyes.","files":[]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 4","task":"Plan + order flight suit, green skin paint, lekku materials"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Build the lekku + flight-cap headpiece"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Practice the green skin + makeup"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Hera Syndulla</span> — the Twi'lek rebel pilot, captain of the Ghost.</p><p>Green skin + gold/tan flight suit + the flight-cap + lekku rig.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Headpiece","body":"<p class='lead'>Flight cap on top, lekku coming out the back.</p><p>The cap is a beanie-shape; the lekku attach inside the back hem and drape forward over the shoulders.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Goggles</div><p>The single most recognisable Hera detail: aviator-style flight goggles with orange/amber lenses, worn pushed up on the forehead between the lekku, over the fitted flight cap. This is the detail that says 'Hera' before anything else — don't skip or hide them.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Green Skin","body":"<p class='lead'>Sage / olive green.</p><p>Hera's green is darker than typical alien-green — closer to olive. Patch test.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Match the Lekku</div><p>Paint the face, neck, and hands, and match the lekku colour exactly — then add her subtle darker markings with a fine brush. Build the lekku light and anchored, or your neck will tire by mid-event.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Flight Suit","body":"<p class='lead'>Gold/tan, Rebel-pilot style.</p><p>Standard rebel pilot suits work; Hera's is gold/tan, not the bright orange of Luke's X-wing suit.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Gear","body":"<p class='lead'>Belt + holster + pilot boots.</p><p>Practical pilot kit — not flashy.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Cap + lekku as one unit.</li><li>Olive-green skin.</li><li>Gold/tan jumpsuit.</li><li>We have hope.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Play the Captain</div><p>Calm, capable, in command — Hera keeps her head when everyone else loses theirs. Warm but firm: she's the crew's anchor. Goggles up, confident pilot's stance. She belongs in the Rebel Legion (the heroes' club) and pairs beautifully with a whole Ghost crew.</p></div>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;If all you do is fight for your own life, then your life is worth nothing.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; calm captain voice — steady, no shouting</i></li><li>&ldquo;Once a rebel, always a rebel.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; quick and proud, with a small grin</i></li><li>&ldquo;It doesn't matter where we come from, Admiral. Our will to be free is what's going to beat you.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; her big line to Thrawn — level stare, zero fear</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I've flown through asteroid fields calmer than this cafeteria.</li><li>This is your captain speaking: recess is now extended. Spectres, move out!</li><li>Chopper tidied his room faster than this — and Chopper never listens.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Rebel pilot blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=rebel+pilot+blaster"},{"name":"Twi'lek lekku tutorial","designer":"YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=twi%27lek+lekku+tutorial"},{"name":"Full Hera costume","designer":"Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=hera+syndulla+cosplay"},{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Blaster (optional)","detail":"Or buy a Rebel-pilot style."}],"buy":[{"name":"Gold/tan Rebel-pilot flight suit","detail":"One-piece, bright."},{"name":"Olive-green skin paint","detail":"Set with powder."},{"name":"Flight cap (off-white)","detail":"Beanie base."},{"name":"Lekku materials","detail":"Foam tubes + green fabric, inside cap."},{"name":"Tall brown pilot boots","detail":"Knee-high."},{"name":"Brown pilot gloves","detail":"Both hands."},{"name":"Tactical belt + holster","detail":"Left hip."}]}},"revan":{"meta":{"word":"REVAN","accent":"#7a1f24","body":"revan","budget":200,"btn":"⚔ OLD REPUBLIC","dur":"7 weeks","hrs":"30–60 hrs","parts":"Mandalorian mask + red robes + saber","budgetRange":"€120–350","lead":"Revan — the legendary Old Republic Jedi-turned-Sith-turned-Jedi from KOTOR. The weathered grey-and-rust-red Mandalorian mask + dark red hooded robes over a cuirass + the red lightsaber. Pairs perfectly with Nihilus.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The mask is a MANDALORIAN T-visor, not a generic mask: dark grey with rust-red detailing, heavily weathered, with two chin prongs. That weathered grey-and-rust-red look is the Revan signature.","intro":"OPERATION REVAN","introSub":"OLD REPUBLIC · BUILD MANUAL · FILE PRODIGAL","footer":"OPERATION REVAN · BUILD MANUAL · THE PRODIGAL KNIGHT · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 9 TOTAL","pubPdf":"revan_public.pdf","weekPdf":"revan_byweek.pdf","quote":"I am Revan reborn. And before me you are nothing."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Mandalorian Mask","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":10,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Revan's iconic T-visor mask: dark grey with rust-red detailing, heavily weathered, with two chin prongs and a dark eye-slit lens.","tip":"Weather it heavily — grey base, rust-red panels. (SWTOR-era look adds a vertical scar across the left eye slit; optional.)","files":[{"name":"Revan mask STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=revan+mask"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Wraps","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Sew","hours":2,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark fabric shoulder pieces under the robe — not separate pauldrons.","tip":"Part of the robe construction.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Cuirass + Ab Plate","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print + Foam","hours":8,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Revan wears his robes OVER rigid armour: a chest cuirass plus abdominal plate worn under the cloak. Dark plates with bronze/copper-toned trim (the SWTOR redesign leans more overt bronze/copper).","tip":"Foam or print the cuirass; the robe sits over it. Bronze/copper accents read as Revan.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Inner Tunic","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Dark red/grey layered tunic under the outer robe.","tip":"Layered: black under, dark red over.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Wide Belt + Clip","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide black leather belt with a saber clip.","tip":"Same family as Sith..","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Sash","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Dark sash across the waist.","tip":"Old Republic style.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Dark Red Hooded Cloak","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":4,"cost":55,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Floor-length dark red hooded cloak. Heavier and more structured than a Jedi robe.","tip":"Wine red, not orange-red. Hood up for the entrance.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Revan is from KOTOR (game era); 501st recognises him as a Sith.","tip":"Niche but recognised.","files":[{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Dark trousers under the robe.","tip":"Hidden by the floor-length cloak.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Tall Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall dark boots, mostly hidden.","tip":"Plain.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gauntlets + Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Print + Buy","hours":3,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark vambraces + black gloves on both hands.","tip":"Old Republic gauntlets are simpler than later eras.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Red Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":70,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Red blade. The hilt is OLD-REPUBLIC style — chunkier, more rectangular than later sabers.","tip":"Old Republic hilts have a distinct blocky shape. Revan's colours ran blue (Jedi) then red (Sith) then purple (reborn) — red is the pick for this dark-side look.","files":[{"name":"Old Republic saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=old+republic+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 7–6","task":"Plan + order filament, dark red fabric, mask print"},{"label":"Weeks 5–4","task":"Print + finish the mask — crossed red+grey pattern"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Sew the dark red hooded cloak"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Layered inner tunic + belt + saber"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Revan</span> — the legendary Old Republic Sith/Jedi from KOTOR.</p><p>The iconic grey-and-rust-red Mandalorian mask + dark red hooded robes + a red blade.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Mask","body":"<p class='lead'>It's a MANDALORIAN T-visor, painted with a crossed red+grey pattern.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ THE PATTERN</div>Black base, then red on the visor sides, then grey lines forming the crossed pattern across the brow and cheeks. Reference images are essential.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Eyes &amp; Fit</div><p>Back the eye openings with dark mesh you can see through, and confirm vision before finishing. The mask sits inside the deep hood, so leave room for both — the hood frames the mask.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Robes","body":"<p class='lead'>Floor-length dark RED hooded cloak.</p><p>Wine red, not bright. Heavier than a Jedi robe.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">The Layers</div><ul><li><strong>Inner robe/tunic</strong> — dark red, layered.</li><li><strong>Hooded outer robe</strong> — the deep hood frames the mask.</li><li><strong>The cape</strong> — long and flowing, often with a structured collar, over the robe. It gives Revan that heroic, dramatic movement — lose the cape and you lose the legend.</li><li><strong>Wide belt + sash</strong> — dark, with a clip for the saber.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"Old Republic Era","body":"<p class='lead'>Everything is slightly chunkier than modern Star Wars.</p><p>The mask, the saber hilt, the gauntlets — all blockier and more medieval-feeling than later eras.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"Pair with Nihilus","body":"<p class='lead'>If you have a friend building Nihilus, you have an instant KOTOR mini-line.</p><p>The masks pair perfectly: bone-white Nihilus + red-and-grey Revan.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"The Lightsaber","body":"<p class='lead'>Red blade, blocky Old Republic hilt.</p><p>Not the sleeker modern designs.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Mask: crossed red+grey on black.</li><li>Wine red robe, hooded.</li><li>Old Republic = blockier.</li><li>I am Revan reborn.</li></ul><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">Move Like a Legend</div><p>Tall, composed, unhurried — Revan has seen and done everything. Let the cape and robes flow; turn slowly so they move. The masked stare needs no expression — stillness reads as power. Hood up, mask forward: the reveal is just standing there.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Old Republic style</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · OLD REPUBLIC STYLE</div><p>Four thousand years before the films, the seven forms weren't yet carved in stone — Revan fought as a strategist, folding saber work, Force mastery, and battlefield cunning into a single weapon. Reads closest to Form VI Niman, the balanced blend that trades flash for total flexibility. No source pins Revan to a numbered form — the Revanchist rewrote every rulebook he touched, so an unclassifiable Old Republic style is the honest answer.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#d0312d\">⬤</span> Red — chunky rectangular Old Republic hilt — the Dark Lord's blade</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Alternate one saber cut with one open-palm Force-push gesture, blade-power-blade — Revan's rhythm is never just the sword. Keep the footwork square and the mask facing forward.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I've saved the Republic twice before. I've fought Mandalores and armies of the dark side. You won't stop me.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; from The Old Republic — build it up so the last four words land like thunder</i></li><li>&ldquo;I am Darth Revan, Dark Lord of the Sith. Those who use the dark side are also bound to serve it.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; from his holocron — slow and deep, let the mask do the work</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I forgot my own name once. Forgetting my homework? Rookie stuff.</li><li>I have returned... from the lunch line. And before me, these fries are nothing.</li><li>Some call me a hero. Some call me a villain. My teacher calls me 'late.'</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Revan mask STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=revan+mask"},{"name":"Old Republic saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=old+republic+lightsaber"},{"name":"Full Revan cosplay reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=revan"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Revan mask","detail":"Black + crossed red+grey pattern."},{"name":"Old Republic saber hilt","detail":"Blocky."}],"buy":[{"name":"Floor-length dark RED hooded cloak","detail":"Wine red, not bright."},{"name":"Black/dark red layered inner tunic","detail":"Layered."},{"name":"Wide black leather belt + clip","detail":"Old Republic style."},{"name":"Dark trousers + tall boots","detail":"Hidden under robe."},{"name":"Black gloves","detail":"Both hands."},{"name":"Mask paints","detail":"Black + red + grey for the pattern."}]}},"plokoon":{"meta":{"word":"PLO KOON","accent":"#a84e2e","body":"plokoon","budget":160,"btn":"⚔ JEDI","dur":"5 weeks","hrs":"18–35 hrs","parts":"Jedi robes + antiox mask","budgetRange":"€90–260","lead":"Plo Koon — the Kel Dor Jedi Master, the one in the breathing mask and goggles. Brown Jedi robes, the distinctive antiox mask + protective goggles, and a blue blade.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The antiox mask + goggles ARE Plo Koon. Kel Dor can't breathe our air — without the mask he's just a robed Jedi.","intro":"OPERATION PLO KOON","introSub":"JEDI ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE KEL DOR","footer":"OPERATION PLO KOON · BUILD MANUAL · MASTER OF THE COUNCIL · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"plokoon_public.pdf","weekPdf":"plokoon_byweek.pdf","quote":"When you ask for trouble, you should not be surprised when it finds you."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Antiox Mask + Goggles","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print + Craft","hours":12,"cost":55,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The breathing mask covering nose + mouth, plus the round protective goggles over the eyes. The full face is covered.","tip":"Print the mask + goggles; use opaque smoked lenses so the eyes are not visible behind them.","files":[{"name":"Plo Koon mask STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=plo+koon+mask"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Robe Shoulders","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Sew","hours":2,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The Jedi robe drapes over the shoulders.","tip":"Part of the robe.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Plo Koon is robes.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Tunic + Tabards","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Layered brown/tan Jedi tunic with the crossed front tabards.","tip":"Classic Jedi layering.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Obi (Belt)","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide Jedi belt with saber clip.","tip":"Leather, brown.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Tabard Drape","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Sew","hours":1,"cost":10,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"The tabards continue past the belt.","tip":"Hangs front + back.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Brown Jedi Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":45,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Hooded brown outer robe over everything.","tip":"Hood usually down for Plo.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Plo Koon is a Jedi hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Brown trousers under the robe.","tip":"Hidden mostly.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall brown leather boots.","tip":"Riding-style.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Clawed Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy/Mod","hours":2,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Kel Dor have clawed hands — gloves with sculpted claw tips.","tip":"Add sculpted claws to brown gloves.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blue Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":60,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Plo Koon's blade is BLUE.","tip":"Clean cylindrical Jedi hilt, blue blade.","files":[{"name":"Plo Koon saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=plo+koon+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 1","task":"Plan + order robe, mask print, goggles, blue saber"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Print + finish the antiox mask + goggles"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Fit the Jedi layers + tabards"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Add clawed gloves + boots + saber clip"},{"label":"Week 5","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Plo Koon</span> — the Kel Dor Jedi Master in the breathing mask.</p><p>Standard Jedi robes + the signature antiox mask + goggles.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Mask","body":"<p class='lead'>The whole face is covered.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ MASK + GOGGLES</div>Breathing mask over nose and mouth, round protective goggles over the eyes. Kel Dor can't breathe oxygen — this is life support, not decoration.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">BUILD &amp; FIT</div><p>3D print or foam-build the mask + goggle assembly. Smooth, prime, and paint it the grey-bronze of his antiox mask, with smoked lenses over the eyes — the eyes can glow faintly behind tinted lenses for a great effect. The whole face is covered, so plan your vision and airflow carefully, and confirm you can see and breathe easily before you finish. Comfort first, always.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Robes","body":"<p class='lead'>Classic brown Jedi layering.</p><p>Tunic, crossed tabards, obi belt, hooded outer robe.</p><h3>Hood Down</h3><p>Plo usually wears the hood down so the mask shows.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"Kel Dor Details","body":"<p class='lead'>Clawed hands.</p><p>Add sculpted claw tips to brown gloves — a small detail that sells the species.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>Blue blade.</p><p>Clean Jedi hilt.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Mask + goggles cover the full face.</li><li>Brown Jedi layers.</li><li>Clawed gloves.</li><li>Blue blade.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Unrecorded (Master's blend)</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · UNRECORDED (MASTER'S BLEND)</div><p>Screen canon never names his form, but everything he does reads closest to Form V Shien/Djem So — planted stance, heavy deflections, answering pressure with pressure. Calm as the mask suggests: he doesn't chase a fight, he ends one. He fights the way he sits on the Council — unhurried, protective, immovable — with famous bare-handed skill backing up the blade.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#2f7de0\">⬤</span> Blue — blue on screen; some old Legends comics drew it orange-yellow</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Hold one planted low guard and run three-part deflection sweeps — left, right, overhead — returning to the exact same stance every time. The feet barely move; the blade does all the work.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Not to me.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; the legendary reply when a clone says clones are meant to be expendable — quiet, kind, unforgettable</i></li><li>&ldquo;Your emotions are clouding your judgment.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; gentle, never scolding</i></li><li>&ldquo;There he goes again, craving adventure and excitement.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; dry amusement — said watching Anakin fly off</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I never leave anyone behind. Especially not at recess.</li><li>When you ask for extra homework, you should not be surprised when it finds you.</li><li>Yes, I wear goggles indoors. When you're this wise, the future looks bright.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Plo Koon mask STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=plo+koon+mask"},{"name":"Plo Koon saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=plo+koon+lightsaber"},{"name":"Jedi robe pattern","designer":"Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=jedi+robe+pattern"},{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Antiox mask","detail":"Covers nose + mouth."},{"name":"Protective goggles","detail":"Smoked lenses."},{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Blue blade."}],"buy":[{"name":"Brown Jedi tunic + tabards","detail":"Layered."},{"name":"Obi belt + saber clip","detail":"Brown leather."},{"name":"Hooded brown outer robe","detail":"Hood usually down."},{"name":"Brown trousers + tall boots","detail":"Riding-style."},{"name":"Gloves + sculpted claws","detail":"Kel Dor hands."},{"name":"Blue lightsaber","detail":"Clean hilt."}]}},"kitfisto":{"meta":{"word":"KIT FISTO","accent":"#3d9b7a","body":"kitfisto","budget":170,"btn":"⚔ JEDI","dur":"5 weeks","hrs":"18–35 hrs","parts":"Green skin + head-tentacles + green saber","budgetRange":"€90–280","lead":"Kit Fisto — the Nautolan Jedi Master, the cheerful one with the head-tentacles and the famous smile. Green skin, the long Nautolan tentacles, minimal Jedi gear, and a green blade.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The head-tentacles + green skin = Kit Fisto. The tentacles are heavy — build them light and anchor them well.","intro":"OPERATION KIT FISTO","introSub":"JEDI ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE NAUTOLAN","footer":"OPERATION KIT FISTO · BUILD MANUAL · THE SMILING JEDI · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"kitfisto_public.pdf","weekPdf":"kitfisto_byweek.pdf","quote":"Revenge is not the Jedi way!"},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Head-Tentacles (Lekku)","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Craft","hours":10,"cost":50,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The thick Nautolan head-tentacles — fourteen of them — falling back and over the shoulders. Green, sensory.","tip":"Foam-stuffed fabric tubes on a snug green skullcap; lighter is better.","files":[{"name":"Nautolan tentacle tutorial","designer":"YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=nautolan+head+tentacles"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Green Skin Paint","type":"HEAD · 02","kind":"Makeup","hours":3,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Skin-safe sea-green on face, neck, arms, hands. Big black Nautolan eyes (contacts optional).","tip":"Patch-test. Set with powder.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Kit is light Jedi gear.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Sleeveless Tunic","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Kit's brown sleeveless/short-sleeve tunic — he shows his green arms.","tip":"Bare arms are part of the look.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Saber Clip","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Brown Jedi belt with saber clip.","tip":"Standard Jedi belt.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Tabard Drape","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Sew","hours":1,"cost":10,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Front tabard panel.","tip":"Hangs from the belt.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"No Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Kit usually goes without an outer robe — he's a swimmer.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Kit Fisto is a Jedi hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Brown trousers.","tip":"Tucked into boots.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Brown leather boots.","tip":"Standard Jedi boots.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Bare Hands","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Kit shows his green webbed hands — skin paint only.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Green Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":60,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Kit's blade is GREEN.","tip":"Green blade, clean Jedi hilt.","files":[{"name":"Kit Fisto saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=kit+fisto+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 1","task":"Plan + order green paint, tentacle materials, tunic, green saber"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Build the head-tentacle headpiece (light + anchored)"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Practice the green skin + big-eye look"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Fit the sleeveless tunic + belt"},{"label":"Week 5","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Kit Fisto</span> — the cheerful Nautolan Jedi.</p><p>Green skin + the head-tentacles + minimal Jedi gear + a green blade. And the smile.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Head-Tentacles","body":"<p class='lead'>The big build.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ LIGHT + ANCHORED</div>Fourteen tentacles is a lot of weight. Build them hollow/foam-stuffed and anchor to a snug skullcap, or you'll get a headache by lunch.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">SHAPE &amp; COLOUR</div><p>The tentacles taper toward the ends and drape naturally back and over the shoulders. Match the green to your skin paint exactly so the head reads as one creature — and it's better to have slightly fewer, lighter tentacles than a heavy full set you can't wear all day.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Green Skin","body":"<p class='lead'>Sea-green, skin-safe.</p><p>Face, neck, arms, hands — Kit shows a lot of skin. Big black Nautolan eyes with contacts (optional).</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">SKIN-SAFE GREEN</div><p>Use skin-safe theatrical paint set with translucent powder, and patch-test the paint 24 hours early. If costume contacts are used, they must be fitted with an adult and an eye-care professional — never shared or slept in.</p></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Gear","body":"<p class='lead'>Sleeveless brown tunic + belt.</p><p>Bare green arms are the look. No heavy outer robe.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>Green blade.</p><p>Clean Jedi hilt.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Tentacles light + anchored.</li><li>Sea-green skin.</li><li>Bare arms.</li><li>Green blade + the smile.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Shii-Cho</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ FORM I · SHII-CHO — “The Way of the Sarlacc”</div><p>The oldest form in the book, and he makes it look brand new — wide sweeping strikes, loose bright footwork, built for facing many opponents at once. Shii-Cho is simple on purpose; in a master's hands, simple is terrifying. Canon's great Shii-Cho master — he polished the training form every youngling learns first into a smiling, unpredictable art that even Grievous struggled to read.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#3fae5a\">⬤</span> Green — hilt sealed for underwater duels — his blade works fully submerged</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Run the classic Shii-Cho velocities: broad horizontal sweeps flowing into diagonal cuts, big and relaxed, without stopping between them. Kit's secret is loose shoulders, constant motion, and the grin.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;You may have been a proud warrior once, but now you're just a pawn in Dooku's game.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; to Grievous — calm, almost feeling sorry for him</i></li><li>&ldquo;That power will only consume you.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; quiet and certain</i></li><li>&ldquo;His heart was in the right place, but he tried to answer Grievous' power with his own.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; soft and sad — his report to the Jedi Council</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>Yes, they're tentacles. No, you may not borrow one for jump rope.</li><li>I'm the only Jedi who can smile underwater. It's a gift.</li><li>Grievous has four lightsabers. I still won on style points.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Kit Fisto saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=kit+fisto+lightsaber"},{"name":"Nautolan tentacle tutorial","designer":"YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=nautolan+head+tentacles"},{"name":"Full Kit Fisto costume","designer":"Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=kit+fisto+cosplay"},{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Green blade."}],"buy":[{"name":"Sea-green skin paint","detail":"Set with powder."},{"name":"Tentacle materials","detail":"Foam + green fabric + skullcap."},{"name":"Black Nautolan contacts (optional)","detail":"Adult eye-care check first."},{"name":"Sleeveless brown tunic","detail":"Bare arms."},{"name":"Brown belt + saber clip","detail":"Standard Jedi."},{"name":"Brown trousers + boots","detail":"Standard."},{"name":"Green lightsaber","detail":"Clean hilt."}]}},"bastila":{"meta":{"word":"BASTILA","accent":"#e0cc52","body":"bastila","budget":180,"btn":"⚔ OLD REPUBLIC","dur":"6 weeks","hrs":"20–40 hrs","parts":"Rust robe-dress + double saber + ringed ponytails","budgetRange":"€100–300","lead":"Bastila Shan — the Jedi of the Old Republic, master of Battle Meditation, ally of Revan. Her signature look is the high-collared RUST / burnt-orange-red robe-dress, gold-ringed ponytails, and a YELLOW double-bladed lightsaber.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The gold-ringed ponytails + the YELLOW double-blade are her signature, worn over the high-collared rust robe-dress. A single blue blade reads as generic Jedi.","intro":"OPERATION BASTILA","introSub":"OLD REPUBLIC · BUILD MANUAL · FILE SHAN","footer":"OPERATION BASTILA · BUILD MANUAL · BATTLE MEDITATION · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"bastila_public.pdf","weekPdf":"bastila_byweek.pdf","quote":"The Force fights with me!"},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Gold-Ringed Ponytails","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Craft","hours":6,"cost":30,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Her signature multi-ponytail style — one top ponytail pulling back the bangs plus two behind, threaded through stacked gold rings/cuffs.","tip":"Long ponytails (or a wig) segmented with gold ring/cuff bands — not cone forms.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Robe Shoulders","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Sew","hours":2,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Old Republic robe shoulders.","tip":"Squarer than later Jedi robes.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Bastila is robes.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Rust Robe-Dress (High Collar)","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Her signature high-collared rust / burnt-orange-red Old Republic robe-dress with layered chest panels. Tan/brown is only the generic equippable Jedi robe.","tip":"Rust/burnt-orange-red with a high collar — the defining feature. Keep tan as an optional generic-Jedi alternative.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Clip","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide belt with double-saber clip.","tip":"Double sabers need a bigger clip.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Lower Robe Panels","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Sew","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Hanging robe panels.","tip":"Front + sides.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Outer Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Optional rust/brown hooded robe over the dress.","tip":"Often worn down or off.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Bastila is from KOTOR (game era); Rebel Legion recognises her as a Jedi.","tip":"Niche but recognised.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tan trousers.","tip":"Match the tunic.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tan/brown boots.","tip":"Old Republic style.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":12,"priority":"LOW","description":"Optional fingerless gloves.","tip":"Skip for the clean look.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Yellow Double-Bladed Saber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":4,"cost":90,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Bastila's iconic YELLOW double-bladed lightsaber (saberstaff).","tip":"Yellow blades, both ends. The colour + double-blade are essential.","files":[{"name":"Double-bladed saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=double+bladed+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Plan + order tunic fabric, double saber, wig if needed"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Sew/fit the Old Republic robes"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Build the gold-ringed ponytails"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Set saber to yellow + fit the double clip"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Bastila Shan</span> — the Old Republic Jedi from KOTOR.</p><p>Rust robe-dress + the gold-ringed ponytails + a yellow double-bladed saber.</p><h3>A Beloved Jedi</h3><p>Bastila Shan is one of the most beloved Jedi of the Knights of the Old Republic era — a gifted young Jedi, master of Battle Meditation, and a key ally of Revan.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Gold-Ringed Ponytails","body":"<p class='lead'>Her signature silhouette.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ GOLD-RINGED PONYTAILS</div>One top ponytail pulling back the bangs plus two behind, threaded through stacked gold rings. Segment long ponytails (or a wig) with gold ring bands.</div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Robes","body":"<p class='lead'>Old Republic Jedi — chunkier than prequel-era.</p><p>Rust / burnt-orange robe-dress with a high collar, layered panels, squarer shoulders.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"Pair with Revan","body":"<p class='lead'>If a friend builds Revan, you have a KOTOR duo.</p><p>Revan + Bastila + Malak + Nihilus = a full Old Republic line.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Double Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>YELLOW, double-bladed.</p><p>The saberstaff with yellow blades is unmistakably Bastila.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">YELLOW, BOTH ENDS</div><p>It's one of the rare yellow blades in all of Star Wars — the colour and the double-blade together are essential. Because it's a long staff, plan a bigger belt clip and mind its length around crowds and doorways.</p></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Gold-ringed ponytails.</li><li>Rust Old Republic robe-dress.</li><li>Yellow double-blade.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Old Republic style</span>, wielded double-bladed staff.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · OLD REPUBLIC STYLE</div><p>No numbered form survives from her era — she fights the Old Republic way, the saberstaff whirling to buy time while Battle Meditation does the real damage, tilting a whole battlefield's will to fight. The staff work reads closest to Form VI Niman, the balanced form later staff-fighters favoured. Her true weapon is Battle Meditation, not the blade — the yellow saberstaff exists to keep enemies off her while she wins the wider battle inside their heads.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#ecc93a\">⬤</span> Yellow — double-bladed staff — yellow from both emitters</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">double-bladed staff</span></div></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ MORE THAN ONE BLADE — THE CRAFT</div><ul><li>A staff needs full 360-degree clearance — arm-span plus blade in every direction before a single swing.</li><li>Hands stay near the middle of the hilt, about shoulder-width apart; steer with the wrists, not the arms.</li><li>One end strikes while the other guards — think seesaw, never windmill.</li><li>Never spin near people: step out of the group, spin, step back.</li></ul></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Slow figure-eights at half speed, ten passes each side, finishing every pass in a two-handed guard held across the body. Control first — speed never.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;What greater weapon is there than to turn an enemy to your cause? To use their own knowledge against them?&rdquo; <i>&mdash; cool and confident — very 'I planned this all along'</i></li><li>&ldquo;I am simply trying to help you and complete this mission, and yet you battle me at every turn!&rdquo; <i>&mdash; exasperated — hands on hips</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>My battle meditation works on spelling tests, too.</li><li>I had everything under control. Mostly under control. Fine — who knows long division?</li><li>A Jedi does not lose at board games. A Jedi strategically retreats.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Double-bladed saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=double+bladed+lightsaber"},{"name":"Old Republic robe reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=bastila+shan"},{"name":"Full Bastila costume","designer":"Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=bastila+shan+cosplay"},{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Double saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Yellow blades, both ends."}],"buy":[{"name":"Rust robe-dress (high collar)","detail":"Layered, chunky cut."},{"name":"Wide belt + double clip","detail":"Bigger clip for saberstaff."},{"name":"Gold ring/cuff hair bands or styled wig","detail":"Ringed ponytails."},{"name":"Tan trousers + boots","detail":"Match."},{"name":"Optional outer robe","detail":"Often down."},{"name":"Yellow double-bladed saber","detail":"The signature."}]}},"malak":{"meta":{"word":"MALAK","accent":"#6a7480","body":"malak","budget":220,"btn":"⚔ OLD REPUBLIC","dur":"7 weeks","hrs":"30–60 hrs","parts":"Sith armour + metal jaw + red saber","budgetRange":"€130–350","lead":"Darth Malak — Revan's apprentice turned Dark Lord of the Sith. Bald, with the iconic grey metal prosthetic jaw, heavy burgundy Sith armour over a ribbed maroon tunic, and a red blade. Completes the KOTOR line.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The METAL JAW is Malak. The grey prosthetic plate wraps the lower face AND ties into a ring around the neck — build it as one connected piece. It's the detail no one forgets.","intro":"OPERATION MALAK","introSub":"OLD REPUBLIC · BUILD MANUAL · FILE SION-ERA","footer":"OPERATION MALAK · BUILD MANUAL · DARK LORD OF THE SITH · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 9 TOTAL","pubPdf":"malak_public.pdf","weekPdf":"malak_byweek.pdf","quote":"The Star Forge... it hungers. And it can feed on the dark side that is within all of us."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Bald Cap + Metal Jaw","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print + Makeup","hours":10,"cost":45,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Bald cap + the grey metal prosthetic jaw plate covering the lower face from nose to chin, tied into a ring around the base of the neck.","tip":"Build the jaw plate and grey neck ring/collar as one connected piece, not a free-floating chin plate; blend the top edge with makeup.","files":[{"name":"Malak jaw STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=darth+malak+jaw"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Armour","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Heavy burgundy Sith shoulder plates.","tip":"Old Republic = chunky. Matte burgundy.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Sith Chest Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print + Foam","hours":10,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The rigid burgundy armoured chest piece worn over a full ribbed maroon Sith tunic — the torso is fully covered, with horizontal stomach ribbing.","tip":"Burgundy chest plate over a body-conforming ribbed maroon undersuit; no bare skin.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Belt Harness","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"3D Print","hours":4,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"The lower harness connecting chest to belt.","tip":"Mechanical, burgundy with grey accents.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Heavy Belt","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide Old Republic Sith belt with saber clip.","tip":"Chunky buckle. Brown/grey belt against burgundy armour.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Hip Plates","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print","hours":4,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Burgundy hip + groin plates.","tip":"Match the chest — burgundy with grey edges.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Lower Robes","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark skirt-robes from the waist down, over burgundy pants.","tip":"Heavy, floor-length black fabric panels.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Malak is from KOTOR (game era); 501st recognises him as a Sith.","tip":"Niche but recognised.","files":[{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin Armour","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print","hours":6,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Grey shin + knee plates.","tip":"Both legs. Grey/gunmetal accents against burgundy.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall dark boots.","tip":"Under the robes.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gauntlets","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"3D Print + Buy","hours":4,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Burgundy Sith vambraces + gloves.","tip":"Old Republic chunk, burgundy with grey trim.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Red Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":70,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Red blade, blocky Old Republic hilt.","tip":"Like Revan's — chunkier than modern sabers.","files":[{"name":"Old Republic saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=old+republic+lightsaber"}]},"diagonalcapepanel":{"name":"Diagonal Cape Panel","type":"BODY · 13","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Matte black cloth panel crossing diagonally from the right shoulder to the left elbow, dropping down the left side to near the floor.","tip":"This diagonal drape defines Malak's silhouette — anchor it at the right shoulder and let it fall long on the left.","files":[]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 7–6","task":"Plan + order filament, dark fabric, jaw print, red saber"},{"label":"Weeks 5–4","task":"Print + finish the metal jaw + chest armour"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Shoulders, harness, hip plates, shins"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Bald cap practice + lower robes"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>An <span class='accent'>Old Republic Sith armour</span> build with one unforgettable feature: the metal jaw.</p><p>Chunky armour + bald cap + the prosthetic jaw plate.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">TWO PROJECTS IN ONE</div><p>Malak is an armour build and a prosthetic build. Tackle them as separate jobs: get the metal jaw working comfortably first (it's the icon), then build the chunky Sith armour around it. It's the hardest of this Old Republic group — but the payoff is one of the most memorable looks in the archive.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Metal Jaw","body":"<p class='lead'>The signature.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ LOWER FACE PLATE</div>Print a metal-finish jaw plate covering nose-to-chin. Strap it on, blend the top edge with makeup. You'll speak through it — leave a gap.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE BALD HEAD</div><p>Above the jaw, Malak is bald. A quality bald cap, blended at the edges and painted to match your skin, completes the silhouette — the bald head + metal jaw combination is instantly Malak.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Armour","body":"<p class='lead'>Heavy chest harness over a bare/skin-base midriff.</p><p>Old Republic Sith armour is chunkier and more mechanical than later eras.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE PLATES</div><ul><li>Shoulder plates — heavy Old Republic pauldrons.</li><li>Belt harness + hip plates — connecting chest to waist.</li><li>Vambraces + gauntlets — chunky dark forearms.</li><li>Shin + knee plates — dark, over tall boots.</li><li>Lower robes — a dark, floor-length skirt-robe from the waist down.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"Pair with the KOTOR Line","body":"<p class='lead'>Malak + Revan + Bastila + Nihilus.</p><p>Build the whole Old Republic crew with friends.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"Finishing","body":"<p class='lead'>Dark metal, steel highlights.</p><p>Weather the armour with silver edge-rubbing.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"The Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>Red blade, blocky hilt.</p><p>Match the Old Republic era.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Metal jaw = the icon.</li><li>Chunky Sith armour.</li><li>Bald cap.</li><li>Red blade.</li></ul>"},{"num":"08","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Old Republic style</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · OLD REPUBLIC STYLE</div><p>Brute force in heavy armour — huge two-handed power arcs meant to smash a guard flat, with no finesse wasted on anything smaller. Canon assigns him no numbered form, but it reads closest to Form V Djem So: overwhelm, press forward, repeat until something gives. Malak took Revan's throne with raw power instead of cunning, and every swing shows it.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#cc2f2e\">⬤</span> Red — blocky Old Republic hilt</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Slow-motion power arcs: raise the saber in a full two-handed overhead sweep, freeze for three seconds at the top, then bring it down along one controlled line. Ten reps builds Malak's heavy, deliberate rhythm without ever swinging fast.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Savior, conqueror, hero, villain. You are all things, Revan… and yet you are nothing.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; his most famous speech — slow and mocking, pause hard before 'nothing'</i></li><li>&ldquo;In the end you belong to neither the light nor the darkness. You will forever stand alone.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; the follow-up line from the same speech — let it hang</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>You are all things, Revan… and yet you forgot the snacks.</li><li>The Star Forge hungers. So do I. Point me to the pizza.</li><li>This metal jaw is definitely not for chewing gum in class. Mostly.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Malak jaw STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=darth+malak+jaw"},{"name":"Old Republic saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=old+republic+lightsaber"},{"name":"Full Malak reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=darth+malak"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Metal jaw plate","detail":"Nose-to-chin, metal finish."},{"name":"Chest harness","detail":"Over bare/skin base."},{"name":"Shoulder + hip plates","detail":"Chunky."},{"name":"Vambraces + shins","detail":"Both sides."},{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Blocky."}],"buy":[{"name":"Bald cap","detail":"Quality silicone/latex."},{"name":"Skin-tone base layer","detail":"Under the harness."},{"name":"Dark lower robes","detail":"Floor-length."},{"name":"Heavy belt + boots","detail":"Old Republic."},{"name":"Steel + dark paint","detail":"For armour + jaw."},{"name":"Red lightsaber","detail":"Blocky hilt."}]}},"mae":{"meta":{"word":"MAE","accent":"#9c3848","body":"mae","budget":120,"btn":"⚔ ACOLYTE","dur":"4 weeks","hrs":"12–25 hrs","parts":"Dark assassin outfit + hood","budgetRange":"€70–220","lead":"Mae — the vengeful twin from The Acolyte. A purple patchwork hooded cloak layered over dark, fitted underlayers and samurai-style bamboo-and-chainmail armour. The Jedi-killer who vows to fight without a weapon.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"Mae is HOODED, in her signature purple patchwork cloak, worn over fitted dark underlayers and bamboo/chainmail armour — a layered, samurai-style look, not flowing Sith robes.","intro":"OPERATION MAE","introSub":"ACOLYTE ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE ANISEYA","footer":"OPERATION MAE · BUILD MANUAL · THE ACOLYTE · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"mae_public.pdf","weekPdf":"mae_byweek.pdf","quote":"I'm going to kill a Jedi without a weapon."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Hood + Wrap","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":2,"cost":20,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The dark hood that frames the face; sometimes a face wrap for stealth.","tip":"Hood up is the assassin silhouette.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Fitted Top","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Close-fitting dark top — layered, with wrapped/quilted detail.","tip":"Fitted, not flowing. Dark underlayer beneath the purple cloak.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Bamboo + Chainmail Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":35,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Layered armour worn under the cloak — faux-bamboo plating plus a chainmail panel, samurai/gladiator-inspired.","tip":"Real costume uses bamboo cast in silicone, pewter plates and chainmail. Faux-bamboo and craft chainmail read fine under the cloak.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Wrap Detail","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Sew","hours":2,"cost":15,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Diagonal wrap/sash detail across the chest.","tip":"Asymmetric wrap.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Pouches","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Belt with small pouches.","tip":"Assassin kit.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Lower Wrap","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Sew","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Wrapped lower panels.","tip":"Allows movement.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Purple Patchwork Cloak","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":35,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Mae's signature hooded cloak — hand-stitched from many fabric swatches, dyed purple, deliberately tattered.","tip":"Purple is her memory color. Piece it from scraps and distress it; this is the #1 recognition cue.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Mae is recent (The Acolyte); check costume-club recognition.","tip":"Recent show — references online.","files":[{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Fitted Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Close-fitting dark trousers.","tip":"Stealth movement.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Soft Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Soft-soled dark boots.","tip":"Quiet, assassin-style.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Wraps / Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Hand wraps or dark gloves.","tip":"She fights with her hands.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"No Weapon (or red, later)","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":60,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Mae's vow is to kill without a weapon — but her later arc carries a red blade. Optional.","tip":"Carry nothing for the early look; a red blade for the later arc.","files":[{"name":"Sith saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=sith+lightsaber+hilt"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 1","task":"Plan + order fitted top, trousers, hood, optional saber"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Fit the layered top + wrap detail"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Add belt, cloak, hand-wraps"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Mae</span> — the vengeful twin from The Acolyte.</p><p>A fitted, dark, hooded assassin's outfit — stealth, not flowing robes.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Silhouette","body":"<p class='lead'>Fitted + hooded.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ STEALTH, NOT SITH</div>Mae's look is close-fitting and practical for movement — layered wraps, a hood, soft boots. Not the big flowing robes of a Sith Lord.</div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Layers","body":"<p class='lead'>Dark top + diagonal wrap + belt.</p><p>Black with dark crimson accents. Asymmetric wrap across the chest.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">MORE PIECES</div><ul><li>Hood / face wrap — dark, framing the face; a face wrap adds to the stealth look for the early scenes.</li><li>Belt + pouches — an assassin's kit.</li><li>Short cloak — shorter than a Sith robe, for the silhouette.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"Weapon (or Not)","body":"<p class='lead'>Her vow: kill a Jedi without a weapon.</p><p>Early look carries nothing. Later arc adds a red blade — your choice.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"Movement","body":"<p class='lead'>Soft boots, hand-wraps.</p><p>Built for fighting — everything allows movement.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">MOVE LIKE THE ASSASSIN</div><p>Low, balanced, ready — a martial-artist's stance. Quick and quiet; a hand-to-hand ready pose (hood up, wraps on) is the signature photo. Single-minded intensity — Mae is on a mission and it shows.</p></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Fitted + hooded.</li><li>Dark with crimson accents.</li><li>Soft, quiet, practical.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Attack me with all your strength.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; her opening challenge to Master Indara — calm and confident, chin up</i></li><li>&ldquo;The power of one. The power of two. The power of many.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; the twins' chant — say it like a rhyme, growing louder on 'many'</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I'm going to win this spelling bee without a pencil.</li><li>Attack me with all your strength… at thumb wars.</li><li>I have a twin. Whatever went wrong today — that was her.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Acolyte costume reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=the+acolyte+mae"},{"name":"Hooded assassin pattern","designer":"Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=assassin+hood+costume"},{"name":"Sith saber STL (optional)","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=sith+lightsaber+hilt"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Red, later arc only."}],"buy":[{"name":"Fitted dark top","detail":"Layered, wrap detail."},{"name":"Hood / face wrap","detail":"Up for stealth."},{"name":"Fitted dark trousers","detail":"Movement."},{"name":"Soft dark boots","detail":"Quiet."},{"name":"Belt + pouches","detail":"Assassin kit."},{"name":"Hand-wraps or gloves","detail":"She fights bare-handed."},{"name":"Short cloak","detail":"Shorter than Sith robes."}]}},"sol":{"meta":{"word":"SOL","accent":"#8a7340","body":"sol","budget":150,"btn":"⚔ JEDI","dur":"5 weeks","hrs":"15–30 hrs","parts":"High Republic Jedi robes","budgetRange":"€90–260","lead":"Sol — the Jedi Master from The Acolyte, the High Republic era. Warm cream-and-gold layered Jedi robes (lighter and more refined than prequel-era), a beard, and a blue blade.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"High Republic Jedi robes are LIGHTER + more refined than prequel-era — cream and gold, not brown and tan.","intro":"OPERATION SOL","introSub":"HIGH REPUBLIC · BUILD MANUAL · FILE ACOLYTE","footer":"OPERATION SOL · BUILD MANUAL · MASTER OF THE HIGH REPUBLIC · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 8 TOTAL","pubPdf":"sol_public.pdf","weekPdf":"sol_byweek.pdf","quote":"Your eyes can deceive you. We must not trust them."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Hair + Beard","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Style","hours":2,"cost":20,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Short dark hair + a neat beard. A costume beard if needed.","tip":"Neat, groomed — a respected Master.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Robe Shoulders","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Sew","hours":2,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"High Republic robe shoulders — cleaner lines.","tip":"More tailored than prequel Jedi.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Sol is robes.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"White Tunic + Gold Tabards","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":4,"cost":50,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Sol's iconic white/ivory temple tunic with rich GOLD tabards.","tip":"Commit to the hero temple look: white tunic, gold tabards.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Obi + Clip","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":20,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Wide belt with saber clip.","tip":"Refined leather.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Tabard Drape","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Sew","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tabards continue past the belt.","tip":"Front + back.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Ivory Outer Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":50,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Hooded ivory/white High Republic temple robe with gold braid.","tip":"Lighter than the classic brown — white, not tan.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Sol is recent (The Acolyte); Rebel Legion recognises Jedi.","tip":"Recent show — references online.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Cream/tan trousers.","tip":"Match the tunic.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Brown leather boots.","tip":"Standard Jedi.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Bare Hands","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Sol goes bare-handed.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blue Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":60,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Sol's blade is BLUE.","tip":"Clean hilt, blue blade.","files":[{"name":"Jedi saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=jedi+lightsaber+hilt"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 5","task":"Plan + order cream/gold robe fabric, blue saber"},{"label":"Week 4","task":"Sew/fit the High Republic layers"},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Add the outer robe + tabards"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Groom the hair + beard; saber clip"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Sol</span> — the Jedi Master from The Acolyte, High Republic era.</p><p>Refined cream + gold Jedi robes + a blue blade.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">PAIR WITH THE ACOLYTE CAST</div><p>Sol pairs naturally with the other Acolyte builds in this archive — Mae and Qimir/the Stranger. A High Republic Jedi Master against the assassin twin and the masked Sith makes a striking trio with friends.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"High Republic Robes","body":"<p class='lead'>Lighter + finer than prequel Jedi.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ CREAM, NOT BROWN</div>High Republic Jedi wear lighter, more tailored robes — creams and golds with cleaner lines. Don't reach for the classic brown.</div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Layers","body":"<p class='lead'>Tunic, tabards, obi, outer robe.</p><p>Same Jedi structure, refined materials.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">PIECE BY PIECE</div><ul><li>Cream tunic + tabards — the layered Jedi front, in cream and gold rather than brown.</li><li>Obi belt — wide, with a saber clip; refined leather.</li><li>Hooded outer robe — cream/tan, lighter than the classic brown.</li><li>Cream trousers + standard brown Jedi boots.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"04","title":"Grooming","body":"<p class='lead'>Neat hair + beard.</p><p>Sol is a respected, composed Master — keep it tidy.</p>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>Blue blade.</p><p>Clean hilt.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">MOVE LIKE A MASTER</div><ul><li>Calm, composed, warm — Sol is a steady, respected teacher.</li><li>Measured, graceful movement — dignity over flash.</li><li>A clean blue-blade ready stance makes a great photo.</li><li>He belongs in the Rebel Legion (the heroes' club).</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Cream + gold, not brown.</li><li>Tailored High Republic lines.</li><li>Neat beard.</li><li>Blue blade.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">High Republic orthodox</span>, wielded single.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · HIGH REPUBLIC ORTHODOX</div><p>Textbook control — balanced stance, short economical cuts, nothing flashy until the moment absolutely demands it. The Acolyte never names his form, but it reads closest to Form III Soresu fundamentals: defence first, then one clean, decisive answer. Sol fights the way he teaches — calm, precise, and holding back far more than he shows.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#2e7de6\">⬤</span> Blue — single classic Jedi blade</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single</span></div></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Hold a centred guard and practise the smallest parry that would still work — tiny wrist deflections left, right and high without ever moving your feet. Sol's calm comes from doing less, perfectly.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"08","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;Close your eyes.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; his gentle teaching cue — it comes right before the card quote</i></li><li>&ldquo;Connect with the Force.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; same meditation lesson — soft and steady, palms open</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>Close your eyes… no peeking. Especially you.</li><li>Your eyes can deceive you. That's why I checked the cookie jar twice.</li><li>A Jedi seeks balance. Especially standing on one foot in the lunch line.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Jedi saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=jedi+lightsaber+hilt"},{"name":"High Republic robe reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=the+acolyte+sol"},{"name":"Full Sol costume","designer":"Etsy","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=the+acolyte+jedi+costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Blue blade."}],"buy":[{"name":"Cream/gold tunic + tabards","detail":"High Republic cut."},{"name":"Wide belt + clip","detail":"Refined."},{"name":"Cream hooded outer robe","detail":"Lighter than brown."},{"name":"Cream trousers + brown boots","detail":"Match."},{"name":"Costume beard (if needed)","detail":"Neat."},{"name":"Blue lightsaber","detail":"Clean hilt."}]}},"qimir":{"meta":{"word":"QIMIR","accent":"#5a5560","body":"qimir","budget":200,"btn":"⚔ THE STRANGER","dur":"6 weeks","hrs":"25–50 hrs","parts":"Cortosis helmet + dark robes + red saber","budgetRange":"€110–320","lead":"Qimir — the Stranger from The Acolyte. A menacing cortosis helmet with its grille of exposed metal teeth and narrow eye slit, dark layered robes, and a red blade. One of the most striking modern Sith designs.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The dark cortosis helmet is the whole look — a sinister grinning grille of exposed metal \"teeth\" (a breathing/voice apparatus) and a narrow eye slit. Forged, scarred metal, not a smooth blank mask.","intro":"OPERATION QIMIR","introSub":"ACOLYTE ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE STRANGER","footer":"OPERATION QIMIR · BUILD MANUAL · THE STRANGER · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 9 TOTAL","pubPdf":"qimir_public.pdf","weekPdf":"qimir_byweek.pdf","quote":"Freedom to wield my power the way I like."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Cortosis Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"3D Print","hours":12,"cost":50,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The forged cortosis helmet — a sinister grille of exposed metal 'teeth' forming a grin (a breathing/voice apparatus) with a narrow horizontal eye slit. Dark, scarred, battle-worn metal. The whole costume hinges on it.","tip":"Print/sculpt the toothed grille and eye slit, then finish in a dark weathered metallic (bronzed gunmetal) — NOT glossy. Add scratches and welding marks. Hidden mesh-vision behind the eye slit.","files":[{"name":"Qimir helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=qimir+stranger+helmet"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Robe Shoulders","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Sew","hours":2,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark layered robe shoulders.","tip":"Heavy, structured.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Qimir is robes + the helmet, not armour.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Layered Tunic","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":4,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Dark grey-black layered tunic, textured fabric.","tip":"Multiple dark layers — all matte, not shiny. The helmet is weathered metal, so nothing in the fit should be glossy.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Clip","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark belt with saber clip.","tip":"Simple, dark.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Lower Robe Panels","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Sew","hours":1,"cost":12,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Hanging dark panels.","tip":"Layered.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Hooded Cloak","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":50,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Dark hooded cloak — worn over the helmet, hood up, in the entrance.","tip":"Hood over the toothed cortosis helmet = the iconic reveal.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Qimir is recent (The Acolyte); check costume-club recognition.","tip":"Recent show — references online.","files":[{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":18,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Dark trousers.","tip":"Hidden by the robe.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":40,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall dark boots.","tip":"Under the robe.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Dark Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":12,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark gloves, both hands.","tip":"Matte black.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Red Lightsaber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":3,"cost":70,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"Red blade on a sleek, angular black hilt. The Stranger's hilt is a split design — the pommel detaches to form a second short shoto blade.","tip":"For screen accuracy, reference the split-hilt: a main blade plus a concealed shoto in the pommel. Red blade; the helmet carries the look.","files":[{"name":"Sith saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=sith+lightsaber+hilt"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 6–5","task":"Plan + order filament, dark fabric, red saber"},{"label":"Weeks 4–3","task":"Print + PERFECTLY smooth the helmet — gloss black"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Sew the dark layered robes + hooded cloak"},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Belt + saber + hidden vision strip in the helmet"},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal + game day"}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>The whole costume is the <span class='accent'>helmet</span>.</p><p>A dark cortosis mask with a grille of metal teeth and a narrow eye slit. It must be flawless, because there's nothing else to hide behind.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Helmet","body":"<p class='lead'>Blank + glossy + perfect.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ SAND IT PERFECTLY</div>Print, then sand through every grit to glass-smooth, prime, and gloss black. Any bump or seam shows instantly on a blank curved surface. Hide a mesh vision strip low near the neck.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE GRIT LADDER</div><p>Sand through every grit — 120, 220, 400, 800+ — until it's glass-smooth. Fill every seam, prime, then check for flaws under bright light before the final gloss black. The patience here is the build.</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"Seeing Out","body":"<p class='lead'>The hard part.</p><p>The narrow eye slit is cosmetic — you can't actually see through it. Use a thin perforated/mesh strip low on the helmet where shadow hides it, or a one-way tint panel. Practise walking in it safely.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Robes","body":"<p class='lead'>Dark, layered, MATTE.</p><p>The helmet is the only glossy thing — keep the fabric matte so the helmet pops.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">THE LAYERS</div><ul><li>Layered tunic — dark grey-black, textured matte fabric, multiple layers.</li><li>Belt + saber clip — simple, dark.</li><li>Trousers + tall boots + dark gloves — all matte black.</li><li>Hooded cloak — worn over the helmet, hood up, for the entrance.</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Cloak","body":"<p class='lead'>Hood over the blank helmet.</p><p>The entrance: hood up, blank face in shadow, then the hood comes back. That's the reveal.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">STILLNESS = MENACE</div><p>Move slowly and deliberately — with no expression to read, your stillness does all the menace. He belongs with the 501st Legion (the villains' club).</p></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"The Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>Red blade, sleek modern hilt.</p><p>The helmet carries everything; keep the saber clean.</p>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>Helmet flawless + glossy.</li><li>Vision strip hidden low.</li><li>Robes matte + dark.</li><li>Red blade.</li></ul>"},{"num":"08","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Unorthodox</span>, wielded single, splits to dual JarKai.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · UNORTHODOX</div><p>Ferocious and dirty — he crowds in close, lets the cortosis armour eat your blade, then punishes the opening. No canon form is named, but it reads closest to Form VII Juyo ferocity, weaponised with tricks no Jedi academy would ever sign off on. The Stranger's style is built to kill Jedi who fight by the book — so he threw the book away.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#d32f2f\">⬤</span> Red — main blade, sleek angular black hilt</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#c92a2a\">⬤</span> Red — short shoto dagger — the detachable pommel</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">single, splits to dual JarKai</span></div></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ MORE THAN ONE BLADE — THE CRAFT</div><ul><li>The long blade leads and threatens; the short pommel dagger stays back and guards until the surprise moment.</li><li>Keep the short blade below shoulder height and close to your body — it is a shield first, a striker second.</li><li>Never split the hilt with anyone inside arm's reach; step back, split, then re-engage.</li></ul></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>Footwork over swordwork: practise one quick diagonal step inside an imaginary opponent's reach, pivot, and step back out, saber held short and close. Add the draw-and-split motion only once the feet are quiet.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;I have no name. But the Jedi like you might call me… Sith.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; the big reveal — long pause before 'Sith'</i></li><li>&ldquo;I want a pupil. An acolyte.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; from the same speech as the card quote — quiet, almost friendly; it's the title drop</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I have no name. But kids like you might call me… substitute teacher.</li><li>I want the freedom to wield my snacks the way I like.</li><li>My helmet blocks out everything. Especially chores.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Qimir / Stranger helmet STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=qimir+stranger+helmet"},{"name":"Sith saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=sith+lightsaber+hilt"},{"name":"The Stranger costume reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=the+acolyte+stranger"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Cortosis helmet","detail":"Toothed grille, narrow eye slit, battle-worn."},{"name":"Saber hilt (optional)","detail":"Sleek modern."}],"buy":[{"name":"Dark layered tunic","detail":"Matte fabric."},{"name":"Hooded cloak","detail":"Over the helmet."},{"name":"Dark trousers + tall boots","detail":"Under the robe."},{"name":"Dark gloves","detail":"Both hands."},{"name":"Sandpaper 120–800 + gloss black","detail":"For the flawless helmet."},{"name":"Mesh vision strip","detail":"Hidden low for safety."},{"name":"Red lightsaber","detail":"Sleek hilt."}]}},"poe":{"meta":{"word":"POE","accent":"#7a4a2e","body":"poe","budget":160,"btn":"⚔ RESISTANCE","dur":"4 weeks","hrs":"12–25 hrs","parts":"Flight jacket or pilot flight suit","budgetRange":"€80–260","lead":"Poe Dameron — the Resistance's best pilot, the hotshot flyboy. Two looks: the brown leather flight jacket with the natural/tan Resistance henley, and the orange X-wing pilot flight suit.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The brown leather jacket is Poe. Get a real lived-in brown leather (or good faux) jacket and the rest falls into place — a stiff shiny jacket reads as a costume, a worn one reads as a pilot.","intro":"OPERATION POE","introSub":"RESISTANCE ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE BLACK LEADER","footer":"OPERATION POE · BUILD MANUAL · THE BEST PILOT IN THE RESISTANCE · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 7 TOTAL","pubPdf":"poe_public.pdf","weekPdf":"poe_byweek.pdf","quote":"We are the spark that'll light the fire that'll burn the First Order down."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Hair / Pilot Helmet","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Style/Buy","hours":2,"cost":30,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Casual look: tousled dark hair. Pilot look: the black-and-orange X-wing flight helmet with Black Squadron markings.","tip":"Casual = just good hair; pilot = the marked helmet.","files":[]},"shoulders":{"name":"Jacket Shoulders","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Part of the leather jacket — sits naturally.","tip":"No separate piece.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"No Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Poe is cloth + flight gear.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Tan Henley Shirt","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":25,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The natural/ecru long-sleeve Resistance henley with a standing collar, worn under the jacket.","tip":"Light tan/cream, not blue — standing collar, tucked in.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Holster","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Brown belt with a side blaster holster.","tip":"Practical pilot gear.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"No Codpiece","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"Skip","hours":0,"cost":0,"priority":"LOW","description":"Not applicable.","tip":"Not used.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Brown Leather Jacket","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy","hours":2,"cost":80,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"THE signature: a worn brown leather jacket, slightly cropped, with a plain stand-up leather collar and a smooth lining.","tip":"Lived-in brown leather, plain collar — not a shearling bomber. The heart of the costume.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the Rebel Legion standards — Poe is a Resistance hero.","tip":"Rebel Legion = good guys.","files":[{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion CRL","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Trousers","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":20,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Dark trousers (casual) or the orange flight-suit legs (pilot).","tip":"Era-dependent.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":45,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Brown leather boots.","tip":"Pilot boots, scuffed.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Pilot Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":0,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Brown fingerless or full pilot gloves.","tip":"Optional for casual, expected for pilot.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Blaster","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":35,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Poe's Resistance blaster pistol, holstered at the hip.","tip":"Pilot side-arm.","files":[{"name":"Resistance blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=resistance+blaster"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Week 4","task":"Pick a look. Order the brown leather jacket, tan henley, boots, and a blaster."},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Fit the jacket and shirt. Source the belt + holster. (Pilot look: get the orange flight suit + marked helmet.)"},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Sort the hair (casual) or fit the helmet (pilot). Add gloves + blaster."},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal. Practise the easy, confident flyboy grin."}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Mission Brief","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds <span class='accent'>Poe Dameron</span> — the Resistance's best pilot.</p><p>Two looks: the casual brown-leather-jacket flyboy, and the orange X-wing pilot. Mostly cloth + a great jacket.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">GREAT FOR A GROUP</div><p>Poe pairs naturally with a Rey, a Finn, or a BB-8 for a sequel-trilogy crew. He's also a friendly first build — the casual look needs no armour and no printing. Maximum cool for manageable effort.</p></div>"},{"num":"02","title":"Pick Your Look","body":"<ul><li><b>Casual</b> — brown leather jacket + tan henley + dark trousers + boots. Easy and iconic.</li><li><b>Pilot</b> — orange X-wing flight suit + the black/orange helmet + chest box. More involved.</li></ul>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Jacket","body":"<p class='lead'>The whole costume in one piece.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ LIVED-IN, NOT SHINY</div>A worn brown leather jacket (real or good faux), slightly cropped. Scuff it gently if it's too new — Poe's been flying in it.</div>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Pilot Option","body":"<p class='lead'>Orange flight suit + marked helmet.</p><p>The X-wing pilot look adds the orange jumpsuit, the chest control box, and the black-and-orange Black Squadron helmet. Same family as Luke's pilot gear.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">CALL SIGN · BLACK LEADER</div><p>Poe leads Black Squadron — that's why the helmet carries the Black Squadron markings. More involved than the casual look, but a fantastic pairing with an X-wing photo backdrop.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Gear","body":"<p class='lead'>Belt, holster, blaster, boots.</p><p>Practical pilot kit. A blaster on the hip finishes it.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">PLAY HIM CONFIDENT</div><ul><li>Easy, confident, a little cocky — Poe's a hotshot and he knows it.</li><li>A warm, ready grin — he's a hero who enjoys the job.</li><li>Relaxed pilot's stance, hand near the blaster; tousled dark hair — Poe's easy, slightly messy style.</li><li>He belongs in the Rebel Legion (the heroes' club).</li></ul></div>"},{"num":"06","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>The jacket is everything — worn, not shiny.</li><li>Muted tan henley underneath.</li><li>Confident, easy grin.</li><li>Find a BB-8 if you can.</li></ul>"},{"num":"07","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;So who talks first? You talk first, I talk first?&rdquo; <i>&mdash; fast and cocky, like you're genuinely confused</i></li><li>&ldquo;I can fly anything.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; flat confidence — it's a fact, not a brag</i></li><li>&ldquo;Permission to jump in an X-wing and blow something up?&rdquo; <i>&mdash; big grin, hand already on an imaginary throttle</i></li><li>&ldquo;Somehow, Palpatine returned.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; total deadpan — instant laugh with anyone who's seen it</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>I can fly anything. Paper airplanes count. Especially in class.</li><li>Somehow, my homework disappeared.</li><li>Permission to jump on my bike and blow past everybody?</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Resistance blaster STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=resistance+blaster"},{"name":"Poe flight helmet reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=poe+dameron+helmet"},{"name":"Full Poe costume","designer":"Etsy / eBay","url":"https://www.etsy.com/search?q=poe+dameron+costume"},{"name":"Rebel Legion","designer":"Rebel Legion","url":"https://rebellegion.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Blaster (optional)","detail":"Or buy a Resistance-style pistol."}],"buy":[{"name":"Brown leather jacket","detail":"Worn, slightly cropped. THE piece."},{"name":"Natural/tan henley shirt","detail":"Muted, casual."},{"name":"Brown belt + holster","detail":"Side hip."},{"name":"Brown boots + gloves","detail":"Scuffed pilot gear."},{"name":"Dark trousers","detail":"Casual look."},{"name":"Orange flight suit + helmet","detail":"Pilot look only."}]}},"inquisitor":{"meta":{"word":"INQUISITOR","accent":"#9a1f1f","body":"inquisitor","budget":210,"btn":"⚔ INQUISITORIUS","dur":"7 weeks","hrs":"30–60 hrs","parts":"Pau'an makeup + black armour + spinning saber","budgetRange":"€130–360","lead":"The Grand Inquisitor — the Empire's chief Jedi-hunter. A pale Pau'an face with glowing yellow Sith eyes and red dark-side markings, sleek black Inquisitor armour, and the iconic double-bladed spinning red lightsaber.","ruleLabel":"▌ THE ONE RULE","rule":"The pale Pau'an face + the spinning double-saber are the Grand Inquisitor. The gaunt grey Pau'an face with yellow eyes and red facial markings, plus the ring-hilted spinning twin-blade, are unmistakable — a generic black-armour Sith misses both.","intro":"OPERATION INQUISITOR","introSub":"INQUISITORIUS ARCHIVE · BUILD MANUAL · FILE GRAND INQUISITOR","footer":"OPERATION INQUISITOR · BUILD MANUAL · THE EMPIRE'S CHIEF JEDI-HUNTER · FREE TO SHARE","chapLabel":"▌ CHAPTERS · 9 TOTAL","pubPdf":"inquisitor_public.pdf","weekPdf":"inquisitor_byweek.pdf","quote":"You have no idea what you've unleashed here today."},"forge":{"helmet":{"name":"Pau'an Face + Hood","type":"HEAD · 01","kind":"Makeup","hours":8,"cost":40,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The gaunt pale-grey Pau'an face with glowing yellow Sith eyes, sunken skull-like cheeks, and red dark-side facial markings/tattoos, framed by a dark hood.","tip":"A brow-and-cheek prosthetic or silicone Pau'an appliance gives the gaunt, sunken bone structure flat makeup can't. Over that: skin-safe grey base, yellow contacts (with care), red markings running down from the eyes.","files":[{"name":"Inquisitor makeup reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=grand+inquisitor"}]},"shoulders":{"name":"Shoulder Armour","type":"SHOULDER · 02","kind":"3D Print/Foam","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Sleek black Inquisitor pauldrons.","tip":"Angular, glossy black.","files":[]},"chestplate":{"name":"Chest Armour","type":"TORSO · 03","kind":"3D Print/Foam","hours":8,"cost":35,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The black Inquisitor chest plate — sleek, angular, with the Inquisitorius detailing.","tip":"Glossy black over a black flight suit.","files":[]},"chestpanel":{"name":"Layered Tunic","type":"TORSO · 04","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":30,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark layered tunic under the chest armour.","tip":"Matte black layers.","files":[]},"belt":{"name":"Belt + Saber Mount","type":"WAIST · 05","kind":"Buy/Print","hours":2,"cost":22,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Dark belt with a mount for the circular saber.","tip":"The ring-hilt needs a special clip.","files":[]},"codpiece":{"name":"Hip Plates","type":"WAIST · 06","kind":"3D Print/Foam","hours":3,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Dark angular hip plates.","tip":"Match the chest.","files":[]},"cape":{"name":"Cape / Robe","type":"OUTER · 07","kind":"Buy/Sew","hours":3,"cost":45,"priority":"HIGH","description":"A dark cape or skirted robe over the armour.","tip":"Floor-length, dark, dramatic.","files":[]},"chain":{"name":"Reference & Fit","type":"SYSTEM · 08","kind":"Plan","hours":1,"cost":0,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Check against the 501st Inquisitorius standards — the Grand Inquisitor is a villain.","tip":"501st = bad guys.","files":[{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}]},"shins":{"name":"Shin Armour","type":"LEGS · 09","kind":"3D Print/Foam","hours":5,"cost":18,"priority":"HIGH","description":"Black angular shin + knee plates.","tip":"Both legs.","files":[]},"boots":{"name":"Boots","type":"LEGS · 10","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":45,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Tall black boots.","tip":"Under the robe.","files":[]},"gloves":{"name":"Gloves","type":"ARM · 11","kind":"Buy","hours":1,"cost":15,"priority":"MEDIUM","description":"Black gloves; dark vambraces optional.","tip":"Matte black.","files":[]},"saber":{"name":"Spinning Double Saber","type":"WEAPON · 12","kind":"3D Print/Buy","hours":6,"cost":90,"priority":"CRITICAL","description":"The iconic CIRCULAR Inquisitor hilt — a ring that holds a double blade and can spin. Red blades.","tip":"The ring-hilt + double red blade is THE signature. Spin function optional.","files":[{"name":"Inquisitor saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=inquisitor+lightsaber"}]}},"weeks":[{"label":"Weeks 7–6","task":"Plan + order filament/foam, black + grey paint, Pau'an makeup, a black flight suit, and the circular saber."},{"label":"Weeks 5–4","task":"Practice the Pau'an face (grey skin, red eyes, markings). Build + finish the chest and shoulder armour."},{"label":"Week 3","task":"Hip plates, shins, vambraces. Keep everything sleek and glossy black."},{"label":"Week 2","task":"Build/assemble the circular spinning saber + its belt mount. The signature piece."},{"label":"Week 1.5","task":"Add the cape/robe, gloves, boots. Full makeup test."},{"label":"Week 1","task":"Dress rehearsal. Practise the cold, theatrical menace."}],"chapters":[{"num":"01","title":"Reality Check","body":"<p class='lead'>This builds the <span class='accent'>Grand Inquisitor</span> — the Empire's chief Jedi-hunter from <i>Rebels</i> and <i>Obi-Wan Kenobi</i>.</p><p>Two big jobs: the Pau'an face makeup, and the iconic spinning double-bladed saber. The black armour ties them together.</p>"},{"num":"02","title":"The Pau'an Face","body":"<p class='lead'>The gaunt grey face is half the character.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ PALE, SUNKEN, RED-EYED</div>Skin-safe grey base, deeply shadowed cheeks for the gaunt Pau'an look, dark facial markings, and red eyes (contacts optional — with an adult + eye-care professional, never shared or slept in). Patch-test paint 24h early.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">NO CONTACTS? STILL SELLS</div><p>If fitted contacts aren't available, dark red eyeshadow around the eyes still sells it — the grey contouring and the saber carry the costume. Shading the cheek hollows is what makes it read as Pau'an rather than just 'grey face.'</p></div>"},{"num":"03","title":"The Armour","body":"<p class='lead'>Sleek, angular, glossy black.</p><p>Chest, shoulders, hip plates, and shins over a black flight suit. The Inquisitorius look is smooth and menacing, not bulky.</p>"},{"num":"04","title":"The Spinning Saber","body":"<p class='lead'>The signature weapon.</p><div class='reader-callout'><div class='label'>▌ THE RING HILT</div>A circular hilt that holds a double red blade and can spin. Even without the spin function, the ring-hilt + twin red blades is unmistakably Inquisitor. Search 'Inquisitor lightsaber STL'.</div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">PLAN THE BELT MOUNT</div><p>The circular hilt won't hang from a standard clip — the ring needs a special belt mount, so plan how it hangs before game day.</p></div>"},{"num":"05","title":"The Cape & Robe","body":"<p class='lead'>Dark and dramatic.</p><p>A floor-length cape or skirted robe over the armour adds the theatrical Inquisitor presence.</p>"},{"num":"06","title":"Performance","body":"<p class='lead'>Cold, theatrical, superior.</p><p>The Grand Inquisitor is calm and mocking — he enjoys the hunt. Play him with slow, deliberate menace and a touch of dark humour.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">BUILD A HUNT</div><p>He pairs naturally with Darth Vader (his master) and, if friends build them, the other Inquisitors — a Grand Inquisitor leading a pack of Jedi-hunters is one of the most striking group builds you can stage. He belongs in the 501st Legion (the villains' club), in the Inquisitorius detachment.</p></div>"},{"num":"07","title":"Builder Tips","body":"<ul><li>The Pau'an face + the spinning saber are the two icons.</li><li>Sleek glossy black armour, not bulky.</li><li>Red eyes with care.</li><li>The ring-hilt is the signature — spin optional.</li></ul>"},{"num":"08","title":"Saber Craft","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The blade is half the costume — fight like the character. <span class=\"accent\">Temple Guard training</span>, wielded spinning double.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ STYLE · TEMPLE GUARD TRAINING</div><p>Fear is the real weapon — the spinning ring, the slow advance, the taunts, all designed to make you break form before he does. Canon gives him no numbered form, but it reads closest to disciplined Temple Guard double-blade fundamentals turned inside out for aggressive Jedi-hunting. A former Jedi Temple Guard who kept the double blade and traded the vow of protection for the hunt.</p></div><div class=\"reader-table\"><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#d32b2b\">⬤</span> Red — spinning ring hilt, forward blade</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">BLADE</span><span class=\"col-val\"><span style=\"color:#d32b2b\">⬤</span> Red — spinning ring hilt, rear blade</span></div><div class=\"reader-table-row\"><span class=\"col-key\">WIELD</span><span class=\"col-val\">spinning double</span></div></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">▌ MORE THAN ONE BLADE — THE CRAFT</div><ul><li>A staff needs full 360-degree clearance — check above, behind and both sides before any move, and never spin near people.</li><li>Grip at the centre ring and let the blade ends do the work; big shoulder swings are how staffs hit their own wielder.</li><li>Practise the slow menace walk before any spin trick — the Inquisitor's power is patience, not speed.</li><li>Spinning moves are display only: for actual sparring drills, plant the staff and use one end at a time.</li></ul></div><h3>Drill it</h3><p>In an empty space with full ceiling clearance, trace slow figure-eights with the staff at half speed while walking a straight line. Speed comes later; clearance discipline comes first.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">⚠ DUEL SAFELY</div><p>Duel-grade polycarbonate blades only, never thin display tubes. Agree intensity before you start, no strikes to head or hands, and staff or dual spins need a full 3m of clear space.</p></div>"},{"num":"09","title":"Game Day Lines","body":"<p class=\"lead\">The costume gets you noticed — the <span class=\"accent\">lines</span> make it unforgettable. Say them in character, time the pauses, and let the laughs land.</p><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">● ●  MORE GAME DAY LINES</div><ul><li>&ldquo;There are some things far more frightening than death.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; his famous last words in Rebels — slow, calm, no hurry</i></li><li>&ldquo;The key to hunting Jedi... is patience.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; from the Obi-Wan Kenobi series — pause hard on the dots</i></li><li>&ldquo;Jedi cannot help what they are. Their compassion leaves a trail.&rdquo; <i>&mdash; low and silky, like you already know where they went</i></li></ul></div><div class=\"reader-callout\"><div class=\"label\">😄 FOR LAUGHS — KID EDITION</div><ul><li>The key to hunting snacks... is patience. And knowing where Dad hides them.</li><li>Your compassion leaves a trail. So do your cookie crumbs.</li><li>I sense great fear in this classroom. Ah. Pop quiz day.</li></ul></div>"}],"files":[{"name":"Inquisitor saber STL","designer":"Thingiverse","url":"https://www.thingiverse.com/search?q=inquisitor+lightsaber"},{"name":"Inquisitor armour set","designer":"Cults3D","url":"https://cults3d.com/en/search?q=inquisitor%20armor"},{"name":"Grand Inquisitor reference","designer":"RPF forums","url":"https://www.therpf.com/forums/search/?q=grand+inquisitor"},{"name":"501st standards","designer":"501st.com","url":"https://www.501st.com/"}],"checklist":{"print":[{"name":"Circular spinning saber","detail":"Ring-hilt, double red blade."},{"name":"Chest + shoulder armour","detail":"Sleek glossy black."},{"name":"Hip + shin plates","detail":"Angular black."},{"name":"Vambraces (optional)","detail":"Dark forearms."}],"buy":[{"name":"Grey Pau'an makeup","detail":"Skin-safe; patch-test."},{"name":"Red contacts (optional)","detail":"Adult + eye-care professional only."},{"name":"Black flight suit","detail":"Base layer."},{"name":"Dark cape / skirted robe","detail":"Floor-length."},{"name":"Belt + saber mount","detail":"For the ring-hilt."},{"name":"Black gloves + tall boots","detail":"Matte black."}]}}};

